<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Notation for the appendix</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{P},d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{P},d)</annotation></semantics></math> be a metric space, <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{\prime}\subseteq\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{\prime}\subseteq\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\epsilon,\mathcal{P}^{\prime},d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\epsilon,\mathcal{P}^{\prime},d)</annotation></semantics></math> for the minimum number of closed <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-balls in <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> needed to cover <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m,n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m,n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the identity matrix; for a matrix <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the operator norm of <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|A\|_{\mathrm{op}}\coloneqq\sup_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{m}:\|x\|_{2}=1}\|Ax\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A\|_{\mathrm{op}}\coloneqq\sup_{x\in\mathbb{R}^{m}:\|x\|_{2}=1}\|Ax\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and define its entrywise <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm by <math id="A1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A\|_{\infty}\coloneqq\max_{i\in[n],j\in[m]}|A_{ij}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A\|_{\infty}\coloneqq\max_{i\in[n],j\in[m]}|A_{ij}|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> be probability measures on <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> be a measure on <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math> (such a measure always exists, e.g. <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=P+Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=P+Q</annotation></semantics></math>). Write <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=\frac{\mathrm{d}Q}{\mathrm{d}\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=\frac{\mathrm{d}Q}{\mathrm{d}\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the <em id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Hellinger distance</em> between <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{H}}(P,Q)\coloneqq\Bigl(\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\bigl(\sqrt{p(z)}-\sqrt{q(z)}\bigr)^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\nu(z)\Bigr)^{1/2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{H}}(P,Q)\coloneqq\Bigl(\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\bigl(\sqrt{p(z)}-\sqrt{q(z)}\bigr)^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\nu(z)\Bigr)^{1/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The definition is independent of the choice of the dominating measure <math id="A1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a metric on the space of distributions on <math id="A1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="A1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Kullback–Leibler divergence</em> from <math id="A1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(P,Q)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{P}\biggl(\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}(Z)\biggr)=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}(z)\,\mathrm{d}P(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(P,Q)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{P}\biggl(\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}(Z)\biggr)=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}(z)\,\mathrm{d}P(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">if <math id="A1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\ll Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\ll Q</annotation></semantics></math>, and infinity otherwise; this is the <math id="A1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>-expectation of the log-likelihood ratio between <math id="A1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>. We further define</p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{V}_{2}(P,Q)\coloneqq\mathrm{Var}_{P}\biggl(\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}(Z)\biggr)=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\biggl(\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}(z)-\mathrm{KL}(P,Q)\biggr)^{2}\,\mathrm{d}P(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{V}_{2}(P,Q)\coloneqq\mathrm{Var}_{P}\biggl(\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}(Z)\biggr)=\int_{\mathcal{Z}}\biggl(\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}Q}(z)-\mathrm{KL}(P,Q)\biggr)^{2}\,\mathrm{d}P(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">if <math id="A1.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\ll Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\ll Q</annotation></semantics></math>, and infinity otherwise; this is the <math id="A1.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>-variance of the log-likelihood ratio between <math id="A1.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[1,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[1,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, a Borel measurable function <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and a Borel measure <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|_{L^{p}(\mu)}\coloneqq\biggl(\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|f(x)|^{p}\,\mathrm{d}\mu(x)\biggr)^{1/p}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|_{L^{p}(\mu)}\coloneqq\biggl(\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}|f(x)|^{p}\,\mathrm{d}\mu(x)\biggr)^{1/p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and write <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{p}(\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{p}(\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> for the set of functions <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|_{L^{p}(\mu)}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|_{L^{p}(\mu)}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the domain of <math id="A1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is restricted to <math id="A1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is the Lebesgue measure restricted to a Borel set <math id="A1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we write <math id="A1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|_{L^{p}(\mathcal{X})}\equiv\|f\|_{L^{p}(\mu)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|_{L^{p}(\mathcal{X})}\equiv\|f\|_{L^{p}(\mu)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{p}(\mathcal{X})\equiv L^{p}(\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{p}(\mathcal{X})\equiv L^{p}(\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>; when <math id="A1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is clear from context, we further write <math id="A1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|_{L^{p}}\equiv\|f\|_{L^{p}(\mathcal{X})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></msub><mo>≡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|_{L^{p}}\equiv\|f\|_{L^{p}(\mathcal{X})}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For a zero-mean random variable <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sub-Gamma in the right tail</em> with variance parameter <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and scale parameter <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> if for all <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,1/c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,1/c)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}e^{\lambda X}\leq\exp\biggl(\frac{\sigma^{2}\lambda^{2}}{2(1-c\lambda)}\biggr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}e^{\lambda X}\leq\exp\biggl(\frac{\sigma^{2}\lambda^{2}}{2(1-c\lambda)}\biggr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Similarly, <math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sub-Gamma in the left tail</em> if <math id="A1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-X</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gamma in the right tail. And we say <math id="A1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A1.p4.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sub-Gamma in both tails</em> is it is both sub-Gamma in the right tail and sub-Gamma in the left tail.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we define three commonly used activation functions in Transformers. For <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{ReLU}(x)\coloneqq\max\{0,x\},\quad\mathsf{GELU}(x)\coloneqq x\Phi(x)\quad\text{and}\quad\mathsf{SiLU}(x)\coloneqq\frac{x}{1+e^{-x}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>𝖦𝖤𝖫𝖴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mi>𝖲𝗂𝖫𝖴</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{ReLU}(x)\coloneqq\max\{0,x\},\quad\mathsf{GELU}(x)\coloneqq x\Phi(x)\quad\text{and}\quad\mathsf{SiLU}(x)\coloneqq\frac{x}{1+e^{-x}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi(x)\coloneqq\int_{-\infty}^{x}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-t^{2}/2}\,\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x)\coloneqq\int_{-\infty}^{x}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-t^{2}/2}\,\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math> is the distribution function of standard Gaussian distribution.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 2 Problem set-up and ICL excess risk decomposition ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 2 Problem set-up and ICL excess risk decomposition ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We may assume without loss of generality that <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\ll\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\ll\pi</annotation></semantics></math> since otherwise, the right-hand side of (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In Proposition 1. ‣ 2 Problem set-up and ICL excess risk decomposition ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) is infinite. Note that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\mathcal{R}_{\pi}(\widetilde{f}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\mathcal{R}_{\pi}(\widetilde{f}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\mathcal{R}_{\pi}(g_{\pi})=\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{Y-\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}^{2}-\bigl\{Y-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\mathcal{R}_{\pi}(g_{\pi})=\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{Y-\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}^{2}-\bigl\{Y-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{-2Y\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})+\widetilde{f}_{T}^{2}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})+2Yg_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}^{2}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{-2Y\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})+\widetilde{f}_{T}^{2}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})+2Yg_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}^{2}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the outer expectation is taken over the randomness of <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{f}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{f}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{Y\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{Y\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\bigl\{Y\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\,|\,X,\mathcal{D}_{n}\bigr\}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\bigl\{Y\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\,|\,X,\mathcal{D}_{n}\bigr\}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\cdot\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\bigl(Y\,|\,X,\mathcal{D}_{n}\bigr)\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\cdot\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\bigl(Y\,|\,X,\mathcal{D}_{n}\bigr)\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">and similarly</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{Yg_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{Yg_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\bigl\{Yg_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\,|\,X,\mathcal{D}_{n}\bigr\}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\bigl\{Yg_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\,|\,X,\mathcal{D}_{n}\bigr\}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{g_{\pi}^{2}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{g_{\pi}^{2}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\mathcal{R}_{\pi}(\widetilde{f}_{T})-\mathcal{R}_{\pi}(g_{\pi})=\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{-2g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})+\widetilde{f}_{T}^{2}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})+g_{\pi}^{2}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\mathcal{R}_{\pi}(\widetilde{f}_{T})-\mathcal{R}_{\pi}(g_{\pi})=\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{-2g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})+\widetilde{f}_{T}^{2}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})+g_{\pi}^{2}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}^{2}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2 Problem set-up and ICL excess risk decomposition ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), we have <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})|\leq R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})|\leq R</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely.
Now, for every fixed <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{P}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{P}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math>, so that by Fubini’s theorem and the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}_{\mu}(Z_{P})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\biggl(Z_{P}\cdot\frac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}\pi}(P)\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}_{\mu}(Z_{P})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\biggl(Z_{P}\cdot\frac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}\pi}(P)\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\pi}(Z_{P}^{2})\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\biggl\{\biggl(\frac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}\pi}(P)\biggr)^{2}\biggr\}}\leq\sqrt{4R^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\pi}(Z_{P})\bigl\{\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi)+1\bigr\}}=2R\sqrt{\bigl\{\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi)+1\bigr\}\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\pi}(Z_{P}^{2})\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\biggl\{\biggl(\frac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}\pi}(P)\biggr)^{2}\biggr\}}\leq\sqrt{4R^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\pi}(Z_{P})\bigl\{\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi)+1\bigr\}}=2R\sqrt{\bigl\{\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi)+1\bigr\}\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\mathcal{R}_{\mu}(\widetilde{f}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\mathcal{R}_{\mu}(\widetilde{f}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{Y-\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{Y-\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{-2Y\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})+\widetilde{f}_{T}^{2}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})+2Y\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)-\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{-2Y\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})+\widetilde{f}_{T}^{2}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})+2Y\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)-\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{=}\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{=}\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]+2\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\mathbb{E}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]+2\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\leq}4R\sqrt{\bigl\{\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi)+1\bigr\}\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})}+2\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\leq}4R\sqrt{\bigl\{\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi)+1\bigr\}\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})}+2\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">Here, <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ii)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from (<a href="#A2.E15" title="In Proof of Proposition . ‣ Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>), and <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> follows since</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{Y\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{Y\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{Y\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\,|\,X,\mathcal{D}_{n}\bigr\}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{Y\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\,|\,X,\mathcal{D}_{n}\bigr\}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\cdot\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\cdot\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\cdot\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{\widetilde{f}_{T}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\cdot\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">and similarly,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{Y\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr\}=\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{Y\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\,|\,X\bigr\}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{Y\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr\}=\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{Y\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\,|\,X\bigr\}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl\{\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text">This proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs for Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Universal approximation and learnability ‣ 3 Transformers, universal approximation and learnability ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 Universal approximation and learnability ‣ 3 Transformers, universal approximation and learnability ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We work under the assumptions of Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Universal approximation and learnability ‣ 3 Transformers, universal approximation and learnability ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> and we assume that <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is not a polynomial. For <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y_{g})\sim P_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y_{g})\sim P_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\mapsto f_{\xi}(y,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\mapsto f_{\xi}(y,z)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the conditional density of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Y_{g}\,|\,\{g(X)=z\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{g}\,|\,\{g(X)=z\}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the dominating measure <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>. Further let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}_{\xi}\coloneqq f_{\xi}/R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}_{\xi}\coloneqq f_{\xi}/R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Bayes’ theorem and (<a href="#A5.E41" title="In E.2 Bayesian nonparametric regression ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), the posterior regression function <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</p>
<table id="A3.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{\pi}(x,D_{n})=\frac{\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(x)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i}-g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)}{\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i}-g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{\pi}(x,D_{n})=\frac{\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(x)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i}-g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)}{\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i}-g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Throughout this section, we assume that <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl((X_{1},Y_{1}),\ldots,(X_{N},Y_{N}),(X,Y)\bigr)\,|\,P\sim P^{\otimes(N+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl((X_{1},Y_{1}),\ldots,(X_{N},Y_{N}),(X,Y)\bigr)\,|\,P\sim P^{\otimes(N+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\sim\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\sim\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{model}}\geq d+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{model}}\geq d+2</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A3.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,d_{\mathrm{model}})}\coloneqq\begin{pmatrix}X_{1}^{\top}&amp;Y_{1}&amp;\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2}^{\top}&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
X_{n}^{\top}&amp;Y_{n}&amp;\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2}^{\top}&amp;0\\
X^{\top}&amp;0&amp;\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2}^{\top}&amp;1\end{pmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,d_{\mathrm{model}})}\coloneqq\begin{pmatrix}X_{1}^{\top}&amp;Y_{1}&amp;\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2}^{\top}&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
X_{n}^{\top}&amp;Y_{n}&amp;\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2}^{\top}&amp;0\\
X^{\top}&amp;0&amp;\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2}^{\top}&amp;1\end{pmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first write down the rows of attention layers and FFN layers before we start.
Consider the notation in Definition <a href="#Thmdefn1" title="Definition 1 (Attention layer). ‣ 3.1 Transformers ‣ 3 Transformers, universal approximation and learnability ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, if <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math> has rows <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}^{\top},\ldots,Z_{n+1}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}^{\top},\ldots,Z_{n+1}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th row <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\attn_{\theta_{\mathrm{attn}}}(Z)]_{i,:}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗍𝗍𝗇</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>attn</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\attn_{\theta_{\mathrm{attn}}}(Z)]_{i,:}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\attn_{\theta_{\mathrm{attn}}}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝗍𝗍𝗇</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>attn</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\attn_{\theta_{\mathrm{attn}}}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</p>
<table id="A3.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle[\attn_{\theta_{\mathrm{attn}}}(Z)]_{i,:}=Z_{i}^{\top}+\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{j=1}^{n+1}Z_{j}^{\top}V_{h}\cdot\frac{\exp(Z_{i}^{\top}Q_{h}K_{h}^{\top}Z_{j}/\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{model}}})}{\sum_{\ell=1}^{n+1}\exp(Z_{i}^{\top}Q_{h}K_{h}^{\top}Z_{\ell}/\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{model}}})}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗍𝗍𝗇</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>attn</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[\attn_{\theta_{\mathrm{attn}}}(Z)]_{i,:}=Z_{i}^{\top}+\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{j=1}^{n+1}Z_{j}^{\top}V_{h}\cdot\frac{\exp(Z_{i}^{\top}Q_{h}K_{h}^{\top}Z_{j}/\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{model}}})}{\sum_{\ell=1}^{n+1}\exp(Z_{i}^{\top}Q_{h}K_{h}^{\top}Z_{\ell}/\sqrt{d_{\mathrm{model}}})}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Next, consider the notation in Definition <a href="#Thmdefn2" title="Definition 2 (FFN layer). ‣ 3.1 Transformers ‣ 3 Transformers, universal approximation and learnability ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, if <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math> has rows <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}^{\top},\ldots,Z_{n+1}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}^{\top},\ldots,Z_{n+1}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th row <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}(Z)]_{i,:}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}(Z)]_{i,:}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</p>
<table id="A3.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}(Z)]_{i,:}=\bigl(Z_{i}+W_{2}^{\top}\rho(W_{1}^{\top}Z_{i}+v)\bigr)^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}(Z)]_{i,:}=\bigl(Z_{i}+W_{2}^{\top}\rho(W_{1}^{\top}Z_{i}+v)\bigr)^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Thus the FFN layer applies a single-hidden layer neural network to each row of <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 9</span></span><span id="Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmthm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon,\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon,\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist <math id="Thmthm9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1},\ldots,g_{M}\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1},\ldots,g_{M}\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> such that with probability at least <math id="Thmthm9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{n\in[N]}\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}g_{m}(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{n\in[N]}\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}g_{m}(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{n\in[N]}\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|\leq\epsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{n\in[N]}\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|\leq\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\coloneqq 2\epsilon^{-2}(R^{2}\vee 1)\log(2N/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∨</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\coloneqq 2\epsilon^{-2}(R^{2}\vee 1)\log(2N/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}_{1},\ldots,\widetilde{g}_{M}\overset{\mathrm{iid}}{\sim}\widetilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">iid</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}_{1},\ldots,\widetilde{g}_{M}\overset{\mathrm{iid}}{\sim}\widetilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent of <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{i},Y_{i})_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{i},Y_{i})_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, define events</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle A_{n}\coloneqq\Biggl\{\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\widetilde{g}_{m}(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},\widetilde{g}_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|\leq\epsilon\Biggr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{n}\coloneqq\Biggl\{\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\widetilde{g}_{m}(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},\widetilde{g}_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|\leq\epsilon\Biggr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle B_{n}\coloneqq\Biggl\{\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},\widetilde{g}_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|\leq\epsilon\Biggr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{n}\coloneqq\Biggl\{\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},\widetilde{g}_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|\leq\epsilon\Biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">We have by Hoeffding’s inequality that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(A_{n}^{\mathrm{c}}\,|\,X_{1},Y_{1},\ldots,X_{n},Y_{n},X)\leq\frac{\delta}{2N}\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbb{P}(B_{n}^{\mathrm{c}}\,|\,X_{1},Y_{1},\ldots,X_{n},Y_{n},X)\leq\frac{\delta}{2N}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(A_{n}^{\mathrm{c}}\,|\,X_{1},Y_{1},\ldots,X_{n},Y_{n},X)\leq\frac{\delta}{2N}\quad\text{and}\quad\mathbb{P}(B_{n}^{\mathrm{c}}\,|\,X_{1},Y_{1},\ldots,X_{n},Y_{n},X)\leq\frac{\delta}{2N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then by a union bound,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl\{\mathbb{P}\biggl(\bigcup_{n=1}^{N}(A_{n}^{\mathrm{c}}\cup B_{n}^{\mathrm{c}})\,\bigg|\,\widetilde{g}_{1},\ldots,\widetilde{g}_{M}\biggr)\biggr\}=\mathbb{P}\biggl(\bigcup_{n=1}^{N}(A_{n}^{\mathrm{c}}\cup B_{n}^{\mathrm{c}})\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\biggl\{\mathbb{P}\biggl(\bigcup_{n=1}^{N}(A_{n}^{\mathrm{c}}\cup B_{n}^{\mathrm{c}})\,\bigg|\,\widetilde{g}_{1},\ldots,\widetilde{g}_{M}\biggr)\biggr\}=\mathbb{P}\biggl(\bigcup_{n=1}^{N}(A_{n}^{\mathrm{c}}\cup B_{n}^{\mathrm{c}})\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 113.81102pt=\mathbb{E}\biggl\{\mathbb{P}\biggl(\bigcup_{n=1}^{N}(A_{n}^{\mathrm{c}}\cup B_{n}^{\mathrm{c}})\,\bigg|\,X_{1},Y_{1},\ldots,X_{N},Y_{N},X,Y\biggr)\biggr\}\leq\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="11.658em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 113.81102pt=\mathbb{E}\biggl\{\mathbb{P}\biggl(\bigcup_{n=1}^{N}(A_{n}^{\mathrm{c}}\cup B_{n}^{\mathrm{c}})\,\bigg|\,X_{1},Y_{1},\ldots,X_{N},Y_{N},X,Y\biggr)\biggr\}\leq\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\mathbb{P}\biggl(\bigcup_{n=1}^{N}(A_{n}^{\mathrm{c}}\cup B_{n}^{\mathrm{c}})\,\biggm|\,\widetilde{g}_{1},\ldots,\widetilde{g}_{M}\biggr)\leq\delta\biggr\}&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\mathbb{P}\biggl(\bigcup_{n=1}^{N}(A_{n}^{\mathrm{c}}\cup B_{n}^{\mathrm{c}})\,\biggm|\,\widetilde{g}_{1},\ldots,\widetilde{g}_{M}\biggr)\leq\delta\biggr\}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">This proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 10</span></span><span id="Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">almost surely.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The density (with respect to <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>) of <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> conditional on <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{1},\ldots,X_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{1},\ldots,X_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(y_{1},\ldots,y_{n})\mapsto\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}f_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(X_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(y_{1},\ldots,y_{n})\mapsto\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}f_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(X_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, by definition,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\biggl(\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)=0\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\biggl(\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)=0\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 113.81102pt=\mathbb{E}\biggl\{\mathbb{P}\biggl(\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}f_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(X_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)=0\,\biggm|\,X_{1},\ldots,X_{n}\biggr)\biggr\}=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="11.658em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 113.81102pt=\mathbb{E}\biggl\{\mathbb{P}\biggl(\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}f_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(X_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)=0\,\biggm|\,X_{1},\ldots,X_{n}\biggr)\biggr\}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">This holds for all <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, which proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 11</span></span><span id="Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1},d_{2}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1},d_{2}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmthm11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> be Borel measurable and let <math id="Thmthm11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> be a Borel probability measure on <math id="Thmthm11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for every <math id="Thmthm11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist <math id="Thmthm11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmthm11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}\times d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}\times d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmthm11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}\times d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}\times d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu\Bigl(\bigl\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}:\bigl\|f(x)-W_{2}^{\top}\rho(W_{1}^{\top}x+v)\bigr\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon\bigr\}\Bigr)\geq 1-\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu\Bigl(\bigl\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}:\bigl\|f(x)-W_{2}^{\top}\rho(W_{1}^{\top}x+v)\bigr\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon\bigr\}\Bigr)\geq 1-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first prove the claim for <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a compact set such that <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(K_{0})\geq 1-\delta/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(K_{0})\geq 1-\delta/3</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lusin’s theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Folland, 1999</a>, Theorems 7.8 and 7.10)</cite>, there exists a (compactly supported) continuous function <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\bigl(\{x\in K_{0}:f(x)\neq h(x)\}\bigr)\leq\delta/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\bigl(\{x\in K_{0}:f(x)\neq h(x)\}\bigr)\leq\delta/3</annotation></semantics></math>. Since one-hidden layer neural networks with non-polynomial activation are dense in the set of continuous functions on compact domains equipped with the uniform norm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Leshno et al., 1993</a>, Theorem 1)</cite>, there exist <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}\times d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}\times d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}\times d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}\times d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in K_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in K_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl|h(x)-W_{2}^{\top}\rho(W_{1}^{\top}x+v)\bigr|\leq\frac{\delta\epsilon}{3}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl|h(x)-W_{2}^{\top}\rho(W_{1}^{\top}x+v)\bigr|\leq\frac{\delta\epsilon}{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">It follows by Markov’s inequality that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mu\Bigl(\bigl\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}:\bigl|f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu\Bigl(\bigl\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}:\bigl|f(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-W_{2}^{\top}\rho(W_{1}^{\top}x+v)\bigr|\geq\epsilon\bigr\}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-W_{2}^{\top}\rho(W_{1}^{\top}x+v)\bigr|\geq\epsilon\bigr\}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mu\Bigl(\bigl\{x\in K_{0}:\bigl|f(x)-W_{2}^{\top}\rho(W_{1}^{\top}x+v)\bigr|\geq\epsilon\bigr\}\Bigr)+\frac{\delta}{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mu\Bigl(\bigl\{x\in K_{0}:\bigl|f(x)-W_{2}^{\top}\rho(W_{1}^{\top}x+v)\bigr|\geq\epsilon\bigr\}\Bigr)+\frac{\delta}{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mu\Bigl(\bigl\{x\in K_{0}:\bigl|h(x)-W_{2}^{\top}\rho(W_{1}^{\top}x+v)\bigr|\geq\epsilon\bigr\}\Bigr)+\frac{\delta}{3}+\frac{\delta}{3}\leq\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mu\Bigl(\bigl\{x\in K_{0}:\bigl|h(x)-W_{2}^{\top}\rho(W_{1}^{\top}x+v)\bigr|\geq\epsilon\bigr\}\Bigr)+\frac{\delta}{3}+\frac{\delta}{3}\leq\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">This proves the claim when <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{2}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{2}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we may approximate the component functions in parallel and apply a union bound to deduce the final result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 12</span></span><span id="Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{model}}\geq d+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{model}}\geq d+2</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmthm12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{2}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{2}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be Borel measurable. For <math id="Thmthm12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmthm12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,d_{\mathrm{model}})}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,d_{\mathrm{model}})}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in (<a href="#A3.E17" title="In C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) and let</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U^{(n)}\coloneqq\begin{pmatrix}f_{1}^{\top}(X_{1},Y_{1})\\
\vdots\\
f_{1}^{\top}(X_{n},Y_{n})\\
f_{2}^{\top}(X)\end{pmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U^{(n)}\coloneqq\begin{pmatrix}f_{1}^{\top}(X_{1},Y_{1})\\
\vdots\\
f_{1}^{\top}(X_{n},Y_{n})\\
f_{2}^{\top}(X)\end{pmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm12.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm12.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for <math id="Thmthm12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm12.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an FFN layer <math id="Thmthm12.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that with probability at least <math id="Thmthm12.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{n\in[N]}\bigl\|\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,d_{\mathrm{model}})})-U^{(n)}\bigr\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{n\in[N]}\bigl\|\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,d_{\mathrm{model}})})-U^{(n)}\bigr\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define a Borel measurable function <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y,\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2},0)\coloneqq f_{1}(x,y)-(x,y,\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y,\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2},0)\coloneqq f_{1}(x,y)-(x,y,\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2},0)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,0,\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2},1)\coloneqq f_{2}(x)-(x,0,\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,0,\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2},1)\coloneqq f_{2}(x)-(x,0,\bm{0}_{d_{\mathrm{model}}-d-2},1)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> to be zero otherwise.
Let <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distribution of <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the marginal distribution of <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. Define a distribution <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mu\biggl(\prod_{j=1}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}A_{j}\biggr)\coloneqq\frac{\mu_{1}(\prod_{j=1}^{d+1}A_{j})\mathbbm{1}_{\{0\in A_{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\}}+\mu_{2}(\prod_{j=1}^{d}A_{j})\mathbbm{1}_{\{1\in A_{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\}}}{2}\cdot\prod_{j=d+2}^{{d_{\mathrm{model}}}-1}\mathbbm{1}_{\{0\in A_{j}\}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∏</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∏</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu\biggl(\prod_{j=1}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}A_{j}\biggr)\coloneqq\frac{\mu_{1}(\prod_{j=1}^{d+1}A_{j})\mathbbm{1}_{\{0\in A_{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\}}+\mu_{2}(\prod_{j=1}^{d}A_{j})\mathbbm{1}_{\{1\in A_{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\}}}{2}\cdot\prod_{j=d+2}^{{d_{\mathrm{model}}}-1}\mathbbm{1}_{\{0\in A_{j}\}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">for all measurable sets <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},\ldots,A_{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\subseteq\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},\ldots,A_{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\subseteq\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#Thmthm11" title="Lemma 11. ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and the definition of <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> above, there exists an FFN layer <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\Bigl(\bigl\|\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\Bigl(\bigl\|\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle(X,Y,\bm{0}_{{d_{\mathrm{model}}}-d-2},0)-f_{1}(X,Y)\bigr\|_{\infty}&gt;\epsilon\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(X,Y,\bm{0}_{{d_{\mathrm{model}}}-d-2},0)-f_{1}(X,Y)\bigr\|_{\infty}&gt;\epsilon\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathbb{P}\Bigl(\bigl\|\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}(X,0,\bm{0}_{{d_{\mathrm{model}}}-d-2},1)-f_{2}(X)\bigr\|_{\infty}&gt;\epsilon\Bigr)\leq\frac{\delta}{N+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathbb{P}\Bigl(\bigl\|\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}}(X,0,\bm{0}_{{d_{\mathrm{model}}}-d-2},1)-f_{2}(X)\bigr\|_{\infty}&gt;\epsilon\Bigr)\leq\frac{\delta}{N+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">We conclude the claim by a union bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 Universal approximation and learnability ‣ 3 Transformers, universal approximation and learnability ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\coloneqq\frac{7\epsilon}{80R^{2}}\wedge 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\coloneqq\frac{7\epsilon}{80R^{2}}\wedge 1</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#Thmthm10" title="Lemma 10. ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and a union bound, there exists <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> such that the event</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{0}\coloneqq\Bigl\{\min_{n\in[N]}\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\geq b\Bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{0}\coloneqq\Bigl\{\min_{n\in[N]}\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\geq b\Bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">has probability at least <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{1}\coloneqq\frac{b}{8}\wedge\frac{b\sqrt{\epsilon}}{64(R\vee 1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>∧</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∨</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{1}\coloneqq\frac{b}{8}\wedge\frac{b\sqrt{\epsilon}}{64(R\vee 1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#Thmthm9" title="Lemma 9. ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, there exist <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1},\ldots,g_{M}\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1},\ldots,g_{M}\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the event</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{1}\coloneqq\biggl\{\max_{n\in[N]}\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}g_{m}(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g(X_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|\leq\epsilon_{1}\biggr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{1}\coloneqq\biggl\{\max_{n\in[N]}\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}g_{m}(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g(X_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|\leq\epsilon_{1}\biggr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bigcap\biggl\{\max_{n\in[N]}\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g(X_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|\leq\epsilon_{1}\biggr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigcap\biggl\{\max_{n\in[N]}\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g(X_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|\leq\epsilon_{1}\biggr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">has probability at least <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now let <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\coloneqq 4M+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\coloneqq 4M+1</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}=(f_{1,1},\ldots,f_{1,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}):\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}=(f_{1,1},\ldots,f_{1,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}):\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f_{1,j}(x,y)\coloneqq\begin{cases}\log\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y,g_{j}(x)\bigr)\quad&amp;\text{if }j\in[M]\\
\log\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y,g_{j-M}(x)\bigr)\quad&amp;\text{if }j\in[M+1:2M]\\
0&amp;\text{if }j\in[2M+1:4M+1].\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{1,j}(x,y)\coloneqq\begin{cases}\log\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y,g_{j}(x)\bigr)\quad&amp;\text{if }j\in[M]\\
\log\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y,g_{j-M}(x)\bigr)\quad&amp;\text{if }j\in[M+1:2M]\\
0&amp;\text{if }j\in[2M+1:4M+1].\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Also define <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{2}=(f_{2,1},\ldots,f_{2,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}):\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{2}=(f_{2,1},\ldots,f_{2,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}):\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f_{2,j}(x)\coloneqq\begin{cases}\log g_{j}(x)\quad&amp;\text{if }j\in[M]\\
0&amp;\text{if }j\in[M+1:4M]\\
1&amp;\text{if }j=4M+1.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{2,j}(x)\coloneqq\begin{cases}\log g_{j}(x)\quad&amp;\text{if }j\in[M]\\
0&amp;\text{if }j\in[M+1:4M]\\
1&amp;\text{if }j=4M+1.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, for <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(n)}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(n)}\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U^{(n)}\coloneqq\begin{pmatrix}f_{1}(X_{1},Y_{1})\\
\vdots\\
f_{1}(X_{n},Y_{n})\\
f_{2}(X)\end{pmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U^{(n)}\coloneqq\begin{pmatrix}f_{1}(X_{1},Y_{1})\\
\vdots\\
f_{1}(X_{n},Y_{n})\\
f_{2}(X)\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmthm12" title="Lemma 12. ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, there exists an FFN layer <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}=(W_{1},W_{2},v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}=(W_{1},W_{2},v)</annotation></semantics></math>, such that writing <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{2}\coloneqq\frac{b}{32(N+1)}\wedge\frac{b\sqrt{\epsilon}}{256R(N+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>∧</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{2}\coloneqq\frac{b}{32(N+1)}\wedge\frac{b\sqrt{\epsilon}}{256R(N+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the event</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{2}\coloneqq\Bigl\{\max_{n\in[N]}\bigl\|\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})})-U^{(n)}\bigr\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon_{2}\Bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{2}\coloneqq\Bigl\{\max_{n\in[N]}\bigl\|\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})})-U^{(n)}\bigr\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon_{2}\Bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">has probability at least <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the final column of <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> only affects the final column of <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can choose the final column of <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to be zero, so that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})})\bigr]_{i,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}=\bigl[Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})}\bigr]_{i,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}=\mathbbm{1}_{\{i=n+1\}}=\bigl[U^{(n)}\bigr]_{i,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}\quad\text{for }i\in[n+1]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mtext>for </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})})\bigr]_{i,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}=\bigl[Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})}\bigr]_{i,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}=\mathbbm{1}_{\{i=n+1\}}=\bigl[U^{(n)}\bigr]_{i,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}\quad\text{for }i\in[n+1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.8.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we define <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{(2)}=K^{(2)}\coloneqq\bm{0}_{{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{(2)}=K^{(2)}\coloneqq\bm{0}_{{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{(2)}_{j,2M+j}\coloneqq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{(2)}_{j,2M+j}\coloneqq 1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[2M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[2M]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{(2)}_{4M+1,4M+1}\coloneqq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{(2)}_{4M+1,4M+1}\coloneqq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and zero otherwise. Let <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{(2)}_{\mathrm{attn}}\coloneqq(Q^{(2)},K^{(2)},V^{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>attn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{(2)}_{\mathrm{attn}}\coloneqq(Q^{(2)},K^{(2)},V^{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}\coloneqq\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})})\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}\coloneqq\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})})\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{Z}^{(n)}\coloneqq\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(2)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}(\widetilde{Z}^{(n)})\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝗍𝗍𝗇</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>attn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{Z}^{(n)}\coloneqq\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(2)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}(\widetilde{Z}^{(n)})\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by construction and (<a href="#A3.E18" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), the <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n+1)</annotation></semantics></math>th row of <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{Z}^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{Z}^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,j}=\begin{cases}\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,j}\quad&amp;\text{if }j\in[2M]\\
\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,j}+\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{i,j-2M}\quad&amp;\text{if }j\in[2M+1:4M]\\
1+\frac{1}{n+1}\quad&amp;\text{if }j=4M+1.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,j}=\begin{cases}\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,j}\quad&amp;\text{if }j\in[2M]\\
\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,j}+\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{i,j-2M}\quad&amp;\text{if }j\in[2M+1:4M]\\
1+\frac{1}{n+1}\quad&amp;\text{if }j=4M+1.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.9.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that on <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\biggl|\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}-\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\biggl|\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}-\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex72.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\frac{1}{n+1}\log g_{m}(X)\biggr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)-\frac{1}{n+1}\log g_{m}(X)\biggr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\biggl|\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}+\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{i,m}-\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}U^{(n)}_{i,m}\biggr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\biggl|\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}+\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{i,m}-\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}U^{(n)}_{i,m}\biggr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\bigl|\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}-0\bigr|+\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}\bigl|\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{i,m}-U^{(n)}_{i,m}\bigr|\leq 2\epsilon_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\bigl|\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}-0\bigr|+\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}\bigl|\widetilde{Z}^{(n)}_{i,m}-U^{(n)}_{i,m}\bigr|\leq 2\epsilon_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.10.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, for <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that on <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\biggl|\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,3M+m}-\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)\biggr|\leq 2\epsilon_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\biggl|\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,3M+m}-\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)\biggr|\leq 2\epsilon_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.11.1" class="ltx_text">Now define a continuous function <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{3}:\mathbb{R}^{4M+1}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{3}:\mathbb{R}^{4M+1}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{3}(z_{1},\ldots,z_{4M+1})\coloneqq\frac{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\{z_{2M+m}/(z_{4M+1}-1)\}}{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\{z_{3M+m}/(z_{4M+1}-1)\}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{3}(z_{1},\ldots,z_{4M+1})\coloneqq\frac{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\{z_{2M+m}/(z_{4M+1}-1)\}}{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\{z_{3M+m}/(z_{4M+1}-1)\}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.12.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{P}^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{P}^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> be the distribution of the last row of <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{Z}^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{Z}^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By applying Lemma <a href="#Thmthm11" title="Lemma 11. ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> with <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\bar{P}^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\bar{P}^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> therein, there exists an FFN layer <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(2)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(2)}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the event</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{3}\coloneqq\Bigl\{\max_{n\in[N]}\Bigl|\bigl[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(2)}}(\bar{Z}^{(n)})\bigr]_{n+1,d+1}-f_{3}\bigl(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,1},\ldots,\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}\bigr)\Bigr|\leq\sqrt{\epsilon}/4\Bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{3}\coloneqq\Bigl\{\max_{n\in[N]}\Bigl|\bigl[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(2)}}(\bar{Z}^{(n)})\bigr]_{n+1,d+1}-f_{3}\bigl(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,1},\ldots,\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}\bigr)\Bigr|\leq\sqrt{\epsilon}/4\Bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.13.1" class="ltx_text">has probability at least <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{m}\|_{\infty}\leq R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{m}\|_{\infty}\leq R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{f}_{\xi}\|_{\infty}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{f}_{\xi}\|_{\infty}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have by (<a href="#A3.E19" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E20" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) that on <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\bigl\{\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}/(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,4M+1}-1)\bigr\}-\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\bigl\{\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}/(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,4M+1}-1)\bigr\}-\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\bigl\{\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}/(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,4M+1}-1)\bigr\}-\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}g_{m}(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)\biggr|+\epsilon_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\bigl\{\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}/(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,4M+1}-1)\bigr\}-\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}g_{m}(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)\biggr|+\epsilon_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m\in[M]}\biggl|\exp\bigl\{(n+1)\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}\bigr\}-g_{m}(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)\biggr|+\epsilon_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m\in[M]}\biggl|\exp\bigl\{(n+1)\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}\bigr\}-g_{m}(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)\biggr|+\epsilon_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq R(e^{2(N+1)\epsilon_{2}}-1)+\epsilon_{1}\leq\frac{b\sqrt{\epsilon}}{32}\eqqcolon\epsilon_{3}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>32</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≕</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq R(e^{2(N+1)\epsilon_{2}}-1)+\epsilon_{1}\leq\frac{b\sqrt{\epsilon}}{32}\eqqcolon\epsilon_{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.14.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, on <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> we have by (<a href="#A3.E19" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E21" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) that for all <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\bigl\{\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,3M+m}/(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,4M+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\biggl|\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\bigl\{\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,3M+m}/(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,4M+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex79.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-1)\bigr\}-\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-1)\bigr\}-\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)\biggr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(e^{2(N+1)\epsilon_{2}}-1)+\epsilon_{1}\leq\frac{b\sqrt{\epsilon}}{32R}\wedge\frac{b}{4}\eqqcolon\epsilon_{4}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>∧</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≕</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(e^{2(N+1)\epsilon_{2}}-1)+\epsilon_{1}\leq\frac{b\sqrt{\epsilon}}{32R}\wedge\frac{b}{4}\eqqcolon\epsilon_{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.15.1" class="ltx_text">Now, on the event <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}\cap\mathcal{E}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}\cap\mathcal{E}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{1}\leq b/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{1}\leq b/2</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{n\in[N]}\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)\geq\frac{b}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{n\in[N]}\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(Y_{i},g_{m}(X_{i})\bigr)\geq\frac{b}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.16.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, on <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}\cap\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}\cap\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have by (<a href="#A3.E22" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.E23" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.E24" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E16" title="In C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) that for all <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl|f_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl|f_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex80.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,1},\ldots,\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,1},\ldots,\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,{d_{\mathrm{model}}}})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Biggl|\frac{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\{\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}/(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,4M+1}-1)\}}{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\{\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,3M+m}/(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,4M+1}-1)\}}-\frac{\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)}{\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)}\Biggr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Biggl|\frac{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\{\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,2M+m}/(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,4M+1}-1)\}}{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\{\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,3M+m}/(\bar{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,4M+1}-1)\}}-\frac{\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)}{\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)}\Biggr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\biggl(\frac{1}{1-2\epsilon_{4}/b}-1\biggr)\Biggl|\frac{\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)}{\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)}\Biggr|+\frac{\epsilon_{3}}{b/2-\epsilon_{4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\biggl(\frac{1}{1-2\epsilon_{4}/b}-1\biggr)\Biggl|\frac{\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(X)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)}{\int_{\mathcal{G}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bar{f}_{\xi}\bigl(y_{i},g(x_{i})\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g)}\Biggr|+\frac{\epsilon_{3}}{b/2-\epsilon_{4}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\biggl(\frac{1}{1-2\epsilon_{4}/b}-1\biggr)R+\frac{2\epsilon_{3}}{b-2\epsilon_{4}}\leq\frac{4R\epsilon_{4}}{b}+\frac{4\epsilon_{3}}{b}\leq\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{4}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\biggl(\frac{1}{1-2\epsilon_{4}/b}-1\biggr)R+\frac{2\epsilon_{3}}{b-2\epsilon_{4}}\leq\frac{4R\epsilon_{4}}{b}+\frac{4\epsilon_{3}}{b}\leq\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.17.1" class="ltx_text">where in the penultimate inequality, we used the fact that <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1-x}-1\leq 2x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1-x}-1\leq 2x</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in[0,1/2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in[0,1/2]</annotation></semantics></math> and that <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{4}\leq b/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{4}\leq b/4</annotation></semantics></math>, and the final inequality uses the definitions of <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m57" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. If we set the first attention layer <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m58" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(1)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠𝗍𝗍𝗇</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>attn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(1)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the identity map (i.e. set the parameters of the attention layer to zero), and let <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{Z}^{(n)}\coloneqq\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(2)}}\circ\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(2)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}\circ\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}\circ\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(1)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗍𝗍𝗇</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>attn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝗍𝗍𝗇</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>attn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{Z}^{(n)}\coloneqq\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(2)}}\circ\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(2)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}\circ\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}\circ\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(1)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})})</annotation></semantics></math>, then by (<a href="#A3.E25" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) and the triangle inequality, we have on <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{0}\cap\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2}\cap\mathcal{E}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{0}\cap\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2}\cap\mathcal{E}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> that for all <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Bigl|\check{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,d+1}-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\Bigr|=\Bigl|\bigl[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(2)}}(\bar{Z}^{(n)})\bigr]_{n+1,d+1}-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\Bigr|\leq\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Bigl|\check{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,d+1}-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\Bigr|=\Bigl|\bigl[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(2)}}(\bar{Z}^{(n)})\bigr]_{n+1,d+1}-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\Bigr|\leq\frac{\sqrt{\epsilon}}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.18.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m62" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m63" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{P}^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{P}^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> be the distribution of the last row of <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m64" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{Z}^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{Z}^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math>. By applying Lemma <a href="#Thmthm11" title="Lemma 11. ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> with <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m65" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\check{P}^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\check{P}^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> therein, there exists an FFN layer <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m66" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(3)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(3)}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the event</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{4}\coloneqq\Bigl\{\max_{n\in[N]}\Bigl|\bigl[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(3)}}(\check{Z}^{(n)})\bigr]_{n+1,d+1}-\mathsf{clip}_{R}(\check{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,d+1})\Bigr|\leq\sqrt{\epsilon}/4\Bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗂𝗉</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{4}\coloneqq\Bigl\{\max_{n\in[N]}\Bigl|\bigl[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(3)}}(\check{Z}^{(n)})\bigr]_{n+1,d+1}-\mathsf{clip}_{R}(\check{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,d+1})\Bigr|\leq\sqrt{\epsilon}/4\Bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.19.1" class="ltx_text">has probability at least <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m67" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, let <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m68" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(3)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠𝗍𝗍𝗇</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>attn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(3)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the identity map and let</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TF}\coloneqq\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(3)}}\circ\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(3)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}\circ\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(2)}}\circ\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(2)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}\circ\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}\circ\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(1)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖥</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗍𝗍𝗇</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>attn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗍𝗍𝗇</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>attn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗍𝗍𝗇</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>attn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TF}\coloneqq\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(3)}}\circ\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(3)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}\circ\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(2)}}\circ\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(2)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}\circ\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(1)}}\circ\mathsf{Attn}_{\theta^{(1)}_{\mathrm{attn}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.20.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m69" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{\pi}\|_{\infty}\leq R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{\pi}\|_{\infty}\leq R</annotation></semantics></math>, we have by (<a href="#A3.E26" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ C.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) that on <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m70" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}\coloneqq\mathcal{E}_{0}\cap\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2}\cap\mathcal{E}_{3}\cap\mathcal{E}_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}\coloneqq\mathcal{E}_{0}\cap\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2}\cap\mathcal{E}_{3}\cap\mathcal{E}_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m71" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl|\mathsf{Read}\circ\mathsf{TF}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖺𝖽</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>in</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl|\mathsf{Read}\circ\mathsf{TF}(Z_{\mathrm{in}}^{(n,{d_{\mathrm{model}}})})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Bigl|\bigl[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(3)}}(\check{Z}^{(n)})\bigr]_{n+1,d+1}-\mathsf{clip}_{R}(\check{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,d+1})\Bigr|+\Bigl|\mathsf{clip}_{R}(\check{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,d+1})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\Bigr|\leq\frac{3\sqrt{\epsilon}}{4}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖥𝖥𝖭</mi><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗂𝗉</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗂𝗉</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ϵ</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Bigl|\bigl[\mathsf{FFN}_{\theta_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{(3)}}(\check{Z}^{(n)})\bigr]_{n+1,d+1}-\mathsf{clip}_{R}(\check{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,d+1})\Bigr|+\Bigl|\mathsf{clip}_{R}(\check{Z}^{(n)}_{n+1,d+1})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\Bigr|\leq\frac{3\sqrt{\epsilon}}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.21.1" class="ltx_text">By a union bound, the event <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m72" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> has probability at least <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m73" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-5\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-5\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. We conclude that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{n\in[N]}\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)|P\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\Bigl\{\bigl(\mathsf{Read}\circ\mathsf{TF}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr)^{2}\Bigr\}\leq\frac{9\epsilon}{16}+5R^{2}\delta\leq\epsilon," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖺𝖽</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{n\in[N]}\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)|P\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\Bigl\{\bigl(\mathsf{Read}\circ\mathsf{TF}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr)^{2}\Bigr\}\leq\frac{9\epsilon}{16}+5R^{2}\delta\leq\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.22" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.22.1" class="ltx_text">as required.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 3.2 Universal approximation and learnability ‣ 3 Transformers, universal approximation and learnability ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main idea behind the proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 3.2 Universal approximation and learnability ‣ 3 Transformers, universal approximation and learnability ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> is to use empirical process theory to upper bound <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> by the approximation error and a complexity measure of <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the literature, the complexity measure is often taken to be the covering number with respect to the uniform norm, and upper bounds on this covering number for Transformers are available, provided the input matrix and parameters are bounded. There, the proof strategy is to argue that for any input matrix from a bounded set, the output of the Transformer with bounded parameters is uniformly Lipschitz in its parameters. However, this argument does not work in our setting, since our input matrix and parameters are unbounded. Instead, we use the pseudo-dimension of <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> (see the definition below) as a complexity measure and show that the pseudo-dimension of Transformers is finite. This result (Lemma <a href="#Thmthm15" title="Lemma 15. ‣ C.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> below) may be of independent interest.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefn5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefn5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmdefn5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(VC-dimension and pseudo-dimension)<span id="Thmdefn5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefn5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefn5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefn5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefn5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a set and let <math id="Thmdefn5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be a collection of subsets of <math id="Thmdefn5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="Thmdefn5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\coloneqq\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}\subseteq X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\coloneqq\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}\subseteq X</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that <math id="Thmdefn5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> shatters <math id="Thmdefn5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> if for every <math id="Thmdefn5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\subseteq S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\subseteq S</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="Thmdefn5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmdefn5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\cap S=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\cap S=T</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="Thmdefn5.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">VC-dimension</em> of <math id="Thmdefn5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cardinality of the largest subset of <math id="Thmdefn5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> that can be shattered by <math id="Thmdefn5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefn5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefn5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefn5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Now let <math id="Thmdefn5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> be a set of functions from <math id="Thmdefn5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmdefn5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="Thmdefn5.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">pseudo-dimension</em> <math id="Thmdefn5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pdim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{G})</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmdefn5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> is the VC-dimension of its subgraph class <math id="Thmdefn5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\{\{(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathbb{R}:y\leq g(x)\}:g\in\mathcal{G}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\{\{(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathbb{R}:y\leq g(x)\}:g\in\mathcal{G}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#Thmthm13" title="Lemma 13. ‣ C.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> below controls <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the approximation error and pseudo-dimension of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 13</span></span><span id="Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the setting of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 3.2 Universal approximation and learnability ‣ 3 Transformers, universal approximation and learnability ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, there exists <math id="Thmthm13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, depending only on <math id="Thmthm13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\xi\|_{\psi_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\xi\|_{\psi_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for <math id="Thmthm13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})\leq 2\inf_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)|P\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\Bigl\{\bigl(f(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr)^{2}\Bigr\}+\frac{C\log^{3}(T)\cdot\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{F})}{T}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Pdim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})\leq 2\inf_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)|P\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\Bigl\{\bigl(f(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr)^{2}\Bigr\}+\frac{C\log^{3}(T)\cdot\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{F})}{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\sim\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\sim\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)|P\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)|P\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{D}_{n}^{(t)},X^{(t)},Y^{(t)})_{t\in[T]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{D}_{n}^{(t)},X^{(t)},Y^{(t)})_{t\in[T]}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent copies of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{(t)}\coloneqq(X^{(t)},\mathcal{D}_{n}^{(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{(t)}\coloneqq(X^{(t)},\mathcal{D}_{n}^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\coloneqq(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\coloneqq(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now note that <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\pi}(Z)=\mathbb{E}(Y\,|\,Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\pi}(Z)=\mathbb{E}(Y\,|\,Z)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{f}_{T}\in\argmin_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\bigl(Y^{(t)}-f(Z^{(t)})\bigr)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">argmin</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{f}_{T}\in\argmin_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\bigl(Y^{(t)}-f(Z^{(t)})\bigr)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})=\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(Y-\mathsf{clip}_{R}\widehat{f}_{T}(Z)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}-\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(Y-g_{\pi}(Z)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗂𝗉</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})=\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(Y-\mathsf{clip}_{R}\widehat{f}_{T}(Z)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}-\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(Y-g_{\pi}(Z)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">We have therefore reduced our problem to bounding the excess risk of a nonparametric regression estimator in a problem with bounded regression function and sub-Gaussian noise. The conclusion now follows by applying, for example, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma, Wang and Samworth (2025, Theorem 1)</a></cite> with the following minor modifications: (i) we ignore their <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> vectors since our data do not have missing values, (ii) by inspecting their proof, we may truncate <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> at level <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> since this is a known bound on the regression function, (iii) the optimisation error term (the first term in their upper bound) is zero since we consider the empirical risk minimiser, and (iv) by inspecting their proof and using <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Györfi et al. (2002, Theorem 9.4)</a></cite>, we can replace the third term in their upper bound by <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C\log^{3}(T)\cdot\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{F})}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Pdim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C\log^{3}(T)\cdot\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{F})}{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\xi\|_{\psi_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\xi\|_{\psi_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Next we will show that the class of Transformers with fixed architecture has finite pseudo-dimension. The proof uses terminology and results from model theory, a branch of mathematical logic. Since this field will probably be unfamiliar to most readers, we now provide a minimal glossary (sufficient for our proof) of the relevant terms; we refer the readers to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Marker (2002)</a></cite> for a formal introduction to model theory. We will be concerned with an object called a <em id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">structure</em>, which is a set equipped with a collection of distinguished functions, relations and elements that together give meaning to the symbols of a formal language. Our structure of interest is <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\coloneqq(\mathbb{R};0,1,+,-,\cdot,&lt;,\exp,\Phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\coloneqq(\mathbb{R};0,1,+,-,\cdot,&lt;,\exp,\Phi)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math> refers to multiplication, <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp:\mathbb{R}\to(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp:\mathbb{R}\to(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the exponential function and <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi:\mathbb{R}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:\mathbb{R}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the distribution function of the standard Gaussian distribution. Our goal is to show that Transformers can be defined within <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, in a sense that we will make precise below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Given a countable set <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> of variable symbols, which we intrepret as syntactic placeholders, the set of <em id="A3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">terms</em> in the structure <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\coloneqq(\mathbb{R};0,1,+,-,\cdot,&lt;,\exp,\Phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\coloneqq(\mathbb{R};0,1,+,-,\cdot,&lt;,\exp,\Phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is the smallest set <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> such that (i) <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, (ii) <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, (iii) if <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1},t_{2}\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1},t_{2}\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}+t_{2},\,t_{1}-t_{2},\,t_{1}\cdot t_{2}\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}+t_{2},\,t_{1}-t_{2},\,t_{1}\cdot t_{2}\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, and (iv) if <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(t),\Phi(t)\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(t),\Phi(t)\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. We say that <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is an <em id="A3.SS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">atomic formula</em> in <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is either <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}=t_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}=t_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}&lt;t_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}&lt;t_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, for some <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1},t_{2}\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1},t_{2}\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. The set of <em id="A3.SS2.p5.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(first-order) formulas</em> <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> in (the language of) <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is the smallest set such that (i) every atomic formula is in <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, (ii) if <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi,\psi\in\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi,\psi\in\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\neg\varphi),(\varphi\vee\psi),(\varphi\wedge\psi)\in\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\neg\varphi),(\varphi\vee\psi),(\varphi\wedge\psi)\in\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the logic symbolds <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\neg,\vee,\wedge" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>¬</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∨</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\neg,\vee,\wedge</annotation></semantics></math> stand for negation, disjunction and conjunction, and (iii) if <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi\in\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi\in\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists v\;\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists v\;\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall v\;\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall v\;\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> are in <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math>. For a formula <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi\in\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi\in\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that a variable <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A3.SS2.p5.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">free</em> in <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> if it is not inside a <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists v</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall v</annotation></semantics></math> quantifier; e.g. <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is free in the formula <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{1}=0)\vee(v_{1}&gt;0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{1}=0)\vee(v_{1}&gt;0)</annotation></semantics></math>, but it is not free in the formula <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists v_{1}\;v_{2}\cdot v_{2}=v_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists v_{1}\;v_{2}\cdot v_{2}=v_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. When a formula <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> has free variables <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},\ldots,v_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},\ldots,v_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we will often write <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(v_{1},\ldots,v_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(v_{1},\ldots,v_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> to make the free variables explicit. Now, letting <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(v_{1},\ldots,v_{n})\in\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(v_{1},\ldots,v_{n})\in\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> be a formula and <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=(a_{1},\ldots,a_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=(a_{1},\ldots,a_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\models\varphi(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\models\varphi(a)</annotation></semantics></math> (we read ‘<math id="A3.SS2.p5.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> entails <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(a)</annotation></semantics></math>’ or ‘<math id="A3.SS2.p5.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> models <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(a)</annotation></semantics></math>’) if <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(a)</annotation></semantics></math> is true in <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, and otherwise we write <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\not\models\varphi(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊧̸</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\not\models\varphi(a)</annotation></semantics></math>. For example, if <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(v_{1},v_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(v_{1},v_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is the formula <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{1}=v_{2})\vee(v_{1}+v_{2}=0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{1}=v_{2})\vee(v_{1}+v_{2}=0)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\models\varphi(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\models\varphi(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\models\varphi(-1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\models\varphi(-1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, but <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\not\models\varphi(1,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊧̸</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\not\models\varphi(1,2)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and a set <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">definable</em> (in <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>) if there exist <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, a formula <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(v_{1},\ldots,v_{d},w_{1},\ldots,w_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(v_{1},\ldots,v_{d},w_{1},\ldots,w_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\{a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\models\varphi(a,b)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\{a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\models\varphi(a,b)\}</annotation></semantics></math>; we will sometimes abbreviate the notation and write <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\{a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\varphi(a,b)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\{a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\varphi(a,b)\}</annotation></semantics></math> instead. For <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1},d_{2}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1},d_{2}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and a function <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\to\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A3.SS2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">definable</em> (in <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>) if its <em id="A3.SS2.p6.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">graph</em> <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}:y=f(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}:y=f(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a definable set in <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, for a collection <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> of subsets of <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A3.SS2.p6.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">uniformly definable</em> (in <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>) if there exists a formula <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(v,w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(v,w)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=(v_{1},\ldots,v_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=(v_{1},\ldots,v_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=(w_{1},\ldots,w_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=(w_{1},\ldots,w_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for every <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{C}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{C}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\{a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\varphi(a,b_{C})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\{a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\varphi(a,b_{C})\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, for a collection <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> of functions from <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A3.SS2.p6.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">uniformly definable</em> (in <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>) if the collection of graphs of functions in <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly definable.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 14</span></span><span id="Thmthm14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let </span><math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a collection of uniformly definable functions from </span><math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and let </span><math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a collection of uniformly definable functions from </span><math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then </span><math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\{\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}:y\leq f(x)\}:f\in\mathcal{F}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\{\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}:y\leq f(x)\}:f\in\mathcal{F}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{(x,z)\mapsto f(x)+g(z):f\in\mathcal{F},g\in\mathcal{G}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x,z)\mapsto f(x)+g(z):f\in\mathcal{F},g\in\mathcal{G}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{(x,z)\mapsto f(x)\cdot g(z):f\in\mathcal{F},g\in\mathcal{G}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x,z)\mapsto f(x)\cdot g(z):f\in\mathcal{F},g\in\mathcal{G}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are all uniformly definable.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let </span><math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a collection of uniformly definable functions from </span><math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then </span><math id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x\mapsto 1/f(x):f\in\mathcal{F}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x\mapsto 1/f(x):f\in\mathcal{F}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is uniformly definable.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let </span><math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and for </span><math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[p]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[p]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, let </span><math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a collection of uniformly definable functions from </span><math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for some </span><math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Further let </span><math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a collection of uniformly definable functions from </span><math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then </span><math id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bigl\{(x_{1},\ldots,x_{p})\mapsto f\bigl(g_{1}(x_{1}),\ldots,g_{p}(x_{p})\bigr):f\in\mathcal{F},g_{j}\in\mathcal{G}_{j}\,\forall j\in[p]\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.278em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\{(x_{1},\ldots,x_{p})\mapsto f\bigl(g_{1}(x_{1}),\ldots,g_{p}(x_{p})\bigr):f\in\mathcal{F},g_{j}\in\mathcal{G}_{j}\,\forall j\in[p]\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.ix3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is uniformly definable.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(a)</em><span id="A3.SS2.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Suppose that for each <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, the graph of <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}:\varphi(x,y,b_{f})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}:\varphi(x,y,b_{f})\}</annotation></semantics></math> for some formula <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>, some <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{f}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{f}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and some <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>; also suppose that for each <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, the graph of <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(z,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}\times\mathbb{R}:\psi(z,y,c_{g})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(z,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}\times\mathbb{R}:\psi(z,y,c_{g})\}</annotation></semantics></math> for some formula <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>, some <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{g}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{g}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and some <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. The subgraph <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}:y\leq f(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}:y\leq f(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}:\exists t\;\bigl(\varphi(x,t,b_{f})\wedge(y&lt;t\vee y=t)\bigr)\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.280em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}:\exists t\;\bigl(\varphi(x,t,b_{f})\wedge(y&lt;t\vee y=t)\bigr)\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the collection of subgraphs of <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly definable. For <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, the graph of the function <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,z)\mapsto f(x)+g(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,z)\mapsto f(x)+g(z)</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m20" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bigl\{(x,z,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}\times\mathbb{R}:\exists u,v\;\bigl(\varphi(x,u,b_{f})\wedge\psi(z,v,c_{g})\wedge(y=u+v)\bigr)\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\{(x,z,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}\times\mathbb{R}:\exists u,v\;\bigl(\varphi(x,u,b_{f})\wedge\psi(z,v,c_{g})\wedge(y=u+v)\bigr)\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, the graph of the function <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,z)\mapsto f(x)\cdot g(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,z)\mapsto f(x)\cdot g(z)</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bigl\{(x,z,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}\times\mathbb{R}:\exists u,v\;\bigl(\varphi(x,u,b_{f})\wedge\psi(z,v,c_{g})\wedge(y=u\cdot v)\bigr)\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\{(x,z,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}}\times\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}}\times\mathbb{R}:\exists u,v\;\bigl(\varphi(x,u,b_{f})\wedge\psi(z,v,c_{g})\wedge(y=u\cdot v)\bigr)\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(b)</em><span id="A3.SS2.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Again, suppose that for each <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, the graph of <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}:\varphi(x,y,b_{f})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}:\varphi(x,y,b_{f})\}</annotation></semantics></math> for some formula <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>, some <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{f}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{f}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and some <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, the graph of the function <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto 1/f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto 1/f(x)</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}:\exists u\;\bigl(\varphi(x,u,b_{f})\wedge(y\cdot u=1)\bigr)\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.280em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}:\exists u\;\bigl(\varphi(x,u,b_{f})\wedge(y\cdot u=1)\bigr)\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves the claim.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(c)</em><span id="A3.SS2.p9.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Suppose that for each <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, the graph of <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{p}\times\mathbb{R}:\varphi(x,y,b_{f})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{p}\times\mathbb{R}:\varphi(x,y,b_{f})\}</annotation></semantics></math> for some formula <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>, some <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{f}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{f}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and some <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>; also suppose that for <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[p]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[p]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{j}\in\mathcal{G}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{j}\in\mathcal{G}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, the graph of <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(z,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{j}}\times\mathbb{R}:\psi_{j}(z,y,c_{g_{j}})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(z,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{j}}\times\mathbb{R}:\psi_{j}(z,y,c_{g_{j}})\}</annotation></semantics></math> for some formula <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, some <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{g_{j}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{g_{j}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> and some <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{j}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{j}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the graph of the function <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},\ldots,x_{p})\mapsto f\bigl(g_{1}(x_{1}),\ldots,g_{p}(x_{p})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},\ldots,x_{p})\mapsto f\bigl(g_{1}(x_{1}),\ldots,g_{p}(x_{p})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\biggl\{(x_{1},\ldots,x_{p},y)\in\mathbb{R}^{p+1}:\exists v_{1},\ldots,v_{p}\biggl(\bigwedge_{j=1}^{p}\psi_{j}(x_{j},v_{j},c_{g_{j}})\wedge\varphi(v_{1},\ldots,v_{p},y,b_{f})\biggr)\biggr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>p</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\biggl\{(x_{1},\ldots,x_{p},y)\in\mathbb{R}^{p+1}:\exists v_{1},\ldots,v_{p}\biggl(\bigwedge_{j=1}^{p}\psi_{j}(x_{j},v_{j},c_{g_{j}})\wedge\varphi(v_{1},\ldots,v_{p},y,b_{f})\biggr)\biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">This proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 15</span></span><span id="Thmthm15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmthm15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L,H,{d_{\mathrm{model}}},d_{\mathrm{ffn}}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L,H,{d_{\mathrm{model}}},d_{\mathrm{ffn}}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, the class <math id="Thmthm15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{\prime}\coloneqq\mathsf{Read}\circ\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{TF}}(L,H,{d_{\mathrm{model}}},d_{\mathrm{ffn}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖺𝖽</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>TF</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{\prime}\coloneqq\mathsf{Read}\circ\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{TF}}(L,H,{d_{\mathrm{model}}},d_{\mathrm{ffn}})</annotation></semantics></math> has finite pseudo-dimension.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremarkx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremarkx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark</span></span><span id="Thmremarkx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremarkx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremarkx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremarkx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">It is possible to obtain upper bounds on the pseudo-dimension of <math id="Thmremarkx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with polynomial dependence on <math id="Thmremarkx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmremarkx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmremarkx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmremarkx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{ffn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{ffn}}</annotation></semantics></math> via a more detailed analysis, but a finite pseudo-dimension is already enough for our purpose.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined on the space <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{n=1}^{N}\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{n=1}^{N}\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, equipped with the disjoint union topology. Thus, it suffices to show that, for each <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, the restriction <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of the functions in <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> has finite pseudo-dimension.
Now let</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{C}_{n}\coloneqq\Bigl\{\bigl\{(Z,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}\times\mathbb{R}:y\leq f(Z)\bigr\}:f\in\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}\Bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{C}_{n}\coloneqq\Bigl\{\bigl\{(Z,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}\times\mathbb{R}:y\leq f(Z)\bigr\}:f\in\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}\Bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">denote the collection of subgraphs of <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by definition, the pseudo-dimension of <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the VC-dimension of <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will now show that <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly definable in <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>. The graph <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{2}:y=\relu(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{2}:y=\relu(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\relu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\relu</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{2}:\bigl(\neg(x&lt;0)\wedge y=x\bigr)\vee(x&lt;0\wedge y=0)\bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>¬</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∧</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{2}:\bigl(\neg(x&lt;0)\wedge y=x\bigr)\vee(x&lt;0\wedge y=0)\bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\relu:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\relu:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is definable on <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#Thmthm14" title="Lemma 14. ‣ C.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, sums, products, reciprocals and compositions of definable functions are definable. Thus, for any <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d,p\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d,p\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, the set of polynomials on <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with degree at most <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly definable in <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, since <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>exp</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> are definable in <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> by definition, we deduce that <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{GELU}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖦𝖤𝖫𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{GELU}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{SiLU}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝖫𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{SiLU}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\softmax" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗈𝖿𝗍𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\softmax</annotation></semantics></math> are also definable in <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each function <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> comprises compositions, sums and products of <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in\{\mathsf{ReLU},\mathsf{GELU},\mathsf{SiLU}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖫𝖴</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖦𝖤𝖫𝖴</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖲𝗂𝖫𝖴</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in\{\mathsf{ReLU},\mathsf{GELU},\mathsf{SiLU}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\softmax" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗈𝖿𝗍𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\softmax</annotation></semantics></math> and polynomials of degree at most two, we deduce by Lemma <a href="#Thmthm14" title="Lemma 14. ‣ C.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> that <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly definable in <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, by Lemma <a href="#Thmthm14" title="Lemma 14. ‣ C.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a><em id="A3.SS2.p10.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(a)</em>, we have that the subgraph class of <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{\prime}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is also uniformly definable on <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{C}_{n}\subseteq\Bigl\{\bigl\{a\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}\times\mathbb{R}:\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\models\varphi(a,b)\bigr\}:b\in\mathbb{R}^{m}\Bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊧</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{C}_{n}\subseteq\Bigl\{\bigl\{a\in\mathbb{R}^{(n+1)\times{d_{\mathrm{model}}}}\times\mathbb{R}:\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}\models\varphi(a,b)\bigr\}:b\in\mathbb{R}^{m}\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Marker (2002, Therorem 3.4.37)</a></cite>, the structure <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m34" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp}\coloneqq(\mathbb{R};0,1,+,-,\cdot,&lt;,\exp,\Phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp}\coloneqq(\mathbb{R};0,1,+,-,\cdot,&lt;,\exp,\Phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A3.SS2.p10.4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">o-minimal</em>, i.e. every definable set is a finite union of open intervals and singleton points. Further, the derivative <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> given by <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m36" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi^{\prime}(x)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-x^{2}/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\prime}(x)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-x^{2}/2}</annotation></semantics></math> is definable in <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp}</annotation></semantics></math>, so by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Speissegger (1999)</a></cite>, there exists an o-minimal extension <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>exp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp}</annotation></semantics></math> in which <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is definable. Now, every definable set in <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is definable in <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{\exp,\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is o-minimal.
We may therefore apply <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Laskowski (1992, Theorem 3.2)</a></cite> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(see also <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karpinski and Macintyre, 1995</a>, Theorem 2)</cite> to deduce that the VC-dimension of <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 3.2 Universal approximation and learnability ‣ 3 Transformers, universal approximation and learnability ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#Thmthm2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 Universal approximation and learnability ‣ 3 Transformers, universal approximation and learnability ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, there exist <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{model}}^{\circ}\geq d+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{model}}^{\circ}\geq d+2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{\circ}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{\circ}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that if <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\geq d_{\mathrm{model}}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{d_{\mathrm{model}}}\geq d_{\mathrm{model}}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{ffn}}\geq d_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{ffn}}\geq d_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}\coloneqq\mathsf{Read}\circ\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{TF}}(3,1,{d_{\mathrm{model}}},d_{\mathrm{ffn}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖺𝖽</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>TF</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>ffn</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}\coloneqq\mathsf{Read}\circ\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{TF}}(3,1,{d_{\mathrm{model}}},d_{\mathrm{ffn}})</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\inf_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)|P\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\Bigl\{\bigl(f(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr)^{2}\Bigr\}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{4}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\inf_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)|P\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\Bigl\{\bigl(f(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})\bigr)^{2}\Bigr\}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now by Lemma <a href="#Thmthm15" title="Lemma 15. ‣ C.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, we have that <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pdim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{F})</annotation></semantics></math> is finite. Thus, for all <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large, we have <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C\log^{3}(T)\cdot\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{F})}{T}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Pdim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C\log^{3}(T)\cdot\mathrm{Pdim}(\mathcal{F})}{T}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is taken from Lemma <a href="#Thmthm13" title="Lemma 13. ‣ C.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>. The claim then follows from Lemma <a href="#Thmthm13" title="Lemma 13. ‣ C.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Function spaces and wavelets</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Function spaces</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we restrict the domain of the functions to <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Jensen’s inequality, <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|_{L^{p_{1}}}\leq\|f\|_{L^{p_{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|_{L^{p_{1}}}\leq\|f\|_{L^{p_{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq p_{1}\leq p_{2}\leq\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq p_{1}\leq p_{2}\leq\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,g\in L^{2}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,g\in L^{2}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, define the inner product</p>
<table id="A4.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle f,g\rangle\coloneqq\int_{[0,1]^{d}}f(x)g(x)\,\mathrm{d}x." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle f,g\rangle\coloneqq\int_{[0,1]^{d}}f(x)g(x)\,\mathrm{d}x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of continuous functions from <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=(m_{1},\ldots,m_{d})^{\top}\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=(m_{1},\ldots,m_{d})^{\top}\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\coloneqq\|m\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\coloneqq\|m\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-times differentiable <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:[0,1]^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:[0,1]^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the multi-index notation <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial^{m}f\coloneqq\partial^{m_{1}}\cdots\partial^{m_{d}}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{m}f\coloneqq\partial^{m_{1}}\cdots\partial^{m_{d}}f</annotation></semantics></math> for partial derivatives.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefn6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefn6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6</span></span><span id="Thmdefn6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Hölder space)<span id="Thmdefn6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefn6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefn6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefn6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="Thmdefn6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmdefn6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}\coloneqq\lceil\alpha\rceil-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}\coloneqq\lceil\alpha\rceil-1</annotation></semantics></math> be the largest integer strictly smaller than <math id="Thmdefn6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and define the <em id="Thmdefn6.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">Hölder space</em> <math id="Thmdefn6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> to be the set of <math id="Thmdefn6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-times differentiable <math id="Thmdefn6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:[0,1]^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:[0,1]^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{x\neq y}\sum_{m\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d}:\|m\|_{1}=\alpha_{0}}\frac{\partial^{m}f(x)-\partial^{m}f(y)}{\|x-y\|_{2}^{\alpha-\alpha_{0}}}&lt;\infty." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>m</mi></msup><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>m</mi></msup><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{x\neq y}\sum_{m\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d}:\|m\|_{1}=\alpha_{0}}\frac{\partial^{m}f(x)-\partial^{m}f(y)}{\|x-y\|_{2}^{\alpha-\alpha_{0}}}&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the <em id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>th order difference operator</em> <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{h}^{r}:L^{1}([0,1]^{d})\rightarrow L^{1}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{h}^{r}:L^{1}([0,1]^{d})\rightarrow L^{1}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{h}^{r}(f)(x)=\mathbbm{1}_{\{x+rh\in[0,1]^{d}\}}\sum_{k=0}^{r}\binom{r}{k}(-1)^{r-k}f(x+kh)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{h}^{r}(f)(x)=\mathbbm{1}_{\{x+rh\in[0,1]^{d}\}}\sum_{k=0}^{r}\binom{r}{k}(-1)^{r-k}f(x+kh).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{h}^{1}(f)(x)=\{f(x+h)-f(x)\}\mathbbm{1}_{\{x+h\in[0,1]^{d}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{h}^{1}(f)(x)=\{f(x+h)-f(x)\}\mathbbm{1}_{\{x+h\in[0,1]^{d}\}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{h}^{r}(f)(x)=\Delta_{h}^{1}\bigl(\Delta_{h}^{r-1}(f)(x)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{h}^{r}(f)(x)=\Delta_{h}^{1}\bigl(\Delta_{h}^{r-1}(f)(x)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+rh\in[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+rh\in[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, for <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[1,\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[1,\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L^{p}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L^{p}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, define the <em id="A4.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="A4.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>th modulus of smoothness</em></p>
<table id="A4.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\omega_{r,p}(f,t)\coloneqq\sup_{\|h\|_{2}\leq t}\|\Delta_{h}^{r}(f)\|_{L^{p}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\omega_{r,p}(f,t)\coloneqq\sup_{\|h\|_{2}\leq t}\|\Delta_{h}^{r}(f)\|_{L^{p}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefn7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefn7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7</span></span><span id="Thmdefn7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Besov space)<span id="Thmdefn7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefn7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefn7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefn7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="Thmdefn7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in[1,\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in[1,\infty]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefn7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmdefn7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\coloneqq\lfloor\alpha\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\coloneqq\lfloor\alpha\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math> and define the <em id="Thmdefn7.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">Besov space</em> <math id="Thmdefn7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})\coloneqq\begin{cases}{\displaystyle\biggl\{f\in L^{p}([0,1]^{d}):\biggl[\int_{0}^{\infty}\bigl(t^{-\alpha}\omega_{r,p}(f,t)\bigr)^{q}\frac{\mathrm{d}t}{t}\biggr]^{1/q}&lt;\infty\biggr\}}\quad&amp;\text{for }q\in[1,\infty)\\[10.00002pt]
{\displaystyle\Bigl\{f\in L^{p}([0,1]^{d}):\sup_{t&gt;0}t^{-\alpha}\omega_{r,p}(f,t)&lt;\infty\Bigr\}}\quad&amp;\text{for }q=\infty.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>:</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.111em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})\coloneqq\begin{cases}{\displaystyle\biggl\{f\in L^{p}([0,1]^{d}):\biggl[\int_{0}^{\infty}\bigl(t^{-\alpha}\omega_{r,p}(f,t)\bigr)^{q}\frac{\mathrm{d}t}{t}\biggr]^{1/q}&lt;\infty\biggr\}}\quad&amp;\text{for }q\in[1,\infty)\\[10.00002pt]
{\displaystyle\Bigl\{f\in L^{p}([0,1]^{d}):\sup_{t&gt;0}t^{-\alpha}\omega_{r,p}(f,t)&lt;\infty\Bigr\}}\quad&amp;\text{for }q=\infty.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For non-integer smoothness levels, Hölder spaces are special cases of Besov spaces in the sense that <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})=B^{\alpha}_{\infty,\infty}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})=B^{\alpha}_{\infty,\infty}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,\infty)\setminus\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,\infty)\setminus\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, while for <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})\subseteq B^{\alpha}_{\infty,\infty}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})\subseteq B^{\alpha}_{\infty,\infty}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, and in fact, <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with Zygmund spaces when <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>; see e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Giné and Nickl (2021, p. 351)</a></cite> or <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Triebel (1983, Chapter 2.5.7)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Wavelets</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start with the univariate setting where the notation is simpler. For <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, denote the Cohen–Daubechies–Vial (CDV) wavelet basis on <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cohen, Daubechies and Vial, 1993</a>)</cite>, constructed from <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-regular and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-times continuously differentiable father and mother Daubechies wavelets <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Daubechies, 1988</a>)</cite>, by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl\{\phi_{k}:k\in[0:2^{\ell_{0}}-1]\bigr\}\bigcup\bigl\{\psi_{\ell,k}:\ell\in[{\ell_{0}}:\infty),\,k\in[0:2^{\ell}-1]\bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl\{\phi_{k}:k\in[0:2^{\ell_{0}}-1]\bigr\}\bigcup\bigl\{\psi_{\ell,k}:\ell\in[{\ell_{0}}:\infty),\,k\in[0:2^{\ell}-1]\bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{0}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{0}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. The precise definition and construction of this wavelet basis is not important for us, but the functions in (<a href="#A4.E27" title="In D.2 Wavelets ‣ Appendix D Function spaces and wavelets ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) are <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-times continuously differentiable and form an orthonormal basis for <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}([0,1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}([0,1])</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cohen, Daubechies and Vial, 1993</a>, Theorem 4.4)</cite>. Moreover, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is supported on <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl[\frac{k}{2^{\ell_{0}}},\frac{k+1}{2^{\ell_{0}}}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl[\frac{k}{2^{\ell_{0}}},\frac{k+1}{2^{\ell_{0}}}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k\in[0:2^{\ell_{0}}-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[0:2^{\ell_{0}}-1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\ell,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\ell,k}</annotation></semantics></math> is supported on <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl[\frac{k}{2^{\ell}},\frac{k+1}{2^{\ell}}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl[\frac{k}{2^{\ell}},\frac{k+1}{2^{\ell}}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell\in[{\ell_{0}}:\infty),\,k\in[0:2^{\ell}-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[{\ell_{0}}:\infty),\,k\in[0:2^{\ell}-1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The one-dimensional CDV wavelets in (<a href="#A4.E27" title="In D.2 Wavelets ‣ Appendix D Function spaces and wavelets ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) can be extended to an orthonormal basis for <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> via tensor products. For <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k=(k_{1},\ldots,k_{d})^{\top}\in[0:2^{\ell_{0}}-1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=(k_{1},\ldots,k_{d})^{\top}\in[0:2^{\ell_{0}}-1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{d})^{\top}\in[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{d})^{\top}\in[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A4.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Phi_{k}(x)\coloneqq\prod_{j=1}^{d}\phi_{k_{j}}(x_{j})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Phi_{k}(x)\coloneqq\prod_{j=1}^{d}\phi_{k_{j}}(x_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Further, for <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{d})^{\top}\in\{0,1\}^{d}\setminus\{\bm{0}_{d}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{d})^{\top}\in\{0,1\}^{d}\setminus\{\bm{0}_{d}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell\in[{\ell_{0}}:\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[{\ell_{0}}:\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k=(k_{1},\ldots,k_{d})^{\top}\in[0:2^{\ell}-1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=(k_{1},\ldots,k_{d})^{\top}\in[0:2^{\ell}-1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{d})^{\top}\in[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{d})^{\top}\in[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A4.EGx96" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{\ell,k}^{(\tau)}(x)\coloneqq\prod_{j=1}^{d}\psi^{(\tau_{j})}_{\ell,k_{j}}(x_{j})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{\ell,k}^{(\tau)}(x)\coloneqq\prod_{j=1}^{d}\psi^{(\tau_{j})}_{\ell,k_{j}}(x_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{(1)}_{\ell,k^{\prime}}=\psi_{\ell,k^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{(1)}_{\ell,k^{\prime}}=\psi_{\ell,k^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k^{\prime}\in[0:2^{\ell}-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}\in[0:2^{\ell}-1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\psi^{(0)}_{\ell,k^{\prime}})_{k^{\prime}=0}^{2^{\ell}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\psi^{(0)}_{\ell,k^{\prime}})_{k^{\prime}=0}^{2^{\ell}-1}</annotation></semantics></math> are the boundary-corrected (<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-regular and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-times continuously differentiable) father Daubechies wavelets at resolution <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>. Again, the precise definition and construction are not important for us, but we will exploit the following properties. To simplify notation, define</p>
<table id="A4.EGx97" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle K\coloneqq[0:2^{\ell_{0}}-1]^{d}\quad\text{and}\quad\Gamma_{\ell}\coloneqq[0:2^{\ell}-1]^{d}\times\bigl(\{0,1\}^{d}\setminus\{\bm{0}_{d}\}\bigr)\text{ for }\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mtext>and</mtext><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mtext> for </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K\coloneqq[0:2^{\ell_{0}}-1]^{d}\quad\text{and}\quad\Gamma_{\ell}\coloneqq[0:2^{\ell}-1]^{d}\times\bigl(\{0,1\}^{d}\setminus\{\bm{0}_{d}\}\bigr)\text{ for }\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">and for <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=(k,\tau)\in\Gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=(k,\tau)\in\Gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}\coloneqq\Psi_{\ell,k}^{(\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}\coloneqq\Psi_{\ell,k}^{(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx98" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle|K|=2^{\ell_{0}d}\quad\text{and}\quad|\Gamma_{\ell}|=2^{\ell d}(2^{d}-1)&lt;2^{(\ell+1)d}\text{ for }\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>K</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mtext>and</mtext><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mtext> for </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|K|=2^{\ell_{0}d}\quad\text{and}\quad|\Gamma_{\ell}|=2^{\ell d}(2^{d}-1)&lt;2^{(\ell+1)d}\text{ for }\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Each term in the products in (<a href="#A4.E28" title="In D.2 Wavelets ‣ Appendix D Function spaces and wavelets ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E29" title="In D.2 Wavelets ‣ Appendix D Function spaces and wavelets ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) is <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-times continuously differentiable, and the functions</p>
<table id="A4.EGx99" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl\{\Phi_{k}:k\in K\bigr\}\cup\bigl\{\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}:\ell\in[{\ell_{0}}:\infty),\,\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl\{\Phi_{k}:k\in K\bigr\}\cup\bigl\{\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}:\ell\in[{\ell_{0}}:\infty),\,\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p">form an orthonormal basis for <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>; see e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Giné and Nickl (2021, Chapter 4.3.6)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dahmen (1997, Section 4)</a></cite>. By construction, there exist <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C,C^{\prime}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C,C^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (depending only on <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>) such that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx100" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\Phi_{k}\|_{\infty}\leq C2^{\ell_{0}d/2}\quad\text{and}\quad\|\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}\|_{\infty}\leq C2^{\ell d/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\Phi_{k}\|_{\infty}\leq C2^{\ell_{0}d/2}\quad\text{and}\quad\|\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}\|_{\infty}\leq C2^{\ell d/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.7" class="ltx_p">for <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, and that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx101" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k\in K}\mathbbm{1}_{\{\Phi_{k}(x)\neq 0\}}\vee\sup_{\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}\mathbbm{1}_{\{\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}(x)\neq 0\}}\leq C^{\prime}\quad\text{for all }x\in[0,1]^{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∨</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext>for all </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k\in K}\mathbbm{1}_{\{\Phi_{k}(x)\neq 0\}}\vee\sup_{\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}\mathbbm{1}_{\{\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}(x)\neq 0\}}\leq C^{\prime}\quad\text{for all }x\in[0,1]^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.8" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L^{2}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L^{2}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the wavelet decomposition</p>
<table id="A4.EGx102" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f=\sum_{k\in K}a_{k}\Phi_{k}+\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}b_{\ell,\gamma}\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f=\sum_{k\in K}a_{k}\Phi_{k}+\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}b_{\ell,\gamma}\Psi_{\ell,\gamma},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.9" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}\coloneqq\langle f,\Phi_{k}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}\coloneqq\langle f,\Phi_{k}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\ell,\gamma}\coloneqq\langle f,\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\ell,\gamma}\coloneqq\langle f,\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</p>
<table id="A4.EGx103" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle a\coloneqq(a_{k})_{k\in K}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}\quad\text{and}\quad b_{\ell}\coloneqq(b_{\ell,\gamma})_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}\in\mathbb{R}^{\Gamma_{\ell}}\text{ for }\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mtext>and</mtext><msub><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msup><mtext> for </mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a\coloneqq(a_{k})_{k\in K}\in\mathbb{R}^{K}\quad\text{and}\quad b_{\ell}\coloneqq(b_{\ell,\gamma})_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}\in\mathbb{R}^{\Gamma_{\ell}}\text{ for }\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.10" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L^{2}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L^{2}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[2,\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[2,\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in[1,\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in[1,\infty]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,S)</annotation></semantics></math>, define its Besov norm by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx104" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|f\|_{B_{p,q}^{\alpha}}\coloneqq\begin{cases}\displaystyle 2^{\ell_{0}(d/2-d/p)}\|a\|_{p}+\biggl\{\sum_{\ell={\ell_{0}}}^{\infty}\bigl(2^{\ell(\alpha+d/2-d/p)}\|b_{\ell}\|_{p}\bigr)^{q}\biggr\}^{1/q}\quad&amp;\text{for }q\in[1,\infty)\\
\displaystyle 2^{\ell_{0}(d/2-d/p)}\|a\|_{p}+\sup_{\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)}2^{\ell(\alpha+d/2-d/p)}\|b_{\ell}\|_{p}\quad&amp;\text{for }q=\infty.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f\|_{B_{p,q}^{\alpha}}\coloneqq\begin{cases}\displaystyle 2^{\ell_{0}(d/2-d/p)}\|a\|_{p}+\biggl\{\sum_{\ell={\ell_{0}}}^{\infty}\bigl(2^{\ell(\alpha+d/2-d/p)}\|b_{\ell}\|_{p}\bigr)^{q}\biggr\}^{1/q}\quad&amp;\text{for }q\in[1,\infty)\\
\displaystyle 2^{\ell_{0}(d/2-d/p)}\|a\|_{p}+\sup_{\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)}2^{\ell(\alpha+d/2-d/p)}\|b_{\ell}\|_{p}\quad&amp;\text{for }q=\infty.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.11" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[2,\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[2,\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in[1,\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in[1,\infty]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,S)</annotation></semantics></math>, the Besov space <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> in Definition <a href="#Thmdefn7" title="Definition 7 (Besov space). ‣ D.1 Function spaces ‣ Appendix D Function spaces and wavelets ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> can be equivalently characterised by wavelet coefficients in the sense that <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L^{2}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L^{2}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|_{B_{p,q}^{\alpha}}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|_{B_{p,q}^{\alpha}}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(e.g. <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Giné and Nickl, 2021</a>, Chapter 4.3.6)</cite>. Therefore, we can define a closed ball <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d},R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d},R)</annotation></semantics></math> of radius <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> in the space <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx105" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d},R)\coloneqq\{f\in L^{2}([0,1]^{d}):\|f\|_{B_{p,q}^{\alpha}}\leq R\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{p,q}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{d},R)\coloneqq\{f\in L^{2}([0,1]^{d}):\|f\|_{B_{p,q}^{\alpha}}\leq R\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.12" class="ltx_p">As a special case, we have <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m41" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|f\|_{B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}}=2^{\ell_{0}d/2}\|a\|_{\infty}+\sup_{\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)}2^{\ell(\alpha+d/2)}\|b_{\ell}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|_{B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}}=2^{\ell_{0}d/2}\|a\|_{\infty}+\sup_{\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)}2^{\ell(\alpha+d/2)}\|b_{\ell}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Posterior contraction and adaptation</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>General theory</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section is primarily based on material from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ghosal, Lember and van der Vaart (2008)</a></cite>; see also <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ghosal and van der Vaart (2017, Section 10.2)</a></cite>. Here, we make some modifications in order to obtain finite-sample posterior contraction at an exponential rate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> be a measurable space and let <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be a countable index set. For <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> be a space of distributions on <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> dominated by a <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-finite measure <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}\coloneqq\bigcup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}\coloneqq\bigcup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a metric space when equipped with the Hellinger metric <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For example, <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> might index smoothness, in which case <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> might denote the set of distributions of <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> for which the regression function <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto\mathbb{E}(Y\,|\,X=x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto\mathbb{E}(Y\,|\,X=x)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth. For <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> be a distribution on <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=(\lambda_{\alpha})_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=(\lambda_{\alpha})_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> be such that <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\alpha}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\alpha}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\lambda_{\alpha}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\lambda_{\alpha}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. We consider a prior distribution <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> of the form</p>
<table id="A5.EGx106" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi\coloneqq\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\lambda_{\alpha}\pi_{\alpha}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi\coloneqq\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\lambda_{\alpha}\pi_{\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}\in\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}\in\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, we may define a distribution on <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A5.EGx107" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi(B\,|\,z_{1},\ldots,z_{n})\coloneqq\frac{\int_{B}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}\nu}(z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P)}{\int_{\mathcal{P}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}\nu}(z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi(B\,|\,z_{1},\ldots,z_{n})\coloneqq\frac{\int_{B}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}\nu}(z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P)}{\int_{\mathcal{P}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}\nu}(z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">for any measurable <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\subseteq\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\subseteq\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m27" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot\,|\,Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot\,|\,Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> would be the posterior distribution when <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> has prior distribution <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n}\,|\,P\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{iid}}}{{\sim}}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>iid</mi></mover><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n}\,|\,P\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{iid}}}{{\sim}}P</annotation></semantics></math>. In the sequel, however, we will assume instead that <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{iid}}}{{\sim}}P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mover><mo>∼</mo><mi>iid</mi></mover><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\mathrm{iid}}}{{\sim}}P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for some fixed distribution <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, and seek bounds on the expected mass assigned by <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m34" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot\,|\,Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot\,|\,Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> to (Hellinger) balls around <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, a distribution <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> dominated by <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, and for <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A5.EGx108" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle B_{\alpha}(P_{0},\epsilon)\coloneqq\Bigl\{P\in\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}:\mathrm{KL}(P_{0},P)\leq\epsilon^{2},\,\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{0},P)\leq\epsilon^{2}\Bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{\alpha}(P_{0},\epsilon)\coloneqq\Bigl\{P\in\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}:\mathrm{KL}(P_{0},P)\leq\epsilon^{2},\,\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{0},P)\leq\epsilon^{2}\Bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A5.EGx109" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{0},\epsilon)\coloneqq\Bigl\{P\in\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}:d_{\mathrm{H}}(P_{0},P)\leq\epsilon\Bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{0},\epsilon)\coloneqq\Bigl\{P\in\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}:d_{\mathrm{H}}(P_{0},P)\leq\epsilon\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon_{n,\alpha})_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon_{n,\alpha})_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a positive sequence, thought of as the rate of convergence in Hellinger distance on each <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</p>
<table id="A5.EGx110" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{A}_{\geq\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{A}_{\geq\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex105.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\bigl\{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}:\epsilon_{n,\alpha}^{2}\leq H\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\bigl\{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}:\epsilon_{n,\alpha}^{2}\leq H\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex106.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\bigl\{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}:\epsilon_{n,\alpha}^{2}&gt;H\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}\bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\bigl\{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}:\epsilon_{n,\alpha}^{2}&gt;H\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}\bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">to be the sets of indices that are ‘at least as regular as <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>’ and ‘less regular than <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>’, respectively. Here <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> should be thought of as the index of the ‘best model’ for <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We now state five conditions for our posterior contraction theory:</p>
<ol id="A5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(C1)</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Covering number bound: There exists a positive sequence <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E_{\alpha})_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E_{\alpha})_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx111" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{\epsilon\geq\epsilon_{n,\alpha}}\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\epsilon/3,\,B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{0},2\epsilon),\,d_{\mathrm{H}}\bigr)\leq E_{\alpha}n\epsilon_{n,\alpha}^{2}\quad\text{for all }\alpha\in\mathcal{A}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{\epsilon\geq\epsilon_{n,\alpha}}\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\epsilon/3,\,B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{0},2\epsilon),\,d_{\mathrm{H}}\bigr)\leq E_{\alpha}n\epsilon_{n,\alpha}^{2}\quad\text{for all }\alpha\in\mathcal{A}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(C2)</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Prior mass lower bound for <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>: There exists <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx112" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\beta}\bigl(B_{\beta}(P_{0},\epsilon_{n,\beta})\bigr)\geq e^{-Fn\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\beta}\bigl(B_{\beta}(P_{0},\epsilon_{n,\beta})\bigr)\geq e^{-Fn\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(C3)</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Mixture weights: There exists a positive sequence <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{n,\alpha})_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{n,\alpha})_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx113" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\lambda_{\alpha}}{\lambda_{\beta}}\leq\mu_{n,\alpha}\,e^{n(H^{-1}\epsilon_{n,\alpha}^{2}\vee\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2})}\quad\text{for all }\alpha\in\mathcal{A}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>∨</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\lambda_{\alpha}}{\lambda_{\beta}}\leq\mu_{n,\alpha}\,e^{n(H^{-1}\epsilon_{n,\alpha}^{2}\vee\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2})}\quad\text{for all }\alpha\in\mathcal{A}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(C4)</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Prior mass upper bound for <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>: There exist <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M,G&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M,G&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx114" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}}\frac{\lambda_{\alpha}}{\lambda_{\beta}}\cdot\pi_{\alpha}\bigl(B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{0},M\epsilon_{n,\alpha})\bigr)\leq Ge^{-(F+3)n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}}\frac{\lambda_{\alpha}}{\lambda_{\beta}}\cdot\pi_{\alpha}\bigl(B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{0},M\epsilon_{n,\alpha})\bigr)\leq Ge^{-(F+3)n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(C5)</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Uniformity of covering number constants: There exists <math id="A5.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\in(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\in(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx115" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E\geq\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}}E_{\alpha}\vee\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}_{\geq\beta}}\frac{E_{\alpha}\epsilon_{n,\alpha}^{2}}{\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E\geq\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}}E_{\alpha}\vee\sup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}_{\geq\beta}}\frac{E_{\alpha}\epsilon_{n,\alpha}^{2}}{\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The set <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> may be empty; in that case, condition <a href="#A5.I1.i4" title="item (C4) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C4)</span></a> is automatically satisfied, and the supremum over the empty set in <a href="#A5.I1.i5" title="item (C5) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C5)</span></a> is defined as <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The following theorem is a modification of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ghosal, Lember and van der Vaart (2008, Theorem 2.1)</a></cite>, where we use a slightly larger constant in the exponent in <a href="#A5.I1.i4" title="item (C4) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C4)</span></a> and impose an additional sub-Gamma assumption on the log-likelihood ratios in order to obtain exponential posterior contraction (as opposed to the weaker conclusion that the left-hand side of (<a href="#A5.E39" title="In Proposition 16. ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) converges to zero as <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>). In our in-context learning problem, this is crucial to derive rates of convergence for the posterior regression function. The sub-Gamma assumption is verified in Lemma <a href="#Thmthm24" title="Lemma 24. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a><em id="A5.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(c)</em> under a nonparametric regression setting with independent Gaussian noise.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 16</span></span><span id="Thmthm16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a distribution on <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n}\overset{\mathrm{iid}}{\sim}P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">iid</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n}\overset{\mathrm{iid}}{\sim}P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume that the conditions <a href="#A5.I1.i1" title="item (C1) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C1)</span></a>–<a href="#A5.I1.i5" title="item (C5) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C5)</span></a> hold with <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{2}&gt;243(F+1)(HE+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>243</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{2}&gt;243(F+1)(HE+1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\sqrt{\mu_{n,\alpha}}\leq e^{n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><msqrt><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\sqrt{\mu_{n,\alpha}}\leq e^{n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathcal{P}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathcal{P}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> with with <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\ll P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≪</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\ll P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, let</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(P,Z_{i})\coloneqq\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})-\mathbb{E}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(P,Z_{i})\coloneqq\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})-\mathbb{E}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm16.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm16.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that there exist <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in B_{\beta}(P_{0},\epsilon_{n,\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in B_{\beta}(P_{0},\epsilon_{n,\beta})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(P,Z_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(P,Z_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gamma in the left tail with variance parameter <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and scale parameter <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exist <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},c_{2},c_{3}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},c_{2},c_{3}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, not depending on <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, such that if <math id="Thmthm16.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}\geq c_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}\geq c_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx116" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{(Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n})\sim P_{0}^{\otimes n}}\bigl[\pi\bigl(\{P\in\mathcal{P}:d_{\mathrm{H}}(P,P_{0})\geq M\epsilon_{n,\beta}\}\,\big|\,Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n}\bigr)\bigr]\leq C_{1}e^{-c_{2}n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{(Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n})\sim P_{0}^{\otimes n}}\bigl[\pi\bigl(\{P\in\mathcal{P}:d_{\mathrm{H}}(P,P_{0})\geq M\epsilon_{n,\beta}\}\,\big|\,Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n}\bigr)\bigr]\leq C_{1}e^{-c_{2}n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Our assumptions ensure that the conditions of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ghosal, Lember and van der Vaart (2008, Theorem 2.1)</a></cite> hold<span id="footnote6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">6</span>
                  
                  
                  
                As we seek a finite-sample bound, we do not require their condition that <math id="footnote6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="footnote6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span> with <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1/9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1/9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=K/3=1/27" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=K/3=1/27</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I=\sqrt{27(F+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I=\sqrt{27(F+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=M/I=M/\sqrt{27(F+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=M/I=M/\sqrt{27(F+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> therein. Moreover, our conditions <a href="#A5.I1.i2" title="item (C2) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C2)</span></a> and <a href="#A5.I1.i4" title="item (C4) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C4)</span></a> ensure that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx117" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}}\frac{\lambda_{\alpha}}{\lambda_{\beta}}\cdot\frac{\pi_{\alpha}\bigl(B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{0},M\epsilon_{n,\alpha})\bigr)}{\pi_{\beta}\bigl(B_{\beta}(P_{0},\epsilon_{n,\beta})\bigr)}\leq Ge^{-3n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}}\frac{\lambda_{\alpha}}{\lambda_{\beta}}\cdot\frac{\pi_{\alpha}\bigl(B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{0},M\epsilon_{n,\alpha})\bigr)}{\pi_{\beta}\bigl(B_{\beta}(P_{0},\epsilon_{n,\beta})\bigr)}\leq Ge^{-3n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now, by following the proof of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ghosal, Lember and van der Vaart (2008, Theorem 2.1)</a></cite>, replacing the use of their Eq. (2.4) by our (<a href="#A5.E40" title="In Proof. ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>), and the use of their Lemma 6.3 by our Lemma <a href="#Thmthm23" title="Lemma 23. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a> (which applies because of our sub-Gamma assumption on <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(P,Z_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(P,Z_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>), we deduce the desired conclusion.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Bayesian nonparametric regression</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}=\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}=\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this section, we specialise to the setting of regression and take <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}=\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}=\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Borel distribution on <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\sim N(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\sim N(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> be independent of <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and for <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> be a space of measurable functions from <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-R,R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-R,R]</annotation></semantics></math>. For any Borel measurable function <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> for the distribution of <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y_{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y_{g})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{g}=g(X)+\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{g}=g(X)+\xi</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> be a distribution on <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}\sim\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}\sim\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distribution of the random measure <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the randomness comes from <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}\sim\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}\sim\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\pi}\coloneqq\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\lambda_{\alpha}\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\pi}\coloneqq\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\lambda_{\alpha}\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\coloneqq\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\lambda_{\alpha}\pi_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\coloneqq\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\lambda_{\alpha}\pi_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\alpha}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\alpha}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\lambda_{\alpha}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\lambda_{\alpha}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> be the support of <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}\coloneqq\bigcup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}\coloneqq\bigcup_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first provide an alternative expression for the <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>-posterior regression function <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined in (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2 Problem set-up and ICL excess risk decomposition ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). For <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{P}:\mathcal{X}\to\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{P}:\mathcal{X}\to\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the regression function under <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{P}(x)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{(X,Y)\sim P}(Y\,|\,X=x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{P}(x)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{(X,Y)\sim P}(Y\,|\,X=x)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>-posterior regression function <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="A5.EGx118" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{\pi}(x,D_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{\pi}(x,D_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex113.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)|P\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\bigl\{\mathbb{E}(Y\,|\,X=x,\,P)\,|\,X=x,\,\mathcal{D}_{n}=D_{n}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)|P\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\bigl\{\mathbb{E}(Y\,|\,X=x,\,P)\,|\,X=x,\,\mathcal{D}_{n}=D_{n}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)|P\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\bigl(g_{P}(x)\,|\,\mathcal{D}_{n}=D_{n}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\pi,\,(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)|P\sim P^{\otimes(n+1)}}\bigl(g_{P}(x)\,|\,\mathcal{D}_{n}=D_{n}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{P}}g_{P}(x)\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P\,|\,D_{n})=\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(x)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g\,|\,D_{n})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathcal{P}}g_{P}(x)\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P\,|\,D_{n})=\int_{\mathcal{G}}g(x)\,\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}(g\,|\,D_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\pi}(\cdot,D_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\pi}(\cdot,D_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> can be thought of as the posterior mean of the regression function.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 17</span></span><span id="Thmthm17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmthm17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{0}:\mathcal{X}\to[-R,R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{0}:\mathcal{X}\to[-R,R]</annotation></semantics></math> be measurable and write <math id="Thmthm17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}\equiv P_{g^{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}\equiv P_{g^{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that the conditions <a href="#A5.I1.i1" title="item (C1) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C1)</span></a>–<a href="#A5.I1.i5" title="item (C5) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C5)</span></a> hold with <math id="Thmthm17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{2}&gt;243(F+1)(HE+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>243</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{2}&gt;243(F+1)(HE+1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\sqrt{\mu_{n,\alpha}}\leq e^{n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><msqrt><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\sqrt{\mu_{n,\alpha}}\leq e^{n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
There exist <math id="Thmthm17.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2},c_{3},c_{4}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2},c_{3},c_{4}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, not depending on <math id="Thmthm17.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, such that if <math id="Thmthm17.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}\geq c_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}\geq c_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx119" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)\sim P_{0}^{\otimes(n+1)}}\bigl[\bigl\{g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g^{0}(X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]\leq C_{1}\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}+C_{2}e^{-c_{3}n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)\sim P_{0}^{\otimes(n+1)}}\bigl[\bigl\{g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g^{0}(X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]\leq C_{1}\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}+C_{2}e^{-c_{3}n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We write <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{P_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{P_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)\sim P_{0}^{\otimes(n+1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{D}_{n},X,Y)\sim P_{0}^{\otimes(n+1)}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{1}^{\prime}\coloneqq 2R^{2}/\bigl(1-e^{-R^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}^{\prime}\coloneqq 2R^{2}/\bigl(1-e^{-R^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>. We have by (<a href="#A5.E41" title="In E.2 Bayesian nonparametric regression ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx120" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{P_{0}}\bigl[\bigl\{g_{\pi}(X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{P_{0}}\bigl[\bigl\{g_{\pi}(X</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex116.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g^{0}(X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}_{P_{0}}\biggl[\biggl\{\int_{\mathcal{P}}g_{P}(X)\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P\,|\,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g^{0}(X)\biggr\}^{2}\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g^{0}(X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}_{P_{0}}\biggl[\biggl\{\int_{\mathcal{P}}g_{P}(X)\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P\,|\,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g^{0}(X)\biggr\}^{2}\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\leq}\mathbb{E}_{P_{0}}\biggl[\int_{\mathcal{P}}\bigl\{g_{P}(X)-g^{0}(X)\bigr\}^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P\,|\,\mathcal{D}_{n})\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\leq}\mathbb{E}_{P_{0}}\biggl[\int_{\mathcal{P}}\bigl\{g_{P}(X)-g^{0}(X)\bigr\}^{2}\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P\,|\,\mathcal{D}_{n})\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{=}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{n}\sim P_{0}^{\otimes n}}\biggl(\int_{\mathcal{P}}\mathbb{E}_{(X,Y)\sim P_{0}}\bigl[\bigl\{g_{P}(X)-g^{0}(X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P\,|\,\mathcal{D}_{n})\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{=}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{n}\sim P_{0}^{\otimes n}}\biggl(\int_{\mathcal{P}}\mathbb{E}_{(X,Y)\sim P_{0}}\bigl[\bigl\{g_{P}(X)-g^{0}(X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P\,|\,\mathcal{D}_{n})\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\leq}C_{1}^{\prime}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{n}\sim P_{0}^{\otimes n}}\biggl[\int_{\mathcal{P}}d_{\mathrm{H}}^{2}(P,P_{0})\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P\,|\,\mathcal{D}_{n})\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\leq}C_{1}^{\prime}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{n}\sim P_{0}^{\otimes n}}\biggl[\int_{\mathcal{P}}d_{\mathrm{H}}^{2}(P,P_{0})\,\mathrm{d}\pi(P\,|\,\mathcal{D}_{n})\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\leq}C_{1}^{\prime}M^{2}\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}+2C_{1}^{\prime}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{n}\sim P_{0}^{\otimes n}}\bigl[\pi\bigl(\{P\in\mathcal{P}:d_{\mathrm{H}}(P,P_{0})\geq M\epsilon_{n,\beta}\}\,\big|\,\mathcal{D}_{n}\bigr)\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\leq}C_{1}^{\prime}M^{2}\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}+2C_{1}^{\prime}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{n}\sim P_{0}^{\otimes n}}\bigl[\pi\bigl(\{P\in\mathcal{P}:d_{\mathrm{H}}(P,P_{0})\geq M\epsilon_{n,\beta}\}\,\big|\,\mathcal{D}_{n}\bigr)\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\leq}C_{1}\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}+C_{2}e^{-c_{3}n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\leq}C_{1}\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}+C_{2}e^{-c_{3}n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here, <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from Jensen’s inequality, <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ii)</annotation></semantics></math> follows by Fubini’s theorem, <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iii)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from Lemma <a href="#Thmthm24" title="Lemma 24. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a><em id="A5.SS2.p3.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(d)</em>, <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iv)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iv)</annotation></semantics></math> follows by splitting the integral into regions where <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{H}}(P,P_{0})&lt;M\epsilon_{n,\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{H}}(P,P_{0})&lt;M\epsilon_{n,\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{H}}(P,P_{0})\geq M\epsilon_{n,\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{H}}(P,P_{0})\geq M\epsilon_{n,\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from Proposition <a href="#Thmthm16" title="Proposition 16. ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> where the sub-Gamma assumption is verified in Lemma <a href="#Thmthm24" title="Lemma 24. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a><em id="A5.SS2.p3.2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(c)</em>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Proofs for Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with two preliminary lemmas in the setting of Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. Suppose that <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\circ}\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\circ}\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> has wavelet decomposition</p>
<table id="A6.EGx121" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle g^{\circ}=\sum_{k\in K}C_{0}2^{-\ell_{0}d/2}a_{k}^{\circ}\Phi_{k}+\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}C_{0}2^{-\ell(\beta+d/2)}b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ}\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g^{\circ}=\sum_{k\in K}C_{0}2^{-\ell_{0}d/2}a_{k}^{\circ}\Phi_{k}+\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}C_{0}2^{-\ell(\beta+d/2)}b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ}\Psi_{\ell,\gamma},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{k}^{\circ})_{k\in K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{k}^{\circ})_{k\in K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ})_{\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty),\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ})_{\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty),\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math> are deterministic and satisfy <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a^{\circ}_{k}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a^{\circ}_{k}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|b^{\circ}_{\ell,\gamma}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|b^{\circ}_{\ell,\gamma}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[\ell_{0}:\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Lemma <a href="#Thmthm18" title="Lemma 18. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> below provides a lower bound on the prior mass; similar results for the one-dimensional case exist in the literature, e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Giné and Nickl (2011, Proposition 1)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Reiß and Schmidt-Hieber (2020, Lemma 4.1)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 18</span></span><span id="Thmthm18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and assume that (<a href="#A6.E42" title="In F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) holds. Then there exists <math id="Thmthm18.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, depending only on <math id="Thmthm18.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,d,c_{0},C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,d,c_{0},C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm18.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx122" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta}\bigl(\bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}^{2}\leq Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}\bigr\}\bigr)\geq\exp\bigl(-Cn^{d/(2\beta+d)}\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta}\bigl(\bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}^{2}\leq Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}\bigr\}\bigr)\geq\exp\bigl(-Cn^{d/(2\beta+d)}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm18.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm18.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, there exists <math id="Thmthm18.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, depending only on <math id="Thmthm18.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,d,c_{0},C_{0},S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,d,c_{0},C_{0},S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm18.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx123" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\beta}\bigl(B_{\beta}(P_{g^{\circ}},\epsilon_{n,\beta})\bigr)\geq\exp\bigl(-C^{\prime}n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\beta}\bigl(B_{\beta}(P_{g^{\circ}},\epsilon_{n,\beta})\bigr)\geq\exp\bigl(-C^{\prime}n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm18.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm18.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmthm18.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\epsilon_{n,\beta}\coloneqq C^{\prime}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{n,\beta}\coloneqq C^{\prime}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm18.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\beta}(P_{g^{\circ}},\epsilon_{n,\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\beta}(P_{g^{\circ}},\epsilon_{n,\beta})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by (<a href="#A5.E37" title="In E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout the proof, <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> will denote positive quantities that may depend only on <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,d,c_{0},C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,d,c_{0},C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}^{\prime},C_{2}^{\prime},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}^{\prime},C_{2}^{\prime},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> may in addition depend on <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> be given by (<a href="#S4.E8" title="In 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) so that <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}_{\beta}\sim\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}_{\beta}\sim\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and write <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}\equiv a_{k}^{(\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}\equiv a_{k}^{(\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\ell,\gamma}\equiv b_{\ell,\gamma}^{(\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≡</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\ell,\gamma}\equiv b_{\ell,\gamma}^{(\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math> where the random variables <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{k}^{(\beta)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{k}^{(\beta)})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b_{\ell,\gamma}^{(\beta)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b_{\ell,\gamma}^{(\beta)})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the conditions below (<a href="#S4.E8" title="In 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). By (<a href="#A4.E32" title="In D.2 Wavelets ‣ Appendix D Function spaces and wavelets ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E33" title="In D.2 Wavelets ‣ Appendix D Function spaces and wavelets ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>), writing <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\coloneqq\bigl\lceil\frac{\log_{2}n}{2\beta+d}\bigr\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\coloneqq\bigl\lceil\frac{\log_{2}n}{2\beta+d}\bigr\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> (and assuming for now that <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\geq\ell_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\geq\ell_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx124" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex122.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C_{1}\max_{k\in K}|a_{k}-a^{\circ}_{k}|+C_{1}\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}2^{-\ell\beta}\max_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}|b_{\ell,\gamma}-b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ}|+2C_{0}C_{1}\sum_{\ell=L+1}^{\infty}2^{-\ell\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C_{1}\max_{k\in K}|a_{k}-a^{\circ}_{k}|+C_{1}\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}2^{-\ell\beta}\max_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}|b_{\ell,\gamma}-b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ}|+2C_{0}C_{1}\sum_{\ell=L+1}^{\infty}2^{-\ell\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C_{1}\max_{k\in K}|a_{k}-a^{\circ}_{k}|+C_{1}\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}2^{-\ell\beta}\max_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}|b_{\ell,\gamma}-b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ}|+C_{3}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C_{1}\max_{k\in K}|a_{k}-a^{\circ}_{k}|+C_{1}\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}2^{-\ell\beta}\max_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}|b_{\ell,\gamma}-b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ}|+C_{3}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Define the events</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx125" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex123.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\bigcap_{k\in K}\Bigl\{|a_{k}-a^{\circ}_{k}|\leq 2\cdot n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}\Bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\bigcap_{k\in K}\Bigl\{|a_{k}-a^{\circ}_{k}|\leq 2\cdot n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}\Bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex124.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\bigcap_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}\bigcap_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}\Bigl\{|b_{\ell,\gamma}-b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ}|\leq 2\cdot 2^{-2(L-\ell)\beta}\Bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\bigcap_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}\bigcap_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}\Bigl\{|b_{\ell,\gamma}-b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ}|\leq 2\cdot 2^{-2(L-\ell)\beta}\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then, on the event <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have by (<a href="#A6.E45" title="In Proof. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx126" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex125.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2C_{1}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}+2C_{1}2^{-L\beta}\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}2^{-(L-\ell)\beta}+C_{3}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}\leq C_{4}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2C_{1}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}+2C_{1}2^{-L\beta}\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}2^{-(L-\ell)\beta}+C_{3}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}\leq C_{4}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx127" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{4}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{4}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2})=\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{1})\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{1}\cap\mathcal{E}_{2})=\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{1})\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Now, by (<a href="#A4.E31" title="In D.2 Wavelets ‣ Appendix D Function spaces and wavelets ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx128" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{1})\geq\bigl(c_{0}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}\bigr)^{2^{\ell_{0}d}}=\exp(-C_{5}\log n)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{1})\geq\bigl(c_{0}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}\bigr)^{2^{\ell_{0}d}}=\exp(-C_{5}\log n).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx129" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{2})&gt;\prod_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}\bigl(c_{0}2^{-2(L-\ell)\beta}\bigr)^{2^{(\ell+1)d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{2})&gt;\prod_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}\bigl(c_{0}2^{-2(L-\ell)\beta}\bigr)^{2^{(\ell+1)d}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex126.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp\biggl((\log c_{0})\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}2^{(\ell+1)d}-(2^{d+1}\log 2)\beta\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}(L-\ell)2^{\ell d}\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp\biggl((\log c_{0})\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}2^{(\ell+1)d}-(2^{d+1}\log 2)\beta\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}(L-\ell)2^{\ell d}\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\exp(-C_{6}n^{d/(2\beta+d)})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\exp(-C_{6}n^{d/(2\beta+d)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">where the final inequality follows since if we set <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\coloneqq\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}(L-\ell)2^{\ell d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\coloneqq\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{L}(L-\ell)2^{\ell d}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{d}A-A\leq\sum_{\ell=0}^{L}2^{\ell d}\leq 2^{(L+1)d}/(2^{d}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{d}A-A\leq\sum_{\ell=0}^{L}2^{\ell d}\leq 2^{(L+1)d}/(2^{d}-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\leq 2^{(L+1)d}/(2^{d}-1)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\leq 2^{(L+1)d}/(2^{d}-1)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The conclusion (<a href="#A6.E43" title="In Lemma 18. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) for <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> large enough that <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\geq\ell_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\geq\ell_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> follows from (<a href="#A6.E46" title="In Proof. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>), (<a href="#A6.E47" title="In Proof. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>) and (<a href="#A6.E48" title="In Proof. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>). By increasing <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, depending only on <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,d,c_{0},C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,d,c_{0},C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, we can then ensure that (<a href="#A6.E43" title="In Lemma 18. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) holds for all <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (<a href="#A6.E44" title="In Lemma 18. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>), note that by Lemma <a href="#Thmthm24" title="Lemma 24. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a><em id="A6.SS1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(a)</em> and <em id="A6.SS1.p3.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(b)</em>, we have that if <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}^{2}\leq Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}^{2}\leq Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx130" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(P_{g^{\circ}},P_{g})\leq C_{1}^{\prime}Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}\quad\text{and}\quad\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{g^{\circ}},P_{g})\leq C_{1}^{\prime}Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mtext>and</mtext><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(P_{g^{\circ}},P_{g})\leq C_{1}^{\prime}Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}\quad\text{and}\quad\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{g^{\circ}},P_{g})\leq C_{1}^{\prime}Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Writing <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\epsilon_{n,\beta}\coloneqq\sqrt{C_{1}^{\prime}C}\cdot n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{n,\beta}\coloneqq\sqrt{C_{1}^{\prime}C}\cdot n^{-\beta/(2\beta+d)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we deduce from (<a href="#A6.E43" title="In Lemma 18. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx131" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\beta}\bigl(B_{\beta}(P_{g^{\circ}},\epsilon_{n,\beta})\bigr)\geq\exp\bigl(-Cn^{d/(2\beta+d)}\bigr)\geq\exp(-C_{2}^{\prime}n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\beta}\bigl(B_{\beta}(P_{g^{\circ}},\epsilon_{n,\beta})\bigr)\geq\exp\bigl(-Cn^{d/(2\beta+d)}\bigr)\geq\exp(-C_{2}^{\prime}n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus (<a href="#A6.E44" title="In Lemma 18. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>) holds with <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}\coloneqq\sqrt{C_{1}^{\prime}C}\vee C_{2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>∨</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}\coloneqq\sqrt{C_{1}^{\prime}C}\vee C_{2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#Thmthm19" title="Lemma 19. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> below provides an upper bound on the prior mass.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 19</span></span><span id="Thmthm19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and assume that (<a href="#A6.E42" title="In F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) holds. Suppose that <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Borel distribution on <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with the property that there exist <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and a hypercube <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq[0,1]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq[0,1]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of side length <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}(A_{0})\geq c_{0}\mathrm{Vol}_{d}(A_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Vol</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}(A_{0})\geq c_{0}\mathrm{Vol}_{d}(A_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> for all measurable <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}\subseteq A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}\subseteq A</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exist <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\equiv c(\alpha,d,c_{0},C_{0},\tau)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\equiv c(\alpha,d,c_{0},C_{0},\tau)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{0}\equiv n_{0}(\alpha,d,c_{0},C_{0},S,m,\tau)\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{0}\equiv n_{0}(\alpha,d,c_{0},C_{0},S,m,\tau)\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx132" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}\Bigl(\Bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq\frac{c_{0}}{4}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+d)}\Bigr\}\Bigr)\leq\exp\bigl(-cm^{-d/\alpha}n^{d/(2\alpha+d)}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}\Bigl(\Bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq\frac{c_{0}}{4}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+d)}\Bigr\}\Bigr)\leq\exp\bigl(-cm^{-d/\alpha}n^{d/(2\alpha+d)}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm19.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm19.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq n_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq n_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, there exists <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, depending only on <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta,d,c_{0},C_{0},S,\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta,d,c_{0},C_{0},S,\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq n_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq n_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx133" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\alpha}\bigl(B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{g^{\circ}},c^{\prime}mn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+d)})\bigr)\leq\exp\bigl(-cm^{-d/\alpha}n^{d/(2\alpha+d)}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\alpha}\bigl(B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{g^{\circ}},c^{\prime}mn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+d)})\bigr)\leq\exp\bigl(-cm^{-d/\alpha}n^{d/(2\alpha+d)}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm19.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm19.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmthm19.p1.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{g^{\circ}},c^{\prime}mn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+d)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{g^{\circ}},c^{\prime}mn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+d)})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as in (<a href="#A5.E38" title="In E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout the proof, <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> will denote positive quantities that may depend only on <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,d,c_{0},C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,d,c_{0},C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}^{\prime},C_{2}^{\prime},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}^{\prime},C_{2}^{\prime},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> may depend in addition on <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\epsilon\coloneqq n^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\coloneqq n^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+d)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g^{\prime}-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq\frac{c_{0}}{4}m^{2}\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g^{\prime}-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq\frac{c_{0}}{4}m^{2}\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; we may assume without loss of generality that such a <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> exists, since otherwise the left-hand side of (<a href="#A6.E49" title="In Lemma 19. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>) would be zero. Suppose that <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has wavelet decomposition</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx134" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle g^{\prime}=\sum_{k\in K}C_{0}2^{-\ell_{0}d/2}a_{k}^{\prime}\Phi_{k}+\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}C_{0}2^{-\ell(\alpha+d/2)}b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\prime}\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g^{\prime}=\sum_{k\in K}C_{0}2^{-\ell_{0}d/2}a_{k}^{\prime}\Phi_{k}+\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}C_{0}2^{-\ell(\alpha+d/2)}b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\prime}\Psi_{\ell,\gamma},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a_{k}^{\prime}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a_{k}^{\prime}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\prime}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\prime}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that if <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq\frac{c_{0}}{4}m^{2}\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq\frac{c_{0}}{4}m^{2}\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g-g^{\prime}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq 2\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}+2\|g^{\prime}-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}m^{2}\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g-g^{\prime}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq 2\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}+2\|g^{\prime}-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}m^{2}\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx135" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}\Bigl(\Bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}:\|g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}\Bigl(\Bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}:\|g</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E51.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq\frac{c_{0}}{4}m^{2}\epsilon^{2}\Bigr\}\Bigr)\leq\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}\Bigl(\Bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}:\|g-g^{\prime}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}m^{2}\epsilon^{2}\Bigr\}\Bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq\frac{c_{0}}{4}m^{2}\epsilon^{2}\Bigr\}\Bigr)\leq\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}\Bigl(\Bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}:\|g-g^{\prime}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}m^{2}\epsilon^{2}\Bigr\}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}\sim\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}\sim\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, and write <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}\equiv a_{k}^{(\alpha)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}\equiv a_{k}^{(\alpha)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\ell,\gamma}\equiv b_{\ell,\gamma}^{(\alpha)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≡</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\ell,\gamma}\equiv b_{\ell,\gamma}^{(\alpha)}</annotation></semantics></math> with representation (<a href="#S4.E8" title="In 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), where the random variables <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{k}^{(\alpha)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{k}^{(\alpha)})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b_{\ell,\gamma}^{(\alpha)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b_{\ell,\gamma}^{(\alpha)})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the conditions below (<a href="#S4.E8" title="In 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). Further, let <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}\coloneqq\lceil\log_{2}(2/\tau)\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}\coloneqq\lceil\log_{2}(2/\tau)\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by the assumption on <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m24" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C_{2}\in[0:2^{C_{1}}-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}\in[0:2^{C_{1}}-1]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl[\frac{C_{2}}{2^{C_{1}}},\frac{C_{2}+1}{2^{C_{1}}}\bigr]^{d}\subseteq A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl[\frac{C_{2}}{2^{C_{1}}},\frac{C_{2}+1}{2^{C_{1}}}\bigr]^{d}\subseteq A</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{0}\equiv n_{0}(\alpha,d,c_{0},C_{0},S,m,\tau)\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{0}\equiv n_{0}(\alpha,d,c_{0},C_{0},S,m,\tau)\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> large enough that <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\coloneqq\bigl\lfloor\frac{1}{2\alpha}\log_{2}\bigl(\frac{c_{0}C_{0}^{2}}{6m^{2}\epsilon^{2}2^{C_{1}d}}\bigr)\bigr\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\coloneqq\bigl\lfloor\frac{1}{2\alpha}\log_{2}\bigl(\frac{c_{0}C_{0}^{2}}{6m^{2}\epsilon^{2}2^{C_{1}d}}\bigr)\bigr\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> is at least <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{0}\vee C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{0}\vee C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq n_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq n_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume henceforth that <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq n_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq n_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{L}^{\prime}\coloneqq\bigl\{\gamma\in\Gamma_{L}:\mathrm{supp}(\Psi_{L,\gamma})\subseteq\bigl[\frac{C_{2}}{2^{C_{1}}},\frac{C_{2}+1}{2^{C_{1}}}\bigr]^{d}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{L}^{\prime}\coloneqq\bigl\{\gamma\in\Gamma_{L}:\mathrm{supp}(\Psi_{L,\gamma})\subseteq\bigl[\frac{C_{2}}{2^{C_{1}}},\frac{C_{2}+1}{2^{C_{1}}}\bigr]^{d}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{L}\coloneqq(b_{L,\gamma})_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{L}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{L}\coloneqq(b_{L,\gamma})_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{L}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{L}^{\prime}\coloneqq(b_{L,\gamma}^{\prime})_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{L}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{L}^{\prime}\coloneqq(b_{L,\gamma}^{\prime})_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{L}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(\Psi_{L,\gamma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(\Psi_{L,\gamma})</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in a dyadic cube of side length <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{-L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{-L}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Section <a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 Wavelets ‣ Appendix D Function spaces and wavelets ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>), we deduce that <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Gamma_{L}^{\prime}|\geq 2^{(L-C_{1})d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Gamma_{L}^{\prime}|\geq 2^{(L-C_{1})d}</annotation></semantics></math> and that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx136" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{0}^{2}2^{-L(2\alpha+d)}\mathbb{E}\bigl(\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{0}^{2}2^{-L(2\alpha+d)}\mathbb{E}\bigl(\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex130.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq C_{0}^{2}2^{-L(2\alpha+d)}\mathrm{tr}\bigl(\mathrm{Cov}(b_{L})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq C_{0}^{2}2^{-L(2\alpha+d)}\mathrm{tr}\bigl(\mathrm{Cov}(b_{L})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq|\Gamma_{L}^{\prime}|C_{0}^{2}2^{-L(2\alpha+d)}\cdot\frac{c_{0}}{3}\geq\frac{c_{0}C_{0}^{2}2^{-2\alpha L-C_{1}d}}{3}\geq 2m^{2}\epsilon^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq|\Gamma_{L}^{\prime}|C_{0}^{2}2^{-L(2\alpha+d)}\cdot\frac{c_{0}}{3}\geq\frac{c_{0}C_{0}^{2}2^{-2\alpha L-C_{1}d}}{3}\geq 2m^{2}\epsilon^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by the assumption on <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and Lemma <a href="#Thmthm25" title="Lemma 25. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx137" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}-g^{\prime}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}-g^{\prime}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex132.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m^{2}\epsilon^{2}\bigr)\leq\mathbb{P}\bigl(c_{0}\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}-g^{\prime}\|_{L^{2}([C_{2}2^{-C_{1}},(C_{2}+1)2^{-C_{1}}]^{d})}^{2}\leq c_{0}m^{2}\epsilon^{2}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m^{2}\epsilon^{2}\bigr)\leq\mathbb{P}\bigl(c_{0}\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}-g^{\prime}\|_{L^{2}([C_{2}2^{-C_{1}},(C_{2}+1)2^{-C_{1}}]^{d})}^{2}\leq c_{0}m^{2}\epsilon^{2}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}-\mathbb{E}\bigl(\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr)\leq\frac{m^{2}\epsilon^{2}}{C_{0}^{2}2^{-L(2\alpha+d)}}-\mathbb{E}\bigl(\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr)\biggr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}-\mathbb{E}\bigl(\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr)\leq\frac{m^{2}\epsilon^{2}}{C_{0}^{2}2^{-L(2\alpha+d)}}-\mathbb{E}\bigl(\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr)\biggr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}-\mathbb{E}\bigl(\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr)\leq-\frac{m^{2}\epsilon^{2}}{C_{0}^{2}2^{-L(2\alpha+d)}}\biggr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}-\mathbb{E}\bigl(\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr)\leq-\frac{m^{2}\epsilon^{2}}{C_{0}^{2}2^{-L(2\alpha+d)}}\biggr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b_{L,\gamma}-b_{L,\gamma}^{\prime})^{2}\in[0,4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b_{L,\gamma}-b_{L,\gamma}^{\prime})^{2}\in[0,4]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\Gamma_{L}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\Gamma_{L}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have by Hoeffding’s inequality and (<a href="#A4.E31" title="In D.2 Wavelets ‣ Appendix D Function spaces and wavelets ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx138" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\|b_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\|b_{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex134.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}-\mathbb{E}\bigl(\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr)\leq-\frac{m^{2}\epsilon^{2}}{C_{0}^{2}2^{-L(2\alpha+d)}}\biggr\}\leq\exp\biggl(-\frac{m^{4}\epsilon^{4}}{8C_{0}^{4}2^{-(4\alpha+d)L-C_{1}d}}\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}-\mathbb{E}\bigl(\|b_{L}-b_{L}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr)\leq-\frac{m^{2}\epsilon^{2}}{C_{0}^{2}2^{-L(2\alpha+d)}}\biggr\}\leq\exp\biggl(-\frac{m^{4}\epsilon^{4}}{8C_{0}^{4}2^{-(4\alpha+d)L-C_{1}d}}\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\biggl\{-\frac{c_{0}^{2}}{288\cdot 2^{4\alpha+(C_{1}+1)d}}\biggl(\frac{c_{0}C_{0}^{2}}{6m^{2}\epsilon^{2}2^{C_{1}d}}\biggr)^{d/(2\alpha)}\biggr\}\eqqcolon\exp\bigl(-cm^{-d/\alpha}n^{d/(2\alpha+d)}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>288</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≕</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\biggl\{-\frac{c_{0}^{2}}{288\cdot 2^{4\alpha+(C_{1}+1)d}}\biggl(\frac{c_{0}C_{0}^{2}}{6m^{2}\epsilon^{2}2^{C_{1}d}}\biggr)^{d/(2\alpha)}\biggr\}\eqqcolon\exp\bigl(-cm^{-d/\alpha}n^{d/(2\alpha+d)}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,d,c_{0},C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,d,c_{0},C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining (<a href="#A6.E51" title="In Proof. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>), (<a href="#A6.E52" title="In Proof. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) and (<a href="#A6.E53" title="In Proof. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>) yields (<a href="#A6.E49" title="In Lemma 19. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the second claim, note that by (<a href="#A4.E32" title="In D.2 Wavelets ‣ Appendix D Function spaces and wavelets ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E33" title="In D.2 Wavelets ‣ Appendix D Function spaces and wavelets ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx139" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{3}\max_{k\in K}|a_{k}^{\circ}|+C_{3}\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}2^{-\ell\beta}\max_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}|b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ}|\leq C_{1}^{\prime}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{3}\max_{k\in K}|a_{k}^{\circ}|+C_{3}\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}2^{-\ell\beta}\max_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}|b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ}|\leq C_{1}^{\prime},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">and similarly, <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely. Thus, if <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{\mathrm{H}}(P_{g^{\circ}},P_{g})\leq c^{\prime}mn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{H}}(P_{g^{\circ}},P_{g})\leq c^{\prime}mn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+d)}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then by Lemma <a href="#Thmthm24" title="Lemma 24. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a><em id="A6.SS1.p6.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(d)</em>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx140" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq C_{3}^{\prime}d_{\mathrm{H}}^{2}(P_{g^{\circ}},P_{g})\leq C_{3}^{\prime}(c^{\prime})^{2}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+d)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq C_{3}^{\prime}d_{\mathrm{H}}^{2}(P_{g^{\circ}},P_{g})\leq C_{3}^{\prime}(c^{\prime})^{2}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+d)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, taking <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}\coloneqq\sqrt{c_{0}/(4C_{3}^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}\coloneqq\sqrt{c_{0}/(4C_{3}^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math> and applying (<a href="#A6.E49" title="In Lemma 19. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>) proves (<a href="#A6.E50" title="In Lemma 19. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We are now in a position to prove Proposition <a href="#Thmthm4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout the proof, <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> will denote positive quantities that do not depend on <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. By an argument similar to (<a href="#A6.E54" title="In Proof. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>), there exists <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g\|_{\infty}\leq C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g\|_{\infty}\leq C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We now verify the assumptions of Corollary <a href="#Thmthm17" title="Corollary 17. ‣ E.2 Bayesian nonparametric regression ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> with <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=1</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (which does not depend on <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>) be the quantity in Lemma <a href="#Thmthm18" title="Lemma 18. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> such that (<a href="#A6.E44" title="In Lemma 18. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>) holds, and let <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\epsilon_{n,\alpha}\coloneqq C^{\prime}n^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{n,\alpha}\coloneqq C^{\prime}n^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+d)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by Lemma <a href="#Thmthm18" title="Lemma 18. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, condition <a href="#A5.I1.i2" title="item (C2) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C2)</span></a> holds with <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#Thmthm24" title="Lemma 24. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a><em id="A6.SS1.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(d)</em>, (<a href="#S4.E9" title="In 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Giné and Nickl (2021, Eq. (4.184))</a></cite>, for each <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx141" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{\epsilon\geq\epsilon_{n,\alpha}}\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\epsilon/3,\,B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{0},2\epsilon),\,d_{\mathrm{H}}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{\epsilon\geq\epsilon_{n,\alpha}}\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\epsilon/3,\,B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{0},2\epsilon),\,d_{\mathrm{H}}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex136.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\epsilon_{n,\alpha}/3,\,\mathcal{P}_{\alpha},\,d_{\mathrm{H}}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\epsilon_{n,\alpha}/3,\,\mathcal{P}_{\alpha},\,d_{\mathrm{H}}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(2\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha}/3,\,\mathcal{G}_{\alpha},\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>log</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.059em">,</mo><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(2\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha}/3,\,\mathcal{G}_{\alpha},\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(2\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha}/3,\,B^{\alpha}_{\infty,\infty}([0,1]^{d},2C_{0}),\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>log</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.059em">,</mo><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(2\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha}/3,\,B^{\alpha}_{\infty,\infty}([0,1]^{d},2C_{0}),\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq E_{\alpha}n\epsilon_{n,\alpha}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq E_{\alpha}n\epsilon_{n,\alpha}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">for some <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> not depending on <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>; this verifies condition <a href="#A5.I1.i1" title="item (C1) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C1)</span></a>. Moreover, since <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, condition <a href="#A5.I1.i3" title="item (C3) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C3)</span></a> is satisfied with <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{n,\alpha}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{n,\alpha}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large. Similarly, condition <a href="#A5.I1.i5" title="item (C5) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C5)</span></a> is satisfied for some <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> not depending on <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, take <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{2}&gt;243(F+1)(HE+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>243</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{2}&gt;243(F+1)(HE+1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Letting <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,c^{\prime}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,c^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be the quantities in Lemma <a href="#Thmthm19" title="Lemma 19. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> and applying Lemma <a href="#Thmthm19" title="Lemma 19. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> with <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\coloneqq MC^{\prime}/c^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\coloneqq MC^{\prime}/c^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we deduce that for <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx142" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}}\frac{\lambda_{\alpha}}{\lambda_{\beta}}\cdot\pi_{\alpha}\bigl(B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{0},M\epsilon_{n,\alpha})\bigr)\leq\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}:\alpha&lt;\beta}\frac{\lambda_{\alpha}}{\lambda_{\beta}}\cdot\exp\bigl(-cm^{-d/\alpha}n^{d/(2\alpha+d)}\bigr)\leq e^{-(F+3)n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}_{&lt;\beta}}\frac{\lambda_{\alpha}}{\lambda_{\beta}}\cdot\pi_{\alpha}\bigl(B^{\prime}_{\alpha}(P_{0},M\epsilon_{n,\alpha})\bigr)\leq\sum_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}:\alpha&lt;\beta}\frac{\lambda_{\alpha}}{\lambda_{\beta}}\cdot\exp\bigl(-cm^{-d/\alpha}n^{d/(2\alpha+d)}\bigr)\leq e^{-(F+3)n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">which verifies condition <a href="#A5.I1.i4" title="item (C4) ‣ E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(C4)</span></a>. Therefore, by Corollary <a href="#Thmthm17" title="Corollary 17. ‣ E.2 Bayesian nonparametric regression ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, the claim follows for sufficiently large <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-c_{3}n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}\leq\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-c_{3}n\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}}\leq\epsilon_{n,\beta}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> large enough. Moreover, since <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded, the conclusion now follows for all <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> by increasing <math id="A6.SS1.p8.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> in the statement if necessary.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm6" title="Proposition 6. ‣ 4.2 In-context learning for multi-index models ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We work in the setting of Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 In-context learning for multi-index models ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. For <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,p)\in\mathcal{A}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,p)\in\mathcal{A}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}</annotation></semantics></math> similarly to the definition of <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> in Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> but replacing the dimensionality <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. we let <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of all functions <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\alpha}^{(p)}:[0,1]^{p}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\alpha}^{(p)}:[0,1]^{p}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> has wavelet decomposition</p>
<table id="A6.EGx143" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle h_{\alpha}^{(p)}=\sum_{k\in K}C_{0}2^{-\ell_{0}r/2}a_{k}\Phi_{k}^{(p)}+\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}C_{0}2^{-\ell(\beta+r/2)}b_{\ell,\gamma}\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}^{(p)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{\alpha}^{(p)}=\sum_{k\in K}C_{0}2^{-\ell_{0}r/2}a_{k}\Phi_{k}^{(p)}+\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}C_{0}2^{-\ell(\beta+r/2)}b_{\ell,\gamma}\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}^{(p)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Phi_{k}^{(p)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Phi_{k}^{(p)})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}^{(p)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}^{(p)})</annotation></semantics></math> is the tensor product CDV wavelet basis for <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}([0,1]^{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}([0,1]^{p})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a_{k}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a_{k}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|b_{\ell,\gamma}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|b_{\ell,\gamma}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, similarly to (<a href="#S4.E9" title="In 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A6.EGx144" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{p},C_{0})\subseteq\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\subseteq B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{p},2C_{0})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{p},C_{0})\subseteq\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\subseteq B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{p},2C_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm6" title="Proposition 6. ‣ 4.2 In-context learning for multi-index models ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> relies on three preliminary lemmas that we now formulate. We may write</p>
<table id="A6.EGx145" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g^{\circ}(x)=h^{\circ}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\biggr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g^{\circ}(x)=h^{\circ}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\biggr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\circ}\in V_{r}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\circ}\in V_{r}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\circ}\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\circ}\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math> has wavelet decomposition</p>
<table id="A6.EGx146" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E56.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle h^{\circ}=\sum_{k\in K}C_{0}2^{-\ell_{0}r/2}a_{k}^{\circ}\Phi_{k}^{(r)}+\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}C_{0}2^{-\ell(\beta+r/2)}b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ}\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}^{(r)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h^{\circ}=\sum_{k\in K}C_{0}2^{-\ell_{0}r/2}a_{k}^{\circ}\Phi_{k}^{(r)}+\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}C_{0}2^{-\ell(\beta+r/2)}b_{\ell,\gamma}^{\circ}\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}^{(r)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a^{\circ}_{k}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a^{\circ}_{k}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|b^{\circ}_{\ell,\gamma}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|b^{\circ}_{\ell,\gamma}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 20</span></span><span id="Thmthm20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm20.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and assume that (<a href="#A6.E55" title="In F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a>) and (<a href="#A6.E56" title="In F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) hold. Then there exists <math id="Thmthm20.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, depending only on <math id="Thmthm20.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,d,r,c_{0},C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,d,r,c_{0},C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm20.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx147" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta,r}\bigl(\bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}^{2}\leq Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}\bigr\}\bigr)\geq\exp\bigl(-Cn^{r/(2\beta+r)}\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta,r}\bigl(\bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}^{2}\leq Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}\bigr\}\bigr)\geq\exp\bigl(-Cn^{r/(2\beta+r)}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm20.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm20.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, there exists <math id="Thmthm20.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, depending only on <math id="Thmthm20.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,d,r,c_{0},C_{0},S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,d,r,c_{0},C_{0},S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm20.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, such that if <math id="Thmthm20.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\epsilon_{n,\beta,r}\coloneqq C^{\prime}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{n,\beta,r}\coloneqq C^{\prime}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx148" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\beta,r}\bigl(B_{\beta,r}(P_{g^{\circ}},\epsilon_{n,\beta,r})\bigr)\geq\exp\bigl(-C^{\prime}n\epsilon_{n,\beta,r}^{2}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\beta,r}\bigl(B_{\beta,r}(P_{g^{\circ}},\epsilon_{n,\beta,r})\bigr)\geq\exp\bigl(-C^{\prime}n\epsilon_{n,\beta,r}^{2}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm20.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm20.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmthm20.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{\beta,r}(P_{g^{\circ}},\epsilon_{n,\beta,r})\coloneqq\bigl\{P\in\mathcal{P}_{\beta,r}:\mathrm{KL}(P_{g^{\circ}},P)\leq\epsilon_{n,\beta,r}^{2},\,\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{g^{\circ}},P)\leq\epsilon_{n,\beta,r}^{2}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\beta,r}(P_{g^{\circ}},\epsilon_{n,\beta,r})\coloneqq\bigl\{P\in\mathcal{P}_{\beta,r}:\mathrm{KL}(P_{g^{\circ}},P)\leq\epsilon_{n,\beta,r}^{2},\,\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{g^{\circ}},P)\leq\epsilon_{n,\beta,r}^{2}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math>, similarly to (<a href="#A5.E37" title="In E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout the proof, <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> will denote positive quantities that may depend only on <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,d,r,c_{0},C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,d,r,c_{0},C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}^{\prime},C_{2}^{\prime},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}^{\prime},C_{2}^{\prime},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> may in addition depend on <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}_{\beta,r}(x)=\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}\bigl(\frac{(U^{(r)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}_{\beta,r}(x)=\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}\bigl(\frac{(U^{(r)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in (<a href="#S4.E11" title="In 4.2 In-context learning for multi-index models ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) so that <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}_{\beta,r}\sim\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}_{\beta,r}\sim\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta,r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe that <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta}([0,1]^{r},2C_{0})\subseteq B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta\wedge 1}([0,1]^{r},2C_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta}([0,1]^{r},2C_{0})\subseteq B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta\wedge 1}([0,1]^{r},2C_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(e.g. <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Giné and Nickl, 2021</a>, Proposition 4.3.10(ii))</cite>. When <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the space <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta\wedge 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta\wedge 1}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the Hölder space <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> with equivalent norms <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(e.g. <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Giné and Nickl, 2021</a>, Proposition 4.3.23)</cite>, so for all <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in[0,1]^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in[0,1]^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta\wedge 1}([0,1]^{r},2C_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta\wedge 1}([0,1]^{r},2C_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|g(x)-g(y)|\leq C_{1}\|x-y\|_{2}^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|g(x)-g(y)|\leq C_{1}\|x-y\|_{2}^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>; when <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta\wedge 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta\wedge 1}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the Zygmund space of order <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> with equivalent norms <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Triebel, 1983</a>, p. 113)</cite>, so by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anderson and Pitt (1989, Proposition 2.4)</a></cite> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(see also <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zygmund, 2002</a>, Chapter II, Theorem 3.4)</cite>, for all <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in[0,1]^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in[0,1]^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta\wedge 1}([0,1]^{r},2C_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta\wedge 1}([0,1]^{r},2C_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|g(x)-g(y)|\leq C_{2}\|x-y\|_{2}\bigl\{\log(1/\|x-y\|_{2})\vee 1\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|g(x)-g(y)|\leq C_{2}\|x-y\|_{2}\bigl\{\log(1/\|x-y\|_{2})\vee 1\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, for all <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in[0,1]^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in[0,1]^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta}([0,1]^{r},2C_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta}([0,1]^{r},2C_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx149" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|g(x)-g(y)|\leq C_{3}\|x-y\|_{2}^{\beta\wedge 1}\bigl\{\log(1/\|x-y\|_{2})\vee 1\bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|g(x)-g(y)|\leq C_{3}\|x-y\|_{2}^{\beta\wedge 1}\bigl\{\log(1/\|x-y\|_{2})\vee 1\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">On the event <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E\coloneqq\bigl\{\|U^{(r)}-U^{\circ}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\bigl(n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}/\log(en)\bigr)^{1/(\beta\wedge 1)}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\coloneqq\bigl\{\|U^{(r)}-U^{\circ}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\bigl(n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}/\log(en)\bigr)^{1/(\beta\wedge 1)}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have for all <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{B}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{B}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx150" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\widetilde{g}_{\beta,r}(x)-g^{\circ}(x)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\widetilde{g}_{\beta,r}(x)-g^{\circ}(x)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex144"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\biggl|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{(r)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\biggr)-\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\biggr)\biggr|+\biggl|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\biggr)-h^{\circ}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\biggr)\biggr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\biggl|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{(r)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\biggr)-\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\biggr)\biggr|+\biggl|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\biggr)-h^{\circ}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\biggr)\biggr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E60.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C_{4}n^{-\beta/\{(2\beta+r)\}}+\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}-h^{\circ}\|_{\infty}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C_{4}n^{-\beta/\{(2\beta+r)\}}+\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}-h^{\circ}\|_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the second inequality follows from (<a href="#A6.E59" title="In Proof. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>), since <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}^{(r)}\subseteq B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta}([0,1]^{r},2C_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}^{(r)}\subseteq B_{\infty,\infty}^{\beta}([0,1]^{r},2C_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m26" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bigl\|\frac{(U^{(r)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}-\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\bigr\|_{2}\leq\frac{1}{2}\bigl(n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}/\log(en)\bigr)^{1/(\beta\wedge 1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\|\frac{(U^{(r)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}-\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{r}}{2}\bigr\|_{2}\leq\frac{1}{2}\bigl(n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}/\log(en)\bigr)^{1/(\beta\wedge 1)}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. Now by Lemma <a href="#Thmthm26" title="Lemma 26. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx151" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E)\geq C_{5}\biggl(\frac{n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}}{\log(en)}\wedge\frac{1}{2}\biggr)^{dr/(\beta\wedge 1)}\geq\exp(-C_{6}n^{r/(2\beta+r)})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>∧</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(E)\geq C_{5}\biggl(\frac{n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}}{\log(en)}\wedge\frac{1}{2}\biggr)^{dr/(\beta\wedge 1)}\geq\exp(-C_{6}n^{r/(2\beta+r)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">and by (<a href="#A6.E43" title="In Lemma 18. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) (with <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> therein), we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx152" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex146"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}-h^{\circ}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{7}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}\bigr)\geq\exp(-C_{7}n^{r/(2\beta+r)})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}-h^{\circ}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{7}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}\bigr)\geq\exp(-C_{7}n^{r/(2\beta+r)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx153" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta,r}-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta,r}-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex147.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(C_{4}+C_{7})^{2}n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(C_{4}+C_{7})^{2}n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex148"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta,r}-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}\leq(C_{4}+C_{7})n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}\,\big|\,E\bigr)\mathbb{P}(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta,r}-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}\leq(C_{4}+C_{7})n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}\,\big|\,E\bigr)\mathbb{P}(E)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex149"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}-h^{\circ}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{7}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}\bigr)\mathbb{P}(E)\geq\exp\bigl\{-(C_{6}+C_{7})n^{r/(2\beta+r)}\bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}-h^{\circ}\|_{\infty}\leq C_{7}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}\bigr)\mathbb{P}(E)\geq\exp\bigl\{-(C_{6}+C_{7})n^{r/(2\beta+r)}\bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the second inequality follows from (<a href="#A6.E60" title="In Proof. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>) and the fact that <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}_{\beta}^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent. This proves (<a href="#A6.E57" title="In Lemma 20. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">57</span></a>) with <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\coloneqq(C_{4}+C_{7})^{2}\vee(C_{6}+C_{7})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\coloneqq(C_{4}+C_{7})^{2}\vee(C_{6}+C_{7})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of (<a href="#A6.E58" title="In Lemma 20. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>) follows the same argument as the proof of (<a href="#A6.E44" title="In Lemma 18. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>). By Lemma <a href="#Thmthm24" title="Lemma 24. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a><em id="A6.SS2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(a)</em> and <em id="A6.SS2.p3.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(b)</em>, if <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}^{2}\leq Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{\infty}^{2}\leq Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx154" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex150"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(P_{g^{\circ}},P_{g})\leq C_{1}^{\prime}Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}\quad\text{and}\quad\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{g^{\circ}},P_{g})\leq C_{2}^{\prime}Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mtext>and</mtext><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(P_{g^{\circ}},P_{g})\leq C_{1}^{\prime}Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}\quad\text{and}\quad\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{g^{\circ}},P_{g})\leq C_{2}^{\prime}Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Writing <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}\coloneqq C^{1/3}\vee\sqrt{(C_{1}^{\prime}\vee C_{2}^{\prime})C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∨</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∨</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}\coloneqq C^{1/3}\vee\sqrt{(C_{1}^{\prime}\vee C_{2}^{\prime})C}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\epsilon_{n,\beta,r}\coloneqq C^{\prime}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{n,\beta,r}\coloneqq C^{\prime}n^{-\beta/(2\beta+r)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we deduce from (<a href="#A6.E57" title="In Lemma 20. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">57</span></a>) that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx155" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex151"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\beta,r}\bigl(B_{\beta,r}(P_{g^{\circ}},\epsilon_{n,\beta,r})\bigr)\geq\exp\bigl(-Cn^{r/(2\beta+r)}\bigr)\geq\exp(-C^{\prime}n\epsilon_{n,\beta,r}^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\beta,r}\bigl(B_{\beta,r}(P_{g^{\circ}},\epsilon_{n,\beta,r})\bigr)\geq\exp\bigl(-Cn^{r/(2\beta+r)}\bigr)\geq\exp(-C^{\prime}n\epsilon_{n,\beta,r}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">This proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm21" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 21</span></span><span id="Thmthm21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm21.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm21.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm21.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,p)\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,p)\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and assume that (<a href="#A6.E55" title="In F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a>) and (<a href="#A6.E56" title="In F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) hold. Suppose that <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Borel distribution on <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with the property that there exist <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and a closed Euclidean ball <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\mathbb{B}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\mathbb{B}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of radius <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}(A_{0})\geq c_{0}\mathrm{Vol}_{d}(A_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Vol</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}(A_{0})\geq c_{0}\mathrm{Vol}_{d}(A_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> for all measurable <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}\subseteq A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}\subseteq A</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exist <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}^{\prime}\equiv c_{0}^{\prime}(c_{0},\tau,d,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}^{\prime}\equiv c_{0}^{\prime}(c_{0},\tau,d,p)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\equiv c(\alpha,d,p,c_{0},C_{0},\tau)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\equiv c(\alpha,d,p,c_{0},C_{0},\tau)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{0}\equiv n_{0}(\alpha,d,p,c_{0},C_{0},S,m,\tau)\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{0}\equiv n_{0}(\alpha,d,p,c_{0},C_{0},S,m,\tau)\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx156" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha,p}\Bigl(\Bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha,p}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\Bigr\}\Bigr)\leq\exp\bigl(-cm^{-p/\alpha}n^{p/(2\alpha+p)}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha,p}\Bigl(\Bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha,p}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\Bigr\}\Bigr)\leq\exp\bigl(-cm^{-p/\alpha}n^{p/(2\alpha+p)}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm21.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm21.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq n_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq n_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, there exists <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, depending only on <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta,d,p,c_{0},C_{0},S,\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta,d,p,c_{0},C_{0},S,\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq n_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq n_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx157" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\alpha,p}\bigl(B^{\prime}_{\alpha,p}(P_{g^{\circ}},c^{\prime}mn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+p)})\bigr)\leq\exp\bigl(-cm^{-p/\alpha}n^{p/(2\alpha+p)}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\alpha,p}\bigl(B^{\prime}_{\alpha,p}(P_{g^{\circ}},c^{\prime}mn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+p)})\bigr)\leq\exp\bigl(-cm^{-p/\alpha}n^{p/(2\alpha+p)}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm21.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm21.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmthm21.p1.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B^{\prime}_{\alpha,p}(P_{g^{\circ}},c^{\prime}mn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+p)})\coloneqq\bigl\{P\in\mathcal{P}_{\alpha,p}:d_{\mathrm{H}}(P_{g^{\circ}},P)\leq c^{\prime}mn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\prime}_{\alpha,p}(P_{g^{\circ}},c^{\prime}mn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+p)})\coloneqq\bigl\{P\in\mathcal{P}_{\alpha,p}:d_{\mathrm{H}}(P_{g^{\circ}},P)\leq c^{\prime}mn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as in (<a href="#A5.E38" title="In E.1 General theory ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout the proof, <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> will denote positive quantities that may depend only on <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,d,p,c_{0},C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,d,p,c_{0},C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}^{\prime}\equiv c_{0}^{\prime}(c_{0},\tau,d,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}^{\prime}\equiv c_{0}^{\prime}(c_{0},\tau,d,p)</annotation></semantics></math> be the quantity in Lemma <a href="#Thmthm27" title="Lemma 27. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>.
Let <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}_{\alpha,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}_{\alpha,p}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in (<a href="#S4.E11" title="In 4.2 In-context learning for multi-index models ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) so that <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{g}_{\alpha,p}\sim\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{g}_{\alpha,p}\sim\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha,p}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx158" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex152"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\pi}_{\alpha,p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex152.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Bigl(\Bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha,p}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\Bigr\}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Bigl(\Bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha,p}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\Bigr\}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\biggl\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)-h^{\circ}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\biggr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\biggl\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)-h^{\circ}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\biggr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\biggl\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)-h^{\circ}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\,\bigg|\,U^{(p)}\biggr\}\biggr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\biggl[\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\biggl\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)-h^{\circ}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\,\bigg|\,U^{(p)}\biggr\}\biggr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now conditional on <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(p)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(p)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we fix <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bigl\|g^{\prime}\bigl(\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\bigr)-h^{\circ}\bigl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\bigr)\bigr\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\|g^{\prime}\bigl(\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\bigr)-h^{\circ}\bigl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\bigr)\bigr\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}</annotation></semantics></math>. We may assume without loss of generality that such <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> exists, since otherwise the conditional probability in the expectation in (<a href="#A6.E63" title="In Proof. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>) would be zero. Using the same argument as that in (<a href="#A6.E51" title="In Proof. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>), we deduce that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx159" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex154.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\biggl\{\biggl\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}x+1}{2}\biggr)-h^{\circ}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\,\bigg|\,U^{(p)}\biggr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\biggl\{\biggl\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}x+1}{2}\biggr)-h^{\circ}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\circ})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\,\bigg|\,U^{(p)}\biggr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex155"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\biggl\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)-g^{\prime}\biggl(\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq 4c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\,\bigg|\,U^{(p)}\biggr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}\biggl\{\biggl\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\biggl(\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)-g^{\prime}\biggl(\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\leq 4c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\,\bigg|\,U^{(p)}\biggr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}^{(p)}-g^{\prime}\|_{L^{2}(Q(U^{(p)}))}^{2}\leq 4c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\,\big|\,U^{(p)}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}^{(p)}-g^{\prime}\|_{L^{2}(Q(U^{(p)}))}^{2}\leq 4c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\,\big|\,U^{(p)}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(U^{(p)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(U^{(p)})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the conditional distribution of <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}X+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{(U^{(p)})^{\top}X+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(p)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(p)}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#Thmthm27" title="Lemma 27. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>, for every <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in V_{p}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in V_{p}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a hypercube <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}\subseteq[0,1]^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}\subseteq[0,1]^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> of side length <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tau}{2\sqrt{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>p</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tau}{2\sqrt{p}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(U)(A_{0}^{\prime})\geq c_{0}^{\prime}\mathrm{Vol}_{p}(A_{0}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Vol</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(U)(A_{0}^{\prime})\geq c_{0}^{\prime}\mathrm{Vol}_{p}(A_{0}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> for all measurable <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}^{\prime}\subseteq A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}^{\prime}\subseteq A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We may thus apply (<a href="#A6.E49" title="In Lemma 19. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>), with <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> therein, to deduce that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx160" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex156"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl\{\bigl\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}^{(p)}-g^{\prime}\bigr\|_{L^{2}(Q(U^{(p)}))}^{2}\leq 4c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\,\big|\,U^{(p)}\bigr\}\leq\exp\bigl(-cm^{-p/\alpha}n^{p/(2\alpha+p)}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl\{\bigl\|\widetilde{g}_{\alpha}^{(p)}-g^{\prime}\bigr\|_{L^{2}(Q(U^{(p)}))}^{2}\leq 4c_{0}^{\prime}m^{2}n^{-2\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}\,\big|\,U^{(p)}\bigr\}\leq\exp\bigl(-cm^{-p/\alpha}n^{p/(2\alpha+p)}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq n_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq n_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining this with (<a href="#A6.E63" title="In Proof. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>) and (<a href="#A6.E64" title="In Proof. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>) proves (<a href="#A6.E61" title="In Lemma 21. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, the proof of (<a href="#A6.E62" title="In Lemma 21. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>) follows a very similar argument to that in (<a href="#A6.E50" title="In Lemma 19. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm22" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 22</span></span><span id="Thmthm22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm22.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm22.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm22.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm22.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,p)\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,p)\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmthm22.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmthm22.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}\in\mathcal{P}_{\alpha,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}\in\mathcal{P}_{\alpha,p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm22.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}\coloneqq Cn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}\coloneqq Cn^{-\alpha/(2\alpha+p)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exists <math id="Thmthm22.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> depending only on <math id="Thmthm22.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,p,d,\sigma,C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,p,d,\sigma,C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm22.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx161" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex157"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{\epsilon\geq\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}}\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\epsilon/3,B_{\alpha,p}^{\prime}(P_{0},2\epsilon),d_{\mathrm{H}}\bigr)\leq C^{\prime}n\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{\epsilon\geq\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}}\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\epsilon/3,B_{\alpha,p}^{\prime}(P_{0},2\epsilon),d_{\mathrm{H}}\bigr)\leq C^{\prime}n\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout this proof, <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> will denote positive quantities depending only on <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,p,d,\sigma,C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,p,d,\sigma,C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#Thmthm24" title="Lemma 24. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a><em id="A6.SS2.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(d)</em>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx162" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex158"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{\epsilon\geq\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}}\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\epsilon/3,\,B^{\prime}_{\alpha,p}(P_{0},2\epsilon),\,d_{\mathrm{H}}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{\epsilon\geq\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}}\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\epsilon/3,\,B^{\prime}_{\alpha,p}(P_{0},2\epsilon),\,d_{\mathrm{H}}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex158.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}/3,\,\mathcal{P}_{\alpha,p},\,d_{\mathrm{H}}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}/3,\,\mathcal{P}_{\alpha,p},\,d_{\mathrm{H}}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex159"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(2\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}/3,\,\mathcal{G}_{\alpha,p},\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>log</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.059em">,</mo><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(2\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}/3,\,\mathcal{G}_{\alpha,p},\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\subseteq B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{p},2C_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\subseteq B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{p},2C_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\alpha,p}=\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\circ\bigl\{x\mapsto\frac{U^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}:U\in V_{p}(\mathbb{R}^{d})\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\alpha,p}=\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\circ\bigl\{x\mapsto\frac{U^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}:U\in V_{p}(\mathbb{R}^{d})\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now let <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}/3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}/3)</annotation></semantics></math>-cover of <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{p},2C_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{p},2C_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{N}_{1}|\leq\exp(C_{1}n\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{N}_{1}|\leq\exp(C_{1}n\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, which exists by, e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Giné and Nickl (2021, Eq. (4.184))</a></cite>. Recall from (<a href="#A6.E59" title="In Proof. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>) that for all <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in[0,1]^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in[0,1]^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx163" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|g(x)-g(y)|\leq C_{2}\|x-y\|_{2}^{\alpha\wedge 1}\bigl\{\log(1/\|x-y\|_{2})\vee 1\bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|g(x)-g(y)|\leq C_{2}\|x-y\|_{2}^{\alpha\wedge 1}\bigl\{\log(1/\|x-y\|_{2})\vee 1\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">The function <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\mapsto z^{\alpha\wedge 1}\log(1/z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\mapsto z^{\alpha\wedge 1}\log(1/z)</annotation></semantics></math> is increasing on <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(0,e^{-1/(\alpha\wedge 1)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,e^{-1/(\alpha\wedge 1)}]</annotation></semantics></math>, so let <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta\coloneqq\frac{1}{\sqrt{pd}}\bigl(\frac{\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}}{3C_{3}\log(en)}\bigr)^{1/(\alpha\wedge 1)}\wedge\frac{1}{\sqrt{pd}}e^{-1/(\alpha\wedge 1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>∧</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\coloneqq\frac{1}{\sqrt{pd}}\bigl(\frac{\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}}{3C_{3}\log(en)}\bigr)^{1/(\alpha\wedge 1)}\wedge\frac{1}{\sqrt{pd}}e^{-1/(\alpha\wedge 1)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> large enough such that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx164" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{2}(\delta\sqrt{pd})^{\alpha\wedge 1}\biggl\{\log\biggl(\frac{1}{\delta\sqrt{pd}}\biggr)\vee 1\biggr\}\leq\frac{\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}}{3}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∧</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{2}(\delta\sqrt{pd})^{\alpha\wedge 1}\biggl\{\log\biggl(\frac{1}{\delta\sqrt{pd}}\biggr)\vee 1\biggr\}\leq\frac{\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}}{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta\coloneqq\{i\delta:i\in\mathbb{Z},|i\delta|\leq 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\coloneqq\{i\delta:i\in\mathbb{Z},|i\delta|\leq 1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{2}\coloneqq\Delta^{d\times p}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d\times p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{2}\coloneqq\Delta^{d\times p}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d\times p}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\subseteq B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{p},2C_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}^{(p)}\subseteq B_{\infty,\infty}^{\alpha}([0,1]^{p},2C_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in V_{p}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in V_{p}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\prime}\in\mathcal{N}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g^{\prime}-g\|_{\infty}\leq\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g^{\prime}-g\|_{\infty}\leq\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}/3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|U^{\prime}-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\sqrt{pd}\|U^{\prime}-U\|_{\infty}\leq\delta\sqrt{pd}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|U^{\prime}-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\sqrt{pd}\|U^{\prime}-U\|_{\infty}\leq\delta\sqrt{pd}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, for all <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{B}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{B}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|U^{\top}x-(U^{\prime})^{\top}x\|_{2}\leq\delta\sqrt{pd}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|U^{\top}x-(U^{\prime})^{\top}x\|_{2}\leq\delta\sqrt{pd}</annotation></semantics></math>, so by (<a href="#A6.E65" title="In Proof. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a>) and (<a href="#A6.E66" title="In Proof. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>), we deduce that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx165" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex160"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\biggl|g\biggl(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\biggl|g\biggl(</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex160.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{U^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)-g^{\prime}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\prime})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{U^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)-g^{\prime}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\prime})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex161"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\biggl|g\biggl(\frac{U^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)-g\biggl(\frac{(U^{\prime})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr|+\biggl|g\biggl(\frac{(U^{\prime})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)-g^{\prime}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\prime})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\biggl|g\biggl(\frac{U^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)-g\biggl(\frac{(U^{\prime})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr|+\biggl|g\biggl(\frac{(U^{\prime})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)-g^{\prime}\biggl(\frac{(U^{\prime})^{\top}x+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)\biggr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex162"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}}{3}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}}{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{1}\circ\mathcal{N}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{1}\circ\mathcal{N}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}/3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}/3)</annotation></semantics></math>-cover of <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\alpha,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\alpha,p}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m30" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx166" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E67.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(2\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}/3,\,\mathcal{G}_{\alpha,p},\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}\bigr)\leq\log|\mathcal{N}_{1}|+\log|\mathcal{N}_{2}|\leq C^{\prime}n\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.059em">,</mo><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>log</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>log</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>n</mi><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(2\sigma\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}/3,\,\mathcal{G}_{\alpha,p},\,\|\cdot\|_{\infty}\bigr)\leq\log|\mathcal{N}_{1}|+\log|\mathcal{N}_{2}|\leq C^{\prime}n\epsilon_{n,\alpha,p}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.6.1" class="ltx_text">which proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm6" title="Proposition 6. ‣ 4.2 In-context learning for multi-index models ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm6" title="Proposition 6. ‣ 4.2 In-context learning for multi-index models ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> follows the same arguments as the proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, but instead we apply Lemmas <a href="#Thmthm20" title="Lemma 20. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>, <a href="#Thmthm21" title="Lemma 21. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> and <a href="#Thmthm22" title="Lemma 22. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> to verify the assumptions of Corollary <a href="#Thmthm17" title="Corollary 17. ‣ E.2 Bayesian nonparametric regression ‣ Appendix E Posterior contraction and adaptation ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Proofs of Theorems <a href="#Thmthm5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and <a href="#Thmthm7" title="Theorem 7. ‣ 4.2 In-context learning for multi-index models ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any test distribution <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi_{\beta})\leq\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi_{\beta})\leq\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx167" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex163"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi)=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\biggl\{\biggl(\frac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}\pi}\biggr)^{2}\biggr\}-1\leq\max_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\frac{1}{\lambda_{\alpha}}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\beta}}\biggl\{\biggl(\frac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}\pi_{\beta}}\biggr)^{2}\biggr\}-1\leq(\kappa+1)\max_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\frac{1}{\lambda_{\alpha}}-1\eqqcolon\kappa^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≕</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi)=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}\biggl\{\biggl(\frac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}\pi}\biggr)^{2}\biggr\}-1\leq\max_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\frac{1}{\lambda_{\alpha}}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\beta}}\biggl\{\biggl(\frac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}\pi_{\beta}}\biggr)^{2}\biggr\}-1\leq(\kappa+1)\max_{\alpha\in\mathcal{A}}\frac{1}{\lambda_{\alpha}}-1\eqqcolon\kappa^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now, by Proposition <a href="#Thmthm1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 2 Problem set-up and ICL excess risk decomposition ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, then by taking <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{model}}^{\circ}\geq d+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{model}}^{\circ}\geq d+2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{\circ}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>ffn</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{ffn}}^{\circ}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> large enough that Proposition <a href="#Thmthm3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 3.2 Universal approximation and learnability ‣ 3 Transformers, universal approximation and learnability ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> holds with <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1/\{16R^{2}n^{2}(\kappa^{\prime}+1)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1/\{16R^{2}n^{2}(\kappa^{\prime}+1)\}</annotation></semantics></math> and applying Proposition <a href="#Thmthm4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx168" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex164"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mu}^{\mathrm{ICL}}(\widetilde{f}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>ICL</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\mu}^{\mathrm{ICL}}(\widetilde{f}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex164.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 4R\sqrt{\bigl\{\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi)+1\bigr\}\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})}+2\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g^{\circ}(X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 4R\sqrt{\bigl\{\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi)+1\bigr\}\mathcal{E}(\widetilde{f}_{T})}+2\mathbb{E}_{\mu}\mathbb{E}_{P}\bigl[\bigl\{g_{\pi}(X,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g^{\circ}(X)\bigr\}^{2}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex165"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{n}+C^{\prime}n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}\leq Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{n}+C^{\prime}n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}\leq Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime},C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime},C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> depend on neither <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> nor <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm7" title="Theorem 7. ‣ 4.2 In-context learning for multi-index models ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">As in the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, for any test distribution <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\beta,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\beta,r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi_{\beta,r})\leq\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi_{\beta,r})\leq\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi)\leq(\kappa+1)\max_{(\alpha,p)\in\mathcal{A}^{\prime}}\lambda_{\alpha,p}^{-1}-1\eqqcolon\kappa^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≕</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}(\mu,\pi)\leq(\kappa+1)\max_{(\alpha,p)\in\mathcal{A}^{\prime}}\lambda_{\alpha,p}^{-1}-1\eqqcolon\kappa^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The result therefore follows by the same argument as in the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, except that we apply Proposition <a href="#Thmthm6" title="Proposition 6. ‣ 4.2 In-context learning for multi-index models ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> in place of Proposition <a href="#Thmthm4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ 4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> to obtain the improved bound <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mu}^{\mathrm{ICL}}(\widetilde{f}_{T})\leq Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>ICL</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mu}^{\mathrm{ICL}}(\widetilde{f}_{T})\leq Cn^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}</annotation></semantics></math> for sufficiently large <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> depends on neither <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> nor <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm8" title="Theorem 8. ‣ 4.3 Lower bounds on the ICL excess risk ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a></h3>

<div id="A6.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm8" title="Theorem 8. ‣ 4.3 Lower bounds on the ICL excess risk ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use the Bayes risk lower bound techniques developed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen, Guntuboyina and Zhang (2016)</a></cite>. Let <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{P}_{*},\mathcal{G}_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{P}_{*},\mathcal{G}_{*})</annotation></semantics></math> be either <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{P}_{\beta},\mathcal{G}_{\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{P}_{\beta},\mathcal{G}_{\beta})</annotation></semantics></math> defined as in Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 In-context learning for Besov functions ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> or <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{P}_{\beta,r},\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{P}_{\beta,r},\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r})</annotation></semantics></math> defined as in Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 In-context learning for multi-index models ‣ 4 Adaptivity and robustness of ICL ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, and let <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distribution on <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is the distribution of the random function <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X=x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto\mathbb{E}_{P}(Y\,|\,X=x)</annotation></semantics></math>, where the randomness comes from <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen, Guntuboyina and Zhang (2016, Corollary 12(i) and Eq. (48))</a></cite>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx169" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex166"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\inf_{\widehat{g}_{n}\in\widehat{\mathcal{G}}_{n}}\mathcal{R}_{\mu}^{\mathrm{ICL}}(\widehat{g}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>ICL</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\inf_{\widehat{g}_{n}\in\widehat{\mathcal{G}}_{n}}\mathcal{R}_{\mu}^{\mathrm{ICL}}(\widehat{g}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex166.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\inf_{\widehat{g}_{n}\in\widehat{\mathcal{G}}_{n}}\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\mu}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{n}|P\sim P^{\otimes n}}\bigl\{\|\widehat{g}_{n}(\cdot,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{P}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\inf_{\widehat{g}_{n}\in\widehat{\mathcal{G}}_{n}}\mathbb{E}_{P\sim\mu}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{n}|P\sim P^{\otimes n}}\bigl\{\|\widehat{g}_{n}(\cdot,\mathcal{D}_{n})-g_{P}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex167"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\inf_{\widehat{g}_{n}\in\widehat{\mathcal{G}}_{n}}\mathbb{E}_{\widetilde{g}\sim\widetilde{\mu}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{n}|\widetilde{g}\sim P_{\widetilde{g}}^{\otimes n}}\bigl\{\|\widehat{g}_{n}(\cdot,\mathcal{D}_{n})-\widetilde{g}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\inf_{\widehat{g}_{n}\in\widehat{\mathcal{G}}_{n}}\mathbb{E}_{\widetilde{g}\sim\widetilde{\mu}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{n}|\widetilde{g}\sim P_{\widetilde{g}}^{\otimes n}}\bigl\{\|\widehat{g}_{n}(\cdot,\mathcal{D}_{n})-\widetilde{g}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{2}\sup\biggl\{t&gt;0:\sup_{g^{\circ}\in\mathcal{G}_{*}}\widetilde{\mu}\Bigl(\bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{*}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}&lt;t\bigr\}\Bigr)&lt;\frac{1}{4}e^{-2I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}}\biggr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.111em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>KL</mi><mi>up</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{2}\sup\biggl\{t&gt;0:\sup_{g^{\circ}\in\mathcal{G}_{*}}\widetilde{\mu}\Bigl(\bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{*}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}&lt;t\bigr\}\Bigr)&lt;\frac{1}{4}e^{-2I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}}\biggr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx170" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex168"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}\coloneqq\inf_{\eta&gt;0}\bigl\{\log\mathcal{N}(\eta^{2}/n,\mathcal{P}_{*},\mathrm{KL})+\eta^{2}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>KL</mi><mi>up</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}\coloneqq\inf_{\eta&gt;0}\bigl\{\log\mathcal{N}(\eta^{2}/n,\mathcal{P}_{*},\mathrm{KL})+\eta^{2}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">and we recall that <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\eta^{2}/n,\mathcal{P}_{*},\mathrm{KL})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\eta^{2}/n,\mathcal{P}_{*},\mathrm{KL})</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\eta^{2}/n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\eta^{2}/n)</annotation></semantics></math>-covering number of <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the Kullback–Leibler divergence. By Lemma <a href="#Thmthm24" title="Lemma 24. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a><em id="A6.SS4.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(a)</em>, we deduce that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx171" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex169"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}\leq\inf_{\eta&gt;0}\bigl\{\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\sigma\eta\sqrt{2/n},\mathcal{G}_{*},\|\cdot\|_{\infty}\bigr)+\eta^{2}\bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>KL</mi><mi>up</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>log</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}\leq\inf_{\eta&gt;0}\bigl\{\log\mathcal{N}\bigl(\sigma\eta\sqrt{2/n},\mathcal{G}_{*},\|\cdot\|_{\infty}\bigr)+\eta^{2}\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">From now on, <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> will denote positive quantities that do not depend on <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A6.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(a)</em><span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text"> By choosing <math id="A6.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\coloneqq n^{d/(2\beta+d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≔</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\coloneqq n^{d/(2\beta+d)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Giné and Nickl (2021, Eq. (4.184))</a></cite>, we deduce that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx172" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex170"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}\leq C_{1}n^{d/(2\beta+d)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>KL</mi><mi>up</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}\leq C_{1}n^{d/(2\beta+d)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the measurable bijection between <math id="A6.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> and our assumption on <math id="A6.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A6.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}}\frac{\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\mu}}{\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta}}(g)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}}\frac{\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\mu}}{\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta}}(g)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, by Lemma <a href="#Thmthm19" title="Lemma 19. ‣ F.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>, there exists <math id="A6.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> small enough that for all <math id="A6.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\circ}\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\circ}\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx173" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex171"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\mu}\Bigl(\bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\mu}\Bigl(\bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex171.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}&lt;C_{2}n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}\bigr\}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}&lt;C_{2}n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}\bigr\}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex172"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\biggl\{\sup_{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}}\frac{\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\mu}}{\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta}}(g)\biggr\}\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta}\Bigl(\bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}&lt;C_{2}n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}\bigr\}\Bigr)&lt;\frac{1}{4}e^{-2I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>KL</mi><mi>up</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\biggl\{\sup_{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}}\frac{\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\mu}}{\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta}}(g)\biggr\}\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta}\Bigl(\bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}&lt;C_{2}n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+d)}\bigr\}\Bigr)&lt;\frac{1}{4}e^{-2I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The claim then follows from (<a href="#A6.E68" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ F.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A6.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(b)</em><span id="A6.SS4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text"> By choosing <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\coloneqq n^{d/(2\beta+r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≔</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\coloneqq n^{d/(2\beta+r)}</annotation></semantics></math> and applying (<a href="#A6.E67" title="In Proof. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">67</span></a>) with <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,r)</annotation></semantics></math> replacing <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,p)</annotation></semantics></math>, we deduce that</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx174" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex173"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}\leq C_{3}n^{r/(2\beta+r)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>KL</mi><mi>up</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}\leq C_{3}n^{r/(2\beta+r)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, by Lemma <a href="#Thmthm21" title="Lemma 21. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>, there exists <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{4}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{4}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> small enough that for all <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\circ}\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\circ}\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx175" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex174"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\mu}\Bigl(\bigl\{g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\mu}\Bigl(\bigl\{g</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex174.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}&lt;C_{4}n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}\bigr\}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}&lt;C_{4}n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}\bigr\}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex175"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\biggl\{\sup_{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r}}\frac{\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\mu}}{\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta,r}}(g)\biggr\}\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta,r}\Bigl(\bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}&lt;C_{4}n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}\bigr\}\Bigr)&lt;\frac{1}{4}e^{-2I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>KL</mi><mi>up</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\biggl\{\sup_{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r}}\frac{\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\mu}}{\mathrm{d}\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta,r}}(g)\biggr\}\widetilde{\pi}_{\beta,r}\Bigl(\bigl\{g\in\mathcal{G}_{\beta,r}:\|g-g^{\circ}\|_{L^{2}(P_{X})}^{2}&lt;C_{4}n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+r)}\bigr\}\Bigr)&lt;\frac{1}{4}e^{-2I^{\mathrm{up}}_{\mathrm{KL}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">The claim then follows again from (<a href="#A6.E68" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ F.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Auxiliary lemmas</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The lemma below is a modification of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ghosal, Lember and van der Vaart (2008, Lemma 6.3)</a></cite>, where we assume that the log-likelihood ratio is sub-Gamma in the left tail with uniform sub-Gamma parameters in order to obtain an exponential concentration.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm23" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 23</span></span><span id="Thmthm23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm23.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm23.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm23.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> be a measurable space of distributions on a measurable space <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a distribution on <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n}\overset{\mathrm{iid}}{\sim}P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">iid</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n}\overset{\mathrm{iid}}{\sim}P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx176" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex176"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle B(P_{0},\epsilon)\coloneqq\Bigl\{P\in\mathcal{P}:\mathrm{KL}(P_{0},P)\leq\epsilon^{2},\,\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{0},P)\leq\epsilon^{2}\Bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B(P_{0},\epsilon)\coloneqq\Bigl\{P\in\mathcal{P}:\mathrm{KL}(P_{0},P)\leq\epsilon^{2},\,\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{0},P)\leq\epsilon^{2}\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm23.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm23.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\ll P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>≪</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\ll P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, let</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex177" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(P,Z_{i})\coloneqq\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})-\mathbb{E}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(P,Z_{i})\coloneqq\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})-\mathbb{E}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm23.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm23.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that there exist <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in B(P_{0},\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in B(P_{0},\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(P,Z_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(P,Z_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gamma in the left tail with variance parameter <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and scale parameter <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for any probability measure <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon,D&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon,D&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have with <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}^{\otimes n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}^{\otimes n}</annotation></semantics></math>-probability at most <math id="Thmthm23.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\bigl(-\frac{D^{2}n\epsilon^{2}}{2(a+cD)}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\bigl(-\frac{D^{2}n\epsilon^{2}}{2(a+cD)}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx177" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{B(P_{0},\epsilon)}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)&lt;\Pi\bigl(B(P_{0},\epsilon)\bigr)e^{-(1+D)n\epsilon^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{B(P_{0},\epsilon)}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)&lt;\Pi\bigl(B(P_{0},\epsilon)\bigr)e^{-(1+D)n\epsilon^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Writing <math id="A7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\coloneqq B(P_{0},\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\coloneqq B(P_{0},\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, we observe that the conclusion is clear if <math id="A7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi(B)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi(B)=0</annotation></semantics></math> because the right-hand side of (<a href="#A7.E69" title="In Lemma 23. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>) is zero. Moreover, by replacing <math id="A7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> with its conditional distribution on <math id="A7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> if necessary, we may assume without loss of generality that <math id="A7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi(B)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi(B)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, by Jensen’s inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx178" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex178"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\log\int_{B}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\log\int_{B}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex178.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\int_{B}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\int_{B}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex179"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\int_{B}W(P,Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)-\int_{B}\mathrm{KL}(P_{0},P)\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\int_{B}W(P,Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)-\int_{B}\mathrm{KL}(P_{0},P)\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\int_{B}W(P,Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)-\epsilon^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\int_{B}W(P,Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)-\epsilon^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the final inequality follows from the definition of <math id="A7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, for <math id="A7.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda\in(-1/c,0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in(-1/c,0]</annotation></semantics></math>, by Jensen’s inequality and Fubini’s theorem,</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx179" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex180"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{Z_{1}}\exp\biggl\{\lambda\int_{B}W(P,Z_{1})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)\biggr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{Z_{1}}\exp\biggl\{\lambda\int_{B}W(P,Z_{1})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)\biggr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex180.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{Z_{1}}\biggl[\int_{B}\exp\bigl\{\lambda W(P,Z_{1})\bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{Z_{1}}\biggl[\int_{B}\exp\bigl\{\lambda W(P,Z_{1})\bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex181"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}_{Z_{1}}\exp\bigl\{\lambda W(P,Z_{1})\bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)\leq\exp\biggl(\frac{a\epsilon^{2}\lambda^{2}}{2(1-c\lambda)}\biggr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{B}\mathbb{E}_{Z_{1}}\exp\bigl\{\lambda W(P,Z_{1})\bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)\leq\exp\biggl(\frac{a\epsilon^{2}\lambda^{2}}{2(1-c\lambda)}\biggr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the final inequality follows from the sub-Gamma assumption on <math id="A7.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(P,Z_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(P,Z_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. This shows that <math id="A7.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{B}W(P,Z_{1})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{B}W(P,Z_{1})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gamma in the left tail with variance parameter <math id="A7.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and scale parameter <math id="A7.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A7.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\int_{B}W(P,Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\int_{B}W(P,Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)</annotation></semantics></math> is also sub-Gamma in the left tail with variance parameter <math id="A7.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\epsilon^{2}/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\epsilon^{2}/n</annotation></semantics></math> and scale parameter <math id="A7.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c/n</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(e.g. <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Samworth and Shah, 2025+</a>, Exercise 10.6.12)</cite>. Hence, by (<a href="#A7.E70" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx180" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex182"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\biggl(\frac{1}{n}\log\int_{B}\prod_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\biggl(\frac{1}{n}\log\int_{B}\prod_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex182.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)&lt;-(1+D)\epsilon^{2}\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}P_{0}}(Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)&lt;-(1+D)\epsilon^{2}\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex183"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}\biggl(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\int_{B}W(P,Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)&lt;-D\epsilon^{2}\biggr)\leq\exp\biggl(-\frac{D^{2}n\epsilon^{2}}{2(a+cD)}\biggr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}\biggl(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\int_{B}W(P,Z_{i})\,\mathrm{d}\Pi(P)&lt;-D\epsilon^{2}\biggr)\leq\exp\biggl(-\frac{D^{2}n\epsilon^{2}}{2(a+cD)}\biggr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the final inequality follows from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Samworth and Shah (2025+, Proposition 10.6.8(a))</a></cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We next derive some properties about the distributions of nonparametric regression models with Gaussian noise.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm24" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 24</span></span><span id="Thmthm24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm24.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm24.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm24.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Borel distribution on <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\sim N(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\sim N(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> be independent of <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, let <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1},g_{2}:\mathcal{X}\to[-R,R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1},g_{2}:\mathcal{X}\to[-R,R]</annotation></semantics></math> be Borel measurable, let <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{1}=g_{1}(X)+\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{1}=g_{1}(X)+\xi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{2}=g_{2}(X)+\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{2}=g_{2}(X)+\xi</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, let <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distributions of <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm24.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Then</span></p>
<ul id="A7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A7.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(P_{1},P_{2})=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(P_{1},P_{2})=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{1},P_{2})=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\mathrm{Var}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}+2\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{1},P_{2})=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\mathrm{Var}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}+2\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A7.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(P_{1},P_{2})\leq\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(P_{1},P_{2})\leq\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A7.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{1},P_{2})\leq\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{1},P_{2})\leq\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A7.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\coloneqq\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{2}}{\mathrm{d}P_{1}}(X,Y_{1})-\mathbb{E}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{2}}{\mathrm{d}P_{1}}(X,Y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\coloneqq\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{2}}{\mathrm{d}P_{1}}(X,Y_{1})-\mathbb{E}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{2}}{\mathrm{d}P_{1}}(X,Y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.ix3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is sub-Gamma in both tails with variance parameter </span><math id="A7.I1.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(8\vee\frac{2}{\sigma^{2}}\bigr)\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>∨</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(8\vee\frac{2}{\sigma^{2}}\bigr)\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.ix3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and scale parameter </span><math id="A7.I1.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\coloneqq\frac{2R}{\sigma}\vee\frac{4R^{2}}{3\sigma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo>∨</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\coloneqq\frac{2R}{\sigma}\vee\frac{4R^{2}}{3\sigma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.ix3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(d)</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-e^{-R^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}}{2R^{2}}\cdot\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}\leq d_{\mathrm{H}}^{2}(P_{1},P_{2})\leq\frac{1}{4\sigma^{2}}\cdot\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-e^{-R^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}}{2R^{2}}\cdot\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}\leq d_{\mathrm{H}}^{2}(P_{1},P_{2})\leq\frac{1}{4\sigma^{2}}\cdot\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(a)</em><span id="A7.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Let <math id="A7.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{Y_{1}|X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{Y_{1}|X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{Y_{2}|X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{Y_{2}|X}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the conditional distributions of <math id="A7.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A7.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A7.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Then, using the fact that <math id="A7.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{1}=g_{1}(X)+\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{1}=g_{1}(X)+\xi</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx181" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex184"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{2}}{\mathrm{d}P_{1}}(X,Y_{1})=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{Y_{2}|X}}{\mathrm{d}P_{Y_{1}|X}}(X,Y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{2}}{\mathrm{d}P_{1}}(X,Y_{1})=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{Y_{2}|X}}{\mathrm{d}P_{Y_{1}|X}}(X,Y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex184.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{\bigl(Y_{1}-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}+\frac{\bigl(Y_{1}-g_{1}(X)\bigr)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{\bigl(Y_{1}-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}+\frac{\bigl(Y_{1}-g_{1}(X)\bigr)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{-\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}-2\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)\xi}{2\sigma^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{-\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}-2\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)\xi}{2\sigma^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx182" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(P_{1},P_{2})=-\mathbb{E}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{2}}{\mathrm{d}P_{1}}(X,Y_{1})=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(P_{1},P_{2})=-\mathbb{E}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{2}}{\mathrm{d}P_{1}}(X,Y_{1})=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(b)</em><span id="A7.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text"> By (<a href="#A7.E71" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>) and (<a href="#A7.E72" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx183" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex185"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{1},P_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{1},P_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex185.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\Bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}+2\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)\xi-\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}\Bigr\}^{2}\Bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\Bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}+2\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)\xi-\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}\Bigr\}^{2}\Bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex186"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\mathrm{Var}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}+2\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2\sigma^{2}}\mathrm{Var}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}+2\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where in the final equality, we used the fact that <math id="A7.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\perp\!\!\!\perp X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mpadded style="width:0.518em;" width="0.518em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\perp\!\!\!\perp X</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(\xi)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(\xi)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(\xi^{2})=\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(\xi^{2})=\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(c)</em><span id="A7.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text"> From (<a href="#A7.E71" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>) and (<a href="#A7.E72" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix G Auxiliary lemmas ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>), we deduce that</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx184" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex187"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex187.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{2}}{\mathrm{d}P_{1}}(X,Y_{1})-\mathbb{E}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{2}}{\mathrm{d}P_{1}}(X,Y_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{2}}{\mathrm{d}P_{1}}(X,Y_{1})-\mathbb{E}\log\frac{\mathrm{d}P_{2}}{\mathrm{d}P_{1}}(X,Y_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex188"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\bigl(g_{2}(X)-g_{1}(X)\bigr)\xi}{\sigma^{2}}-\frac{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}-\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}}{2\sigma^{2}}\eqqcolon W_{1}+W_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≕</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\bigl(g_{2}(X)-g_{1}(X)\bigr)\xi}{\sigma^{2}}-\frac{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}-\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}}{2\sigma^{2}}\eqqcolon W_{1}+W_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A7.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,\sigma/R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,\sigma/R)</annotation></semantics></math>, using the fact that <math id="A7.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1+x)\leq x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1+x)\leq x</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and Fubini’s theorem,</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx185" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex189"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\mathbb{E}e^{\lambda W_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\mathbb{E}e^{\lambda W_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex189.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\mathbb{E}\exp\biggl(\frac{\lambda\bigl(g_{2}(X)-g_{1}(X)\bigr)\xi}{\sigma^{2}}\biggr)=\log\mathbb{E}\exp\biggl(\frac{\lambda^{2}\bigl(g_{2}(X)-g_{1}(X)\bigr)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\mathbb{E}\exp\biggl(\frac{\lambda\bigl(g_{2}(X)-g_{1}(X)\bigr)\xi}{\sigma^{2}}\biggr)=\log\mathbb{E}\exp\biggl(\frac{\lambda^{2}\bigl(g_{2}(X)-g_{1}(X)\bigr)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex190"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{r=1}^{\infty}\frac{\lambda^{2r}\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{2}(X)-g_{1}(X)\bigr)^{2r}\bigr\}}{(2\sigma^{2})^{r}\cdot r!}\leq\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{2}(X)-g_{1}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}\sum_{r=1}^{\infty}\frac{\lambda^{2r}(2R)^{2r-2}}{(2\sigma^{2})^{r}\cdot r!}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{r=1}^{\infty}\frac{\lambda^{2r}\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{2}(X)-g_{1}(X)\bigr)^{2r}\bigr\}}{(2\sigma^{2})^{r}\cdot r!}\leq\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{2}(X)-g_{1}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}\sum_{r=1}^{\infty}\frac{\lambda^{2r}(2R)^{2r-2}}{(2\sigma^{2})^{r}\cdot r!}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex191"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\lambda^{2}\epsilon^{2}\sum_{r=1}^{\infty}\frac{2^{r-1}}{r!}\biggl(\frac{\lambda R}{\sigma}\biggr)^{2r-2}\leq\lambda^{2}\epsilon^{2}\sum_{r=1}^{\infty}\biggl(\frac{\lambda R}{\sigma}\biggr)^{r-1}=\frac{2\lambda^{2}\epsilon^{2}}{2\bigl(1-\frac{\lambda R}{\sigma}\bigr)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\lambda^{2}\epsilon^{2}\sum_{r=1}^{\infty}\frac{2^{r-1}}{r!}\biggl(\frac{\lambda R}{\sigma}\biggr)^{2r-2}\leq\lambda^{2}\epsilon^{2}\sum_{r=1}^{\infty}\biggl(\frac{\lambda R}{\sigma}\biggr)^{r-1}=\frac{2\lambda^{2}\epsilon^{2}}{2\bigl(1-\frac{\lambda R}{\sigma}\bigr)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">The same holds true if <math id="A7.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is replaced by <math id="A7.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="A7.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gamma in both tails with variance parameter <math id="A7.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and scale parameter <math id="A7.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R/\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R/\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. By part <em id="A7.p6.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(b)</em> and the assumption that <math id="A7.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{1},P_{2})\leq\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{V}_{2}(P_{1},P_{2})\leq\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A7.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(W_{2}^{2})\leq\epsilon^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(W_{2}^{2})\leq\epsilon^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, since <math id="A7.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by <math id="A7.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2R^{2}/\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2R^{2}/\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have for <math id="A7.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex192" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(|W_{2}|^{r})\leq\mathbb{E}(W_{2}^{2})\cdot\Bigl(\frac{2R^{2}}{\sigma^{2}}\Bigr)^{r-2}\leq\frac{r!\epsilon^{2}}{2\cdot 2\sigma^{2}}\Bigl(\frac{2R^{2}}{3\sigma^{2}}\Bigr)^{r-2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(|W_{2}|^{r})\leq\mathbb{E}(W_{2}^{2})\cdot\Bigl(\frac{2R^{2}}{\sigma^{2}}\Bigr)^{r-2}\leq\frac{r!\epsilon^{2}}{2\cdot 2\sigma^{2}}\Bigl(\frac{2R^{2}}{3\sigma^{2}}\Bigr)^{r-2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">The same bound holds for <math id="A7.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, so by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Samworth and Shah (2025+, Proposition 10.6.8(b))</a></cite>, <math id="A7.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gamma in both tails with variance parameter <math id="A7.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\epsilon^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\epsilon^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and scale parameter <math id="A7.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2R^{2}}{3\sigma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2R^{2}}{3\sigma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Samworth and Shah (2025+, Exercise 10.6.12)</a></cite>, we have that <math id="A7.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=W_{1}+W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=W_{1}+W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gamma in both tails with variance parameter <math id="A7.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(8\vee\frac{2}{\sigma^{2}}\bigr)\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>∨</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(8\vee\frac{2}{\sigma^{2}}\bigr)\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and scale parameter <math id="A7.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\frac{2R}{\sigma}\vee\frac{4R^{2}}{3\sigma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo>∨</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\frac{2R}{\sigma}\vee\frac{4R^{2}}{3\sigma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(d)</em><span id="A7.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text"> We have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx186" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex193"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{H}}^{2}(P_{1},P_{2})=\mathbb{E}\,d_{\mathrm{H}}^{2}(P_{Y_{1}|X},P_{Y_{2}|X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{H}}^{2}(P_{1},P_{2})=\mathbb{E}\,d_{\mathrm{H}}^{2}(P_{Y_{1}|X},P_{Y_{2}|X})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex193.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\,\mathbb{E}\biggl\{1-\exp\biggl(-\frac{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}\biggr)\biggr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\,\mathbb{E}\biggl\{1-\exp\biggl(-\frac{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}\biggr)\biggr\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex194"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{1-e^{-R^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}}{2R^{2}}\cdot\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{1-e^{-R^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}}{2R^{2}}\cdot\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the inequality follows since <math id="A7.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto(1-e^{-x})/x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto(1-e^{-x})/x</annotation></semantics></math> is decreasing on <math id="A7.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> and moreover <math id="A7.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X))^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}\leq\frac{R^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X))^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}\leq\frac{R^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand, using the fact that <math id="A7.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-x}\leq x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-x}\leq x</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we also have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx187" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex195"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex195.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\mathbb{E}\biggl\{1-\exp\biggl(-\frac{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}\biggr)\biggr\}\leq\frac{1}{4\sigma^{2}}\cdot\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\mathbb{E}\biggl\{1-\exp\biggl(-\frac{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}}{8\sigma^{2}}\biggr)\biggr\}\leq\frac{1}{4\sigma^{2}}\cdot\mathbb{E}\bigl\{\bigl(g_{1}(X)-g_{2}(X)\bigr)^{2}\bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">as required.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm25" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm25.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 25</span></span><span id="Thmthm25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm25.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm25.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm25.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="Thmthm25.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L^{2}([0,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L^{2}([0,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> has wavelet decomposition</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx188" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex196"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f=\sum_{k\in K}a_{k}\Phi_{k}+\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}b_{\ell,\gamma}\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f=\sum_{k\in K}a_{k}\Phi_{k}+\sum_{\ell=\ell_{0}}^{\infty}\sum_{\gamma\in\Gamma_{\ell}}b_{\ell,\gamma}\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmthm25.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm25.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm25.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq c_{1}&lt;c_{2}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq c_{1}&lt;c_{2}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmthm25.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\coloneqq\bigl\{(\ell,\gamma):\mathrm{supp}(\Psi_{\ell,\gamma})\subseteq[c_{1},c_{2}]^{d}\bigr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\coloneqq\bigl\{(\ell,\gamma):\mathrm{supp}(\Psi_{\ell,\gamma})\subseteq[c_{1},c_{2}]^{d}\bigr\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx189" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex197"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f\|_{L^{2}([c_{1},c_{2}]^{d})}^{2}\geq\sum_{(\ell,\gamma)\in\Lambda}b^{2}_{\ell,\gamma}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f\|_{L^{2}([c_{1},c_{2}]^{d})}^{2}\geq\sum_{(\ell,\gamma)\in\Lambda}b^{2}_{\ell,\gamma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="A7.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(\Psi_{\ell,\gamma})\subseteq[c_{1},c_{2}]^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(\Psi_{\ell,\gamma})\subseteq[c_{1},c_{2}]^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A7.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ell,\gamma)\in\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ell,\gamma)\in\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, so by the orthonormality of the wavelet basis, we have that <math id="A7.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Psi_{\ell,\gamma})_{(\ell,\gamma)\in\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Psi_{\ell,\gamma})_{(\ell,\gamma)\in\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> is also a sequence of orthonormal functions in the Hilbert space <math id="A7.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}([c_{1},c_{2}]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}([c_{1},c_{2}]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> equipped with the inner product</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx190" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex198"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle f_{1},f_{2}\rangle_{[c_{1},c_{2}]^{d}}\coloneqq\int_{[c_{1},c_{2}]^{d}}f_{1}(x)f_{2}(x)\,\mathrm{d}x." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle f_{1},f_{2}\rangle_{[c_{1},c_{2}]^{d}}\coloneqq\int_{[c_{1},c_{2}]^{d}}f_{1}(x)f_{2}(x)\,\mathrm{d}x.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, for <math id="A7.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ell,\gamma)\in\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ell,\gamma)\in\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx191" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex199"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex199.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle f,\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}\rangle_{[c_{1},c_{2}]^{d}}=\int_{[c_{1},c_{2}]^{d}}f(x)\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}(x)\,\mathrm{d}x=\int_{[0,1]^{d}}f(x)\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}(x)\,\mathrm{d}x=b_{\ell,\gamma}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle f,\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}\rangle_{[c_{1},c_{2}]^{d}}=\int_{[c_{1},c_{2}]^{d}}f(x)\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}(x)\,\mathrm{d}x=\int_{[0,1]^{d}}f(x)\Psi_{\ell,\gamma}(x)\,\mathrm{d}x=b_{\ell,\gamma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, an application of Bessel’s inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(e.g. <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rudin, 1987</a>, Theorem 4.17)</cite> yields the desired result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm26" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 26</span></span><span id="Thmthm26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm26.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm26.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm26.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm26.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math> be uniformly distributed on the Stiefel manifold <math id="Thmthm26.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmthm26.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in V_{r}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in V_{r}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> be deterministic. Then for any <math id="Thmthm26.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="Thmthm26.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, depending only on <math id="Thmthm26.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmthm26.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx192" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex200"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|U^{(r)}-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\epsilon\bigr)\geq c\biggl(\epsilon\wedge\frac{1}{2}\biggr)^{dr}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|U^{(r)}-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\epsilon\bigr)\geq c\biggl(\epsilon\wedge\frac{1}{2}\biggr)^{dr}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We may assume that <math id="A7.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chikuse (2003, Theorem 2.2.1(iii))</a></cite>, we may assume without loss of generality that <math id="A7.p9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U^{(r)}=Z(Z^{\top}Z)^{-1/2}\eqqcolon F(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≕</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(r)}=Z(Z^{\top}Z)^{-1/2}\eqqcolon F(Z)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A7.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A7.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times r</annotation></semantics></math> random matrix with independent <math id="A7.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> entries. Let <math id="A7.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> be such that <math id="A7.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\coloneqq\|\Delta\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 1/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\coloneqq\|\Delta\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 1/6</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx193" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex201"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A\coloneqq U^{\top}\Delta+\Delta^{\top}U+\Delta^{\top}\Delta\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A\coloneqq U^{\top}\Delta+\Delta^{\top}U+\Delta^{\top}\Delta\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="A7.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 3\delta\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 3\delta\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A7.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U+\Delta)^{\top}(U+\Delta)=I_{r}+A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U+\Delta)^{\top}(U+\Delta)=I_{r}+A</annotation></semantics></math> is positive definite. Thus</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx194" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex202"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|F(U+\Delta)-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|F(U+\Delta)-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex202.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\|(U+\Delta)(I_{r}+A)^{-1/2}-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|(U+\Delta)(I_{r}+A)^{-1/2}-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex203"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex203.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\|(I_{r}+A)^{-1/2}-I_{r}\|_{\mathrm{op}}+\|\Delta\|_{\mathrm{op}}\|(I_{r}+A)^{-1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\|(I_{r}+A)^{-1/2}-I_{r}\|_{\mathrm{op}}+\|\Delta\|_{\mathrm{op}}\|(I_{r}+A)^{-1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, we can write <math id="A7.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{r}+A=VDV^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{r}+A=VDV^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A7.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonal and <math id="A7.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> is diagonal with diagonal elements bounded between <math id="A7.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-3\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-3\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+3\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+3\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A7.p9.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|(I_{r}+A)^{-1/2}-I_{r}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 3\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(I_{r}+A)^{-1/2}-I_{r}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 3\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p9.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|(I_{r}+A)^{-1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(I_{r}+A)^{-1/2}\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx195" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex204"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex204.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|F(U+\Delta)-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 3\delta+2\delta=5\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|F(U+\Delta)-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 3\delta+2\delta=5\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, if <math id="A7.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Z-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\epsilon/5&lt;1/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Z-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\epsilon/5&lt;1/6</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A7.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|F(Z)-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|F(Z)-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx196" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex205"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex205.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|U^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|U^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex205.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\epsilon\bigr)=\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|F(Z)-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\epsilon\bigr)\geq\mathbb{P}\biggl(\|Z-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{5}\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\epsilon\bigr)=\mathbb{P}\bigl(\|F(Z)-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\epsilon\bigr)\geq\mathbb{P}\biggl(\|Z-U\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{5}\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex206"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex206.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}\biggl(\|Z-U\|_{\infty}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{5\sqrt{dr}}\biggr)\geq\biggl\{\mathbb{P}\biggl(|Z_{11}-1|\leq\frac{\epsilon}{5\sqrt{dr}}\biggr)\biggr\}^{dr}\geq\biggl(\frac{2\epsilon}{25\sqrt{dr}}\biggr)^{dr}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}\biggl(\|Z-U\|_{\infty}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{5\sqrt{dr}}\biggr)\geq\biggl\{\mathbb{P}\biggl(|Z_{11}-1|\leq\frac{\epsilon}{5\sqrt{dr}}\biggr)\biggr\}^{dr}\geq\biggl(\frac{2\epsilon}{25\sqrt{dr}}\biggr)^{dr},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the third inequality follows since <math id="A7.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|U\|_{\infty}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|U\|_{\infty}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> has independent <math id="A7.p9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> entries, and the final inequality follows since <math id="A7.p9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\epsilon}{5\sqrt{dr}}\leq\frac{1}{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\epsilon}{5\sqrt{dr}}\leq\frac{1}{10}</annotation></semantics></math> and the standard normal density is bounded below by <math id="A7.p9.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/5</annotation></semantics></math> on the interval <math id="A7.p9.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.9,1.1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.9,1.1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmthm27" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthm27.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 27</span></span><span id="Thmthm27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthm27.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthm27.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthm27.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthm27.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> be a distribution on <math id="Thmthm27.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies the assumptions of Lemma <a href="#Thmthm21" title="Lemma 21. ‣ F.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix F Proofs for Section ‣ Provable test-time adaptivity and distributional robustness of in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>. Let <math id="Thmthm27.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[d]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmthm27.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in V_{p}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in V_{p}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmthm27.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmthm27.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distribution of <math id="Thmthm27.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{U^{\top}X+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{U^{\top}X+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exist <math id="Thmthm27.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}^{\prime}\equiv c_{0}^{\prime}(c_{0},\tau,d,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}^{\prime}\equiv c_{0}^{\prime}(c_{0},\tau,d,p)</annotation></semantics></math> and a hypercube <math id="Thmthm27.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}\subseteq[0,1]^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}\subseteq[0,1]^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> of side length <math id="Thmthm27.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tau}{2\sqrt{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>p</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tau}{2\sqrt{p}}</annotation></semantics></math> with the property that <math id="Thmthm27.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(A_{0}^{\prime})\geq c_{0}^{\prime}\mathrm{Vol}_{p}(A_{0}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Vol</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(A_{0}^{\prime})\geq c_{0}^{\prime}\mathrm{Vol}_{p}(A_{0}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> for all measurable <math id="Thmthm27.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}^{\prime}\subseteq A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}^{\prime}\subseteq A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A7.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=d</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A7.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonal, so for all measurable <math id="A7.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}\subseteq A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}\subseteq A</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex207" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex207.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\biggl(\frac{U^{\top}A_{0}+\bm{1}_{d}}{2}\biggr)=\mathbb{P}(X\in A_{0})\geq c_{0}\mathrm{Vol}_{d}(A_{0})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Vol</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\biggl(\frac{U^{\top}A_{0}+\bm{1}_{d}}{2}\biggr)=\mathbb{P}(X\in A_{0})\geq c_{0}\mathrm{Vol}_{d}(A_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, <math id="A7.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U^{\top}A+\bm{1}_{d})/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U^{\top}A+\bm{1}_{d})/2</annotation></semantics></math> is a Euclidean ball of radius <math id="A7.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau/2</annotation></semantics></math>, so it contains a hypercube of side length <math id="A7.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tau}{2\sqrt{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>p</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tau}{2\sqrt{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now suppose that <math id="A7.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[d-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[d-1]</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A7.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=(v_{1},\ldots,v_{d})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=(v_{1},\ldots,v_{d})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j_{1}\leq j_{2}\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j_{1}\leq j_{2}\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="A7.p10.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v_{j_{1}:j_{2}}\coloneqq(v_{j_{1}},\ldots,v_{j_{2}})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{j_{1}-j_{2}+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{j_{1}:j_{2}}\coloneqq(v_{j_{1}},\ldots,v_{j_{2}})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{j_{1}-j_{2}+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A7.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the centre of <math id="A7.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A7.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq A</annotation></semantics></math> be the Euclidean ball of radius <math id="A7.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau/2</annotation></semantics></math> and centred at <math id="A7.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math>. We may write <math id="A7.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=VP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=VP</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A7.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonal and <math id="A7.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times p}</annotation></semantics></math> is the first <math id="A7.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> columns of <math id="A7.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math> be Borel measurable, and define <math id="A7.p10.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T\coloneqq\{x\in V^{\top}A:x_{1:p}\in P^{\top}V^{\top}S\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\coloneqq\{x\in V^{\top}A:x_{1:p}\in P^{\top}V^{\top}S\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A7.p10.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="VT\subseteq A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">VT\subseteq A</annotation></semantics></math>; moreover, if <math id="A7.p10.m24" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y=(V^{\top}x)_{1:p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=(V^{\top}x)_{1:p}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A7.p10.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in S\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in S\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p10.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{R}^{d-p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{R}^{d-p}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A7.p10.m27" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|z-(V^{\top}o)_{(p+1):d}\|_{2}\leq\tau/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|z-(V^{\top}o)_{(p+1):d}\|_{2}\leq\tau/2</annotation></semantics></math>, then by the choice of <math id="A7.p10.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx197" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex208"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex208.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\biggl\|\begin{pmatrix}y\\
z\end{pmatrix}-V^{\top}o\biggr\|_{2}^{2}=\|y-(V^{\top}o)_{1:p}\|_{2}^{2}+\|z-(V^{\top}o)_{(p+1):d}\|_{2}^{2}\leq(\tau/2)^{2}+(\tau/2)^{2}&lt;\tau^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>z</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>o</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\biggl\|\begin{pmatrix}y\\
z\end{pmatrix}-V^{\top}o\biggr\|_{2}^{2}=\|y-(V^{\top}o)_{1:p}\|_{2}^{2}+\|z-(V^{\top}o)_{(p+1):d}\|_{2}^{2}\leq(\tau/2)^{2}+(\tau/2)^{2}&lt;\tau^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="A7.p10.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y^{\top},z^{\top})^{\top}\in T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y^{\top},z^{\top})^{\top}\in T</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx198" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle T^{\prime}\coloneqq\bigl\{(y^{\top},z^{\top})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{p+(d-p)}:y\in P^{\top}V^{\top}S,\,\|z-(V^{\top}o)_{(p+1):d}\|_{2}\leq\tau/2\bigr\}\subseteq T." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.059em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T^{\prime}\coloneqq\bigl\{(y^{\top},z^{\top})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{p+(d-p)}:y\in P^{\top}V^{\top}S,\,\|z-(V^{\top}o)_{(p+1):d}\|_{2}\leq\tau/2\bigr\}\subseteq T.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, writing <math id="A7.p10.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(\tau,d,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(\tau,d,p)</annotation></semantics></math> for the Lebesgue measure of a Euclidean ball in <math id="A7.p10.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d-p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d-p}</annotation></semantics></math> of radius <math id="A7.p10.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau/2</annotation></semantics></math>, we deduce that</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx199" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex209"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex209.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q\biggl(\frac{U^{\top}S+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q\biggl(\frac{U^{\top}S+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex209.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\biggl(\frac{P^{\top}V^{\top}X+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\in\frac{P^{\top}V^{\top}S+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>∈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\biggl(\frac{P^{\top}V^{\top}X+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\in\frac{P^{\top}V^{\top}S+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex210"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex210.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}(V^{\top}X\in T)=\mathbb{P}(X\in VT)\geq c_{0}\mathrm{Vol}_{d}(VT)=c_{0}\mathrm{Vol}_{d}(T)\geq c_{0}\mathrm{Vol}_{d}(T^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Vol</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Vol</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Vol</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}(V^{\top}X\in T)=\mathbb{P}(X\in VT)\geq c_{0}\mathrm{Vol}_{d}(VT)=c_{0}\mathrm{Vol}_{d}(T)\geq c_{0}\mathrm{Vol}_{d}(T^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex211"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex211.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=c_{0}\int_{y\in P^{\top}V^{\top}S}\int_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{d-p}:\|z-(V^{\top}o)_{(p+1):d}\|_{2}\leq\tau/2}\,\mathrm{d}z\,\mathrm{d}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c_{0}\int_{y\in P^{\top}V^{\top}S}\int_{z\in\mathbb{R}^{d-p}:\|z-(V^{\top}o)_{(p+1):d}\|_{2}\leq\tau/2}\,\mathrm{d}z\,\mathrm{d}y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.Ex212"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex212.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c_{0}v(\tau,d,p)\mathrm{Vol}_{p}(P^{\top}V^{\top}S)\eqqcolon c_{0}^{\prime}\mathrm{Vol}_{p}\biggl(\frac{U^{\top}S+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Vol</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Vol</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c_{0}v(\tau,d,p)\mathrm{Vol}_{p}(P^{\top}V^{\top}S)\eqqcolon c_{0}^{\prime}\mathrm{Vol}_{p}\biggl(\frac{U^{\top}S+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}\biggr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p10.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p10.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since this holds for all measurable <math id="A7.p10.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq K</annotation></semantics></math>, we deduce that <math id="A7.p10.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(A_{0}^{\prime})\geq c_{0}^{\prime}\mathrm{Vol}_{p}(A_{0}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Vol</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(A_{0}^{\prime})\geq c_{0}^{\prime}\mathrm{Vol}_{p}(A_{0}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A7.p10.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}^{\prime}\subseteq\frac{U^{\top}K+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}^{\prime}\subseteq\frac{U^{\top}K+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now <math id="A7.p10.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{U^{\top}K+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{U^{\top}K+\bm{1}_{p}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a ball of radius <math id="A7.p10.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau/4</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A7.p10.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, so it contains a hypercube <math id="A7.p10.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of side length <math id="A7.p10.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tau}{2\sqrt{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>p</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tau}{2\sqrt{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
